L["Credits Feedback"] = "Feedback"
L["Release Notes Version"] = "Version %s"
L["Release Notes 2.1.1"] = "|cff521902Stories|r\n• Quests that need a chain first now show that chain, in order, so you know what to do before you set out: Zul'Farrak's The Spider God and Nekrum's Medallion, and dungeon and raid quests in The Defias Brotherhood, Secrets of Uldaman, The Hakkari Trail, The Scarlet Crusade, The Key to Scholomance, The Princess of Ironforge, The Drakefire Amulet, and The Brazier of Invocation\n• Seven stories now follow their chains to the end, among them Secrets of Uldaman, The Hakkari Trail, The Scarlet Crusade, Linken's Adventure, and the warrior and shaman class stories\n• An optional quest the game only offers after another one waits for it, and its card says which quest to complete first\n• Secrets of Uldaman has five chapters: the Badlands' odd jobs and Theldurin's chain have their own\n• A chapter of optional quests only joins the Journal once you've done one of them, and its entry grows with the rest\n\n|cff521902WoW Forever|r\n• Quest cards name their dungeon or raid, such as Uldaman or Onyxia's Lair, instead of only saying Dungeon or Raid, and so do their tooltips. Onyxia's attunement quests say Attunement\n• The Brazier of Invocation ends on Legacy's card for its questline challenge, with its points and the day you earned it. Click it to open the challenge in the Legacy window\n• One more story is secret. It stays out of the list until you find a way in\n• Twilight in the Riverglades no longer says Krol'dok's key gets you in, and tells you what it opens\n• The header and quest cards no longer show Legacy's points shield and step numbers\n• The Mad King's quests show as dungeon quests, not raid quests\n\n|cff521902Fixes|r\n• The Cenarion Path: the Aquatic Form chapter waits for your own faction's A Lesson to Learn, not the other faction's\n• On WoW Forever, Back to the Beginning shows its objective on the quest card\n\n|cff521902Localization|r\n• All new text is in every client language. Chinese names Gryphon Master Talonaxe, and Korean names Rog'mar, the way the game does"
L["Release Notes 2.1.0"] = "|cff521902New stories|r\n• A story for each dungeon that had none, leading you in and listing the dungeon's quests: Hidden Enemies (Ragefire Chasm, Horde), Blackfathom Villainy (Blackfathom Deeps), The Mad King (Gnomeregan), and Thorns of the Razorfen (Razorfen Kraul and Razorfen Downs) on Classic Era, Burning Crusade Classic, and WoW Forever, and The City of Dalaran, Lost in the Thicket, and An Ancient Grudge (Alliance) on WoW Forever\n• Profession stories for characters who know the profession: Master of the Wild Leather (Leatherworking), The Mithril Order (Blacksmithing), and The Pledge of Secrecy (Engineering), each ending in your specialization. A story appears as soon as you learn its profession\n• WoW Forever: Strahnbrad Mystery, a short story about the Syndicate in Strahnbrad and a forge that works when no one is watching\n• WoW Forever has its first secret story. It stays out of the list until you find a way in\n\n|cff521902WoW Forever|r\n• The start page is now a letter from the author, with the settings on the facing page. The wax seal in its corner hides a few more pages\n• The Journal turns its pages like the spellbook instead of scrolling. The mouse wheel turns them too, and a page read aloud turns with the voice\n• A quest card whose giver or objective is cut off opens to show it whole\n\n|cff521902Fixes|r\n• Track Quest now leads to the quests a story quest needs first when the story doesn't include them, for 30 quests such as Incendius!, Scholomance, and Test of Lore\n• Twilight in the Riverglades: the Horde chain includes Krom'rosh's quests, so Tran'gul no longer has nothing for you\n• On WoW Forever, The Scarlet Crusade shows Past Due, and The Brazier of Invocation shows the Horde's Back to the Beginning again\n• Quests WoW Forever doesn't offer yet are optional there, so they can't hold a chapter open: the second Valor family quest in Duskwood, the quests after Onyxia's head, and the hunter's last Rhok'delar quests\n• On WoW Forever and Retail, shift-clicking a map pin no longer shows \"StoryMode has been blocked from an action only available to the Blizzard UI\". Track Quest no longer opens the map or quest log there, and its waypoint waits until the map is closed\n• The In progress filter lists only stories with a quest in your log, like Active Stories\n• Hidden quest log entries, such as tracking quests, no longer make a story look active on Retail and WoW Forever\n• The start page logo picks an image big enough for your screen again\n\n|cff521902Localization|r\n• All new text is in every client language, with the names the game uses\n• Twilight in the Riverglades names its people the way the game does in each language, and The Secret Prison, The Dying God, and The Fate of Zephras have translated titles"
L["Release Notes 2.0.1"] = "|cff521902New stories|r\n• WoW Forever: The Drowned City, where an old Gurubashi city has risen off Stranglethorn, and Highway Robbery, a looted camp in Desolace that leads to Booty Bay and the Arathi coast\n• The Green Hills, Waking Naralex, Are We There, Yeti?, and The Shards of Myzrael, plus Thunderfury on Classic Era and Burning Crusade Classic (it comes to Forever when Molten Core opens)\n• The Drakefire Amulet now ends in Onyxia's Lair, with her head hung over Stormwind's gates or the Valley of Strength\n• The Defias Brotherhood gains Westfall's Toxic Soil chapter on WoW Forever\n• Stories that send you into a dungeon list that dungeon's other quests as optional, so you can pick them all up before you go in\n\n|cff521902WoW Forever|r\n• Search the story list by title, zone, chapter, or quest, and filter it by progress, dungeons, or raids. A story found by one of its quests opens on that quest's card\n• The Journal can read itself aloud in your character's voice: click the speaker beside a chapter, or right-click it to pick a voice\n• With Gamepad turned on in the game's options, the D-pad moves around the Story Mode window, A clicks, and B closes it\n• Quest cards show the dungeon or raid icon, and the window's side tabs have icons that say what they hold\n• Explorer mode no longer pings the map, and an optional quest you skipped stays hidden until you pick it up\n\n|cff521902All clients|r\n• Open or close Story Mode with a key of your choice under Key Bindings\n• Hide the minimap button from its right-click menu; /sm minimap brings it back\n• Stories are sorted into Short Stories, Stories, and Epic Stories by every quest they hold, optional ones included, so The Drakefire Amulet is now an Epic Story\n• Chapter tooltips count optional quests, and four stories have their chapters in level order\n• The journal only tells an optional quest once you've done it\n\n|cff521902Fixes|r\n• A quest in your log is never hidden by a branch you didn't take, so The Valley of Bones stays in Active Stories\n• The Begin Story button no longer causes \"Interface action failed\" in combat\n• The Tower of Althalaxx and The Missing Courier show the real Blackfathom Deeps cover\n• Ten quest givers that had a blank portrait now show their model\n\n|cff521902Localization|r\n• All new text is in every client language, with the names the game uses"
L["Release Notes 2.0.0"] = "|cff521902WoW Forever|r\n• Story Mode now runs on WoW Forever, in a window built from Forever's own Legacy screens: Adventure, Progress, and Journal tabs, quest cards with each quest's objective and giver, and a header bar that tracks the selected story\n• Added seven stories of Forever's own: Twilight in the Riverglades, The Secret Prison, The Valley of Bones, Azshara Reclaimed, The Dying God, The Fate of Zephras, and The Cozy Sleeping Bag\n• The old-world stories include Forever's new quests, such as the Valor family of Raven Hill in Duskwood, the Apothecarium in A New Plague, and the Barrens lead-in to The Shady Rest Inn\n• The rogue story follows the letter signed C and Ravenholdt's war on the Syndicate, and the hunter story keeps the Rhok'delar bow quests\n• Choose Guided or Explorer on the start page; in Explorer each quest stays hidden until you reach it\n• Quest givers show the model the game gives them, quest objectives show in every client language, and finished quests show the day you turned them in\n• Suggested levels come from Forever's own quests, and story covers use Forever's art where it has its own\n• Story Mode no longer taints chat on Forever\n\n|cff521902Journal|r\n• Every old-world story's journal is retold in the first person, the way your character would tell it over a drink, and class stories sound like the class. The journal is now titled As I Remember It\n• Chapter intros say who's asking and why, never how it ends, and six story descriptions that gave away the plot are rewritten\n• Stories where the Alliance and the Horde start with different people only tell your side\n• Languages that change words with the narrator's gender, such as Russian, follow your character's\n\n|cff521902Classic Era and Burning Crusade Classic|r\n• Old-world stories are sorted into Epic Stories, Stories, and Short Stories by length, and several have clearer titles: The Road to Ravenholdt, Legends of Maraudon, The Key to Scholomance, Wanted: Hogger, and Arugal's Folly. Saved progress and shared links keep working\n• Checked every story's quests against the game: corrected givers and order in The Key to Scholomance, Secrets of Uldaman, Legends of Maraudon, Raene's Cleansing, The Scarlet Crusade, and the class stories, and added missing steps to the rogue, druid, hunter, shaman, warlock, and warrior stories\n• Fixed three map pins: Melyria at the Shrine of Aessina, Mokvar in Orgrimmar, and the Scholomance key quest in Stratholme\n\n|cff521902Fixes|r\n• The start page no longer comes up blank, or with a stray scroll bar, after a reload\n• Story covers keep their art's shape instead of stretching 4:3 loading screens\n• The start page logo has smooth edges, and its background is dimmed so the logo stands out\n• A story's quest count includes optional quests, so you can see what's left after the story ends\n\n|cff521902Localization|r\n• Forever stories use the names the game shows in each language for quests, characters, and places\n• All new text is in every client language"
