L["Raene Wolfrunner"] = "Raene Wolfrunner"
L["Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar was worried about Teronis, who'd gone west looking for some way to stop the furbolg attacks and hadn't come back. Raene asked me to find Teronis. I did, out by Lake Falathim. The murlocs had found Teronis first.\n\nThere was a journal on the body, though, and a glowing gem still to be found. I found it, and brought both back to Astranaar.\n\nRaene read the journal and the job changed. Teronis had been onto something, a way to slow the attacks, and it wasn't finished. The next step was a moonwell to the northeast and someone there called Shael'dryn. So off I went. Errands from the dead are still errands."] = "Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar was worried about Teronis, who'd gone west looking for some way to stop the furbolg attacks and hadn't come back. Raene asked me to find Teronis. I did, out by Lake Falathim. The murlocs had found Teronis first.\n\nThere was a journal on the body, though, and a glowing gem still to be found. I found it, and brought both back to Astranaar.\n\nRaene read the journal and the job changed. Teronis had been onto something, a way to slow the attacks, and it wasn't finished. The next step was a moonwell to the northeast and someone there called Shael'dryn. So off I went. Errands from the dead are still errands."
L["Shael'dryn, at the moonwell, knew exactly what Teronis had been after: Dartol's Rod, broken into pieces and hidden around the worst corners of Ashenvale. So it was a scavenger hunt, with twisted treants up toward Felwood holding one of the pieces and not in a sharing mood.\n\nThe pommel was the low point. It was down in the Dor'danil barrow den, and I'll spare you exactly where I found it. I washed my hands for a week.\n\nOnce the rod was whole I took it to a hidden shrine to wake it up again, and still nobody had told me what the thing actually did. That came later. It involved fur."] = "Shael'dryn, at the moonwell, knew exactly what Teronis had been after: Dartol's Rod, broken into pieces and hidden around the worst corners of Ashenvale. So it was a scavenger hunt, with twisted treants up toward Felwood holding one of the pieces and not in a sharing mood.\n\nThe pommel was the low point. It was down in the Dor'danil barrow den, and I'll spare you exactly where I found it. I washed my hands for a week.\n\nOnce the rod was whole I took it to a hidden shrine to wake it up again, and still nobody had told me what the thing actually did. That came later. It involved fur."
L["Here's what Dartol's Rod does: you use it, and you're a furbolg. Raene wanted me to find one of the few furbolg left uncorrupted, and apparently walking up in my own skin was not the way to start that conversation.\n\nKrolg was the one, southeast of Mystral Lake. Krolg had no love for the night elves and blamed them for what had happened to the furbolg. Didn't hide it, either. But Ran Bloodtooth's lot had gone bad, and Krolg wanted Ran dead.\n\nSo I obliged. Four of the Bloodtooth guards, then Ran, and Ran's skull came home with me.\n\nRaene got the skull and the rod back. I kept the memory of having fur. Not my look, honestly. And itchy."] = "Here's what Dartol's Rod does: you use it, and you're a furbolg. Raene wanted me to find one of the few furbolg left uncorrupted, and apparently walking up in my own skin was not the way to start that conversation.\n\nKrolg was the one, southeast of Mystral Lake. Krolg had no love for the night elves and blamed them for what had happened to the furbolg. Didn't hide it, either. But Ran Bloodtooth's lot had gone bad, and Krolg wanted Ran dead.\n\nSo I obliged. Four of the Bloodtooth guards, then Ran, and Ran's skull came home with me.\n\nRaene got the skull and the rod back. I kept the memory of having fur. Not my look, honestly. And itchy."
L["Raene's Cleansing"] = "Raene's Cleansing"
