L["Furlbrow's Deed"] = "Furlbrow's Deed"
L["Hooligans overran the Furlbrows' fields one night, and the couple fled in a rush. Now their wagon has broken down by the road near Jansen Stead in Westfall. Farmer Furlbrow left something precious behind, and Verna is fretting over their tired old horse."] = "Hooligans overran the Furlbrows' fields one night, and the couple fled in a rush. Now their wagon has broken down by the road near Jansen Stead in Westfall. Farmer Furlbrow left something precious behind, and Verna is fretting over their tired old horse."
L["The Forgotten Heirloom"] = "The Forgotten Heirloom"
L["On the road into Westfall there's a broken-down wagon, and beside it the Furlbrows, who left their farm in a hurry and couldn't bring much with them.\n\nFarmer Furlbrow wanted one thing. Not the farm, not the furniture. His pocket watch, still sitting in the wardrobe back at the farmhouse. So I walked out to the pumpkin farm and fetched it. Of everything a man could leave behind, that was the one he couldn't stop thinking about.\n\nVerna's worry was Blanchy, their old horse, who was hungry and getting no younger. I went through the fields picking up oats until I had eight handfuls. Blanchy ate every one and looked at me like I'd hung the moon."] = "On the road into Westfall there's a broken-down wagon, and beside it the Furlbrows, who left their farm in a hurry and couldn't bring much with them.\n\nFarmer Furlbrow wanted one thing. Not the farm, not the furniture. His pocket watch, still sitting in the wardrobe back at the farmhouse. So I walked out to the pumpkin farm and fetched it. Of everything a man could leave behind, that was the one he couldn't stop thinking about.\n\nVerna's worry was Blanchy, their old horse, who was hungry and getting no younger. I went through the fields picking up oats until I had eight handfuls. Blanchy ate every one and looked at me like I'd hung the moon."
L["Later on I turned up Furlbrow's deed in a Defias camp in Elwynn. Thieves will take anything that isn't nailed down, and a few things that are."] = "Later on I turned up Furlbrow's deed in a Defias camp in Elwynn. Thieves will take anything that isn't nailed down, and a few things that are."
L["Verna Furlbrow and her husband left their farm in a hurry, only for their wagon to break near the road into Westfall. Behind them are thieves in the fields, a farmhouse they may never see again, and a few keepsakes left in the rush.\n\nRecover what the Furlbrows could not carry, then gather oats for Blanchy. It is a small kindness on the edge of a larger ruin."] = "Verna Furlbrow and her husband left their farm in a hurry, only for their wagon to break near the road into Westfall. Behind them are thieves in the fields, a farmhouse they may never see again, and a few keepsakes left in the rush.\n\nRecover what the Furlbrows could not carry, then gather oats for Blanchy. It is a small kindness on the edge of a larger ruin."
