L["The Skeleton Key"] = "The Skeleton Key"
L["Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp wants someone inside Scholomance, the Scourge's school on Caer Darrow. The door is locked, and nobody hands out keys. Alchemist Arbington, in the same camp, thinks you can make one."] = "Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp wants someone inside Scholomance, the Scourge's school on Caer Darrow. The door is locked, and nobody hands out keys. Alchemist Arbington, in the same camp, thinks you can make one."
L["High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark wants someone inside Scholomance, the Scourge's school on Caer Darrow. The door is locked, and nobody hands out keys. Apothecary Dithers, at the Bulwark too, thinks you can make one."] = "High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark wants someone inside Scholomance, the Scourge's school on Caer Darrow. The door is locked, and nobody hands out keys. Apothecary Dithers, at the Bulwark too, thinks you can make one."
L["Caer Darrow is full of ghosts, and Eva Sarkhoff is one of the saddest. She has unfinished business with Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher, who is still at work somewhere inside Scholomance."] = "Caer Darrow is full of ghosts, and Eva Sarkhoff is one of the saddest. She has unfinished business with Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher, who is still at work somewhere inside Scholomance."
L["Magistrate Marduke, another of Caer Darrow's ghosts, wants the lich Ras Frostwhisper destroyed, and has some advice: before you fight a lich, find out who it used to be. That trail starts in the ruins of Stromgarde."] = "Magistrate Marduke, another of Caer Darrow's ghosts, wants the lich Ras Frostwhisper destroyed, and has some advice: before you fight a lich, find out who it used to be. That trail starts in the ruins of Stromgarde."
L["Weldon Barov at Chillwind Camp wants the family fortune back. It's somewhere in Scholomance, as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Somebody has to go in after them. Weldon has someone in mind."] = "Weldon Barov at Chillwind Camp wants the family fortune back. It's somewhere in Scholomance, as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Somebody has to go in after them. Weldon has someone in mind."
L["Alexi Barov, near the Bulwark, has a business proposal. The Barov fortune is lying in Scholomance as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Alexi wants them home, and would rather not fetch them personally."] = "Alexi Barov, near the Bulwark, has a business proposal. The Barov fortune is lying in Scholomance as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Alexi wants them home, and would rather not fetch them personally."
L["Scholomance has one front door and nobody hands out keys, so you make your own. Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Camp had the recipe, and it was mostly a tour of the worst corners of the world: bones from the Plaguelands, a lava lake at the top of Fire Plume Ridge, a scarab off a summoner in Andorhal.\n\nThe best stop was Gadgetzan. A goblin called Krinkle Goodsteel would turn my bones into a key mold for fifteen gold. Mold rhymes with gold. I noticed. I paid.\n\nWhen it was all done, Arbington fitted the pieces together, handed me the Skeleton Key, and called it as certain to work as anything could be. Then suggested I go and find out.\n\nThat's an alchemist for you. Confident right up to the door."] = "Scholomance has one front door and nobody hands out keys, so you make your own. Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Camp had the recipe, and it was mostly a tour of the worst corners of the world: bones from the Plaguelands, a lava lake at the top of Fire Plume Ridge, a scarab off a summoner in Andorhal.\n\nThe best stop was Gadgetzan. A goblin called Krinkle Goodsteel would turn my bones into a key mold for fifteen gold. Mold rhymes with gold. I noticed. I paid.\n\nWhen it was all done, Arbington fitted the pieces together, handed me the Skeleton Key, and called it as certain to work as anything could be. Then suggested I go and find out.\n\nThat's an alchemist for you. Confident right up to the door."
L["High Executor Derrington wanted me inside Scholomance, and Apothecary Dithers explained the catch. The door is locked, and the only key is one you build yourself, out of bones from the Plaguelands, a lava lake at the top of Fire Plume Ridge and a scarab from a summoner in Andorhal.\n\nThe bit I remember is Gadgetzan. A goblin called Krinkle Goodsteel would make the key mold, for fifteen gold. Mold, gold. I noticed. I paid anyway. You don't haggle with a goblin over something you can't make yourself.\n\nDithers put the pieces together and handed over the Skeleton Key, with a send-off about fame and power and laying waste to Scholomance.\n\nNow that's how you see somebody out the door."] = "High Executor Derrington wanted me inside Scholomance, and Apothecary Dithers explained the catch. The door is locked, and the only key is one you build yourself, out of bones from the Plaguelands, a lava lake at the top of Fire Plume Ridge and a scarab from a summoner in Andorhal.\n\nThe bit I remember is Gadgetzan. A goblin called Krinkle Goodsteel would make the key mold, for fifteen gold. Mold, gold. I noticed. I paid anyway. You don't haggle with a goblin over something you can't make yourself.\n\nDithers put the pieces together and handed over the Skeleton Key, with a send-off about fame and power and laying waste to Scholomance.\n\nNow that's how you see somebody out the door."
L["Caer Darrow is a town of ghosts, and one of the sadder ones is Eva Sarkhoff. Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher, had killed her family, and he was still at work in Scholomance.\n\nEva wanted him dead. Then she wanted her own remains burned, and her family's beside them. That's a strange thing to be asked by the person whose bones you'll be burning. I did it. It seemed to matter to her.\n\nHer last request came with a vial, the Blood of Innocents, and instructions: find the porch, put the blood in the brazier, and Kirtonos the Herald would come to feast upon my soul.\n\nKirtonos came. My soul is still with me. Kirtonos isn't."] = "Caer Darrow is a town of ghosts, and one of the sadder ones is Eva Sarkhoff. Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher, had killed her family, and he was still at work in Scholomance.\n\nEva wanted him dead. Then she wanted her own remains burned, and her family's beside them. That's a strange thing to be asked by the person whose bones you'll be burning. I did it. It seemed to matter to her.\n\nHer last request came with a vial, the Blood of Innocents, and instructions: find the porch, put the blood in the brazier, and Kirtonos the Herald would come to feast upon my soul.\n\nKirtonos came. My soul is still with me. Kirtonos isn't."
L["Ras Frostwhisper haunts Scholomance, and Ras is a lich. Magistrate Marduke, another of Caer Darrow's ghosts, had a theory about liches. You don't kill one. You remind it that it used to be a man, and then you kill the man.\n\nSo I went looking for the man. In the ruins of Stromgarde I found his Keepsake of Remembrance. Leonid Barthalomew at Light's Hope knew what to do with it, and what to do was carry it into Stratholme and set it on the unholy ground called Menethil's Gift. I won't describe that place. You've either been or you're lucky.\n\nBack in Scholomance, I held the Soulbound Keepsake up to the lich, and for one moment Ras Frostwhisper was a mortal again.\n\nIt was a short moment. Marduke got the head."] = "Ras Frostwhisper haunts Scholomance, and Ras is a lich. Magistrate Marduke, another of Caer Darrow's ghosts, had a theory about liches. You don't kill one. You remind it that it used to be a man, and then you kill the man.\n\nSo I went looking for the man. In the ruins of Stromgarde I found his Keepsake of Remembrance. Leonid Barthalomew at Light's Hope knew what to do with it, and what to do was carry it into Stratholme and set it on the unholy ground called Menethil's Gift. I won't describe that place. You've either been or you're lucky.\n\nBack in Scholomance, I held the Soulbound Keepsake up to the lich, and for one moment Ras Frostwhisper was a mortal again.\n\nIt was a short moment. Marduke got the head."
L["Weldon Barov waits at Chillwind Camp for his family's fortune to come back to him. The fortune was in Scholomance, as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Imagine owning Brill. Imagine wanting to.\n\nI brought him the deeds, and then he had one small family matter left over. His brother Alexi wanted the same fortune and was living at the Bulwark, in Horde territory. Weldon wanted Alexi's head. Alexi, he warned me, would be well protected by Horde filth.\n\nAlexi was, a bit. Not enough.\n\nI carried the head back to Chillwind, and that made Weldon the last Barov. Sounds grand. Mostly it means a smaller table at family dinners."] = "Weldon Barov waits at Chillwind Camp for his family's fortune to come back to him. The fortune was in Scholomance, as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Imagine owning Brill. Imagine wanting to.\n\nI brought him the deeds, and then he had one small family matter left over. His brother Alexi wanted the same fortune and was living at the Bulwark, in Horde territory. Weldon wanted Alexi's head. Alexi, he warned me, would be well protected by Horde filth.\n\nAlexi was, a bit. Not enough.\n\nI carried the head back to Chillwind, and that made Weldon the last Barov. Sounds grand. Mostly it means a smaller table at family dinners."
L["Alexi Barov keeps to the Bulwark these days, and Alexi had a business proposal. The Barov fortune was lying about in Scholomance as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Bring them home and the fortune was Alexi's again. Southshore included, for what that's worth.\n\nI brought them home. Then came the other half of the job. There was a brother, Weldon, down at Chillwind Camp with a claim to the very same papers, and Alexi wanted his head. Weldon, I was told, would be well protected by Alliance scum.\n\nLovely family. You could tell they were related.\n\nI walked into Chillwind and came out with the head, and Chillwind had some loud opinions about that. The last Barov. Alexi liked the sound of it."] = "Alexi Barov keeps to the Bulwark these days, and Alexi had a business proposal. The Barov fortune was lying about in Scholomance as four deeds: Caer Darrow, Brill, Tarren Mill and Southshore. Bring them home and the fortune was Alexi's again. Southshore included, for what that's worth.\n\nI brought them home. Then came the other half of the job. There was a brother, Weldon, down at Chillwind Camp with a claim to the very same papers, and Alexi wanted his head. Weldon, I was told, would be well protected by Alliance scum.\n\nLovely family. You could tell they were related.\n\nI walked into Chillwind and came out with the head, and Chillwind had some loud opinions about that. The last Barov. Alexi liked the sound of it."
