L["There's a crumpled map lying at Hammertoe's Digsite in the Badlands, and the note on it says Hammertoe Grez is alive. Prospector Ryedol, camped just down the road, will want to hear that."] = "There's a crumpled map lying at Hammertoe's Digsite in the Badlands, and the note on it says Hammertoe Grez is alive. Prospector Ryedol, camped just down the road, will want to hear that."
L["Somewhere in Uldaman, a shattered necklace is waiting to be found. Broken, but fine work. Track down whoever made it and you might learn what it's worth."] = "Somewhere in Uldaman, a shattered necklace is waiting to be found. Broken, but fine work. Track down whoever made it and you might learn what it's worth."
L["Dran Droffers, of Droffers and Son Salvage in Orgrimmar, has heard about a valuable necklace somewhere in the Uldaman dig site. Possibly damaged. Droffers doesn't mind damaged, as long as somebody brings it back."] = "Dran Droffers, of Droffers and Son Salvage in Orgrimmar, has heard about a valuable necklace somewhere in the Uldaman dig site. Possibly damaged. Droffers doesn't mind damaged, as long as somebody brings it back."
L["At the very bottom of Uldaman, behind the last of its guardians, a stone watcher keeps the Discs of Norgannon. It has been waiting a very long time for someone to come and ask it questions."] = "At the very bottom of Uldaman, behind the last of its guardians, a stone watcher keeps the Discs of Norgannon. It has been waiting a very long time for someone to come and ask it questions."
L["It started with a crumpled map in the Badlands and a note on it saying Hammertoe Grez was alive. Hammertoe was, too, down in Uldaman, and missing an amulet. I got it back.\n\nThen the amulet went on tour: to a prospector in the Badlands, to a historian in Ironforge, to an advisor by way of a note, and back to the historian again. Every leg of it, I should say, walked by me.\n\nAt the end of all that walking, somebody finally handed me a proper job. Kill Ambassador Infernus in Angor Fortress, bring back proof, then go down into Uldaman again for the Tablet of Will before the Shadowforge got to it.\n\nCourier, soldier, treasure hunter. I'd never been all three on one errand before."] = "It started with a crumpled map in the Badlands and a note on it saying Hammertoe Grez was alive. Hammertoe was, too, down in Uldaman, and missing an amulet. I got it back.\n\nThen the amulet went on tour: to a prospector in the Badlands, to a historian in Ironforge, to an advisor by way of a note, and back to the historian again. Every leg of it, I should say, walked by me.\n\nAt the end of all that walking, somebody finally handed me a proper job. Kill Ambassador Infernus in Angor Fortress, bring back proof, then go down into Uldaman again for the Tablet of Will before the Shadowforge got to it.\n\nCourier, soldier, treasure hunter. I'd never been all three on one errand before."
L["Somewhere in Uldaman I picked up a shattered necklace. Fine work, badly broken. A thing like that has a maker, so I went looking and found him in Ironforge: Talvash del Kissel. He'd tell me all about it, for five silver bars.\n\nI paid a man to tell me about his own necklace. Moving on.\n\nHis story sent me back into Uldaman, to what was left of a paladin and a journal saying where the gems had gone. Three gems, three corners of the dig, one of them in the fist of the trogg leader, who didn't let go easily. Talvash had given me a Phial of Scrying, so I could report from down there without the walk.\n\nLast, he wanted a power source off the strongest construct in the place. That was Archaedas. Talvash got his necklace back together. I got a story."] = "Somewhere in Uldaman I picked up a shattered necklace. Fine work, badly broken. A thing like that has a maker, so I went looking and found him in Ironforge: Talvash del Kissel. He'd tell me all about it, for five silver bars.\n\nI paid a man to tell me about his own necklace. Moving on.\n\nHis story sent me back into Uldaman, to what was left of a paladin and a journal saying where the gems had gone. Three gems, three corners of the dig, one of them in the fist of the trogg leader, who didn't let go easily. Talvash had given me a Phial of Scrying, so I could report from down there without the walk.\n\nLast, he wanted a power source off the strongest construct in the place. That was Archaedas. Talvash got his necklace back together. I got a story."
L["Dran Droffers runs a salvage business in Orgrimmar, Droffers and Son, and had heard about a valuable necklace somewhere in the Uldaman dig site. Probably damaged. Droffers didn't mind damaged.\n\nI found it, and it was. No gems. Down in the depths I found what was left of a paladin, and a journal that said where the gems had gone, and I couldn't read a word of it. The nearest translator was Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath, who'd do it in exchange for borrowing the necklace. Everybody wants a little something.\n\nThree gems and a power source later, the last of them pried off the strongest construct in Uldaman, I'd worn a groove in the road between Kargath and Orgrimmar, and Droffers had the necklace and the gem salvage.\n\nIn that trade, everything's salvage eventually."] = "Dran Droffers runs a salvage business in Orgrimmar, Droffers and Son, and had heard about a valuable necklace somewhere in the Uldaman dig site. Probably damaged. Droffers didn't mind damaged.\n\nI found it, and it was. No gems. Down in the depths I found what was left of a paladin, and a journal that said where the gems had gone, and I couldn't read a word of it. The nearest translator was Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath, who'd do it in exchange for borrowing the necklace. Everybody wants a little something.\n\nThree gems and a power source later, the last of them pried off the strongest construct in Uldaman, I'd worn a groove in the road between Kargath and Orgrimmar, and Droffers had the necklace and the gem salvage.\n\nIn that trade, everything's salvage eventually."
L["Past Archaedas, at the very bottom of Uldaman, sits a stone watcher that has been waiting a very long time for someone to ask it a question. I asked. It answered at length. Then I woke the Discs of Norgannon, and they answered at greater length.\n\nThe short of it: the titans shaped the world, and they made the earthen out of stone to look after it. Over the ages the earthen went soft and became something else. You've met the result. They run Ironforge.\n\nI came away with a miniature copy of the discs and took it to the Explorers' League in Ironforge. Proof of where the dwarves came from, small enough to carry under one arm.\n\nMy reward was a voucher for Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault. I found out where a whole people came from and got paid by the bank."] = "Past Archaedas, at the very bottom of Uldaman, sits a stone watcher that has been waiting a very long time for someone to ask it a question. I asked. It answered at length. Then I woke the Discs of Norgannon, and they answered at greater length.\n\nThe short of it: the titans shaped the world, and they made the earthen out of stone to look after it. Over the ages the earthen went soft and became something else. You've met the result. They run Ironforge.\n\nI came away with a miniature copy of the discs and took it to the Explorers' League in Ironforge. Proof of where the dwarves came from, small enough to carry under one arm.\n\nMy reward was a voucher for Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault. I found out where a whole people came from and got paid by the bank."
L["Behind Archaedas, at the bottom of Uldaman, a stone watcher sits waiting for someone with questions. I had a few. It had very old answers, and when it ran out, I woke the Discs of Norgannon for the rest.\n\nHere's the gist. The titans shaped the world and made the earthen out of stone to tend it, and over the ages the earthen softened into flesh. Into dwarves, as it happens. All those dwarves digging up the Badlands were digging up their own family history and didn't know it.\n\nI came away with a miniature copy of the discs and took it to Thunder Bluff, to Sage Truthseeker, who understood exactly what it was.\n\nThen I was handed a voucher for Bena Winterhoof. Secrets of creation, paid out in a slip of paper. I took it. Paper spends."] = "Behind Archaedas, at the bottom of Uldaman, a stone watcher sits waiting for someone with questions. I had a few. It had very old answers, and when it ran out, I woke the Discs of Norgannon for the rest.\n\nHere's the gist. The titans shaped the world and made the earthen out of stone to tend it, and over the ages the earthen softened into flesh. Into dwarves, as it happens. All those dwarves digging up the Badlands were digging up their own family history and didn't know it.\n\nI came away with a miniature copy of the discs and took it to Thunder Bluff, to Sage Truthseeker, who understood exactly what it was.\n\nThen I was handed a voucher for Bena Winterhoof. Secrets of creation, paid out in a slip of paper. I took it. Paper spends."
