L["Korgran has cared for Mourning Rise longer than his failing memory can reliably hold. The memorial grounds still need tending, kobolds have begun looting the dead, and Urtago is trying to help him hand over a duty he is not ready to lose.\n\nFollow Korgran through the last traditions of his post: honoring the fallen, forging a lantern, and choosing how an earthen says farewell."] = "Korgran has cared for Mourning Rise longer than his failing memory can reliably hold. The memorial grounds still need tending, kobolds have begun looting the dead, and Urtago is trying to help him hand over a duty he is not ready to lose.\n\nFollow Korgran through the last traditions of his post: honoring the fallen, forging a lantern, and choosing how an earthen says farewell."
