L["Rhea's errands looked like field work at first: wild eggs, whelps, implanted eggs, and a strange fog that hid more than geography. Then she revealed the truth. She was Rheastrasza, a red dragon trying to rescue the future of the black dragonflight before Deathwing's corruption consumed it forever.\n\nThe samples were not trophies. They were the last chance to create an uncorrupted black dragon egg."] = "Rhea's errands looked like field work at first: wild eggs, whelps, implanted eggs, and a strange fog that hid more than geography. Then she revealed the truth. She was Rheastrasza, a red dragon trying to rescue the future of the black dragonflight before Deathwing's corruption consumed it forever.\n\nThe samples were not trophies. They were the last chance to create an uncorrupted black dragon egg."
