L["Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in Darnassus hasn't heard from her sister Keldara in far too long. Keldara is posted to Talrendis Point in Azshara, where the sentinels fight the naga for the old ruins. Commander Truesong there should know where she is."] = "Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in Darnassus hasn't heard from her sister Keldara in far too long. Keldara is posted to Talrendis Point in Azshara, where the sentinels fight the naga for the old ruins. Commander Truesong there should know where she is."
L["One of Commander Truesong's sentinels has spotted a kaldorei woman alone on the Shattered Strand, plainly no fighter, with naga on every side. Truesong at Talrendis Point wants to know who she is and what she's doing out there."] = "One of Commander Truesong's sentinels has spotted a kaldorei woman alone on the Shattered Strand, plainly no fighter, with naga on every side. Truesong at Talrendis Point wants to know who she is and what she's doing out there."
L["Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar sent a dozen warriors to Azshara to guard Magus Rimtori, a blood elf mage who had promised him the riches of the highborne. That bargain has gone badly. Take Belgrom's sealed letter to Ag'tor Bloodfist at Valormok."] = "Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar sent a dozen warriors to Azshara to guard Magus Rimtori, a blood elf mage who had promised him the riches of the highborne. That bargain has gone badly. Take Belgrom's sealed letter to Ag'tor Bloodfist at Valormok."
L["In the Ruins of Eldarath, a Blackmaw furbolg named Ekkal has a score to settle with the Legashi satyr, who drove the tribe from its home. The Blackmaw are short of friends. Their gatekeeper, Rageroar, is camped to the north at Ursolan."] = "In the Ruins of Eldarath, a Blackmaw furbolg named Ekkal has a score to settle with the Legashi satyr, who drove the tribe from its home. The Blackmaw are short of friends. Their gatekeeper, Rageroar, is camped to the north at Ursolan."
L["Furze, a Blackmaw at Ursolan, is burning up with a fever that seems to unmake its victims from the inside, and Furze isn't the first to catch it. Tell Elder Bramblesnap. If anyone knows a cure, it's the elder."] = "Furze, a Blackmaw at Ursolan, is burning up with a fever that seems to unmake its victims from the inside, and Furze isn't the first to catch it. Tell Elder Bramblesnap. If anyone knows a cure, it's the elder."
L["Gatekeeper Rageroar is ready to take the fight to the Legashi, but the Blackmaw don't have the warriors for it. The Timbermaw might. Go to Timbermaw Hold in Felwood and ask Gorn One Eye for help."] = "Gatekeeper Rageroar is ready to take the fight to the Legashi, but the Blackmaw don't have the warriors for it. The Timbermaw might. Go to Timbermaw Hold in Felwood and ask Gorn One Eye for help."
L["A young sentinel in Darnassus hadn't heard from her sister in too long, so I went to Azshara to look. I found Keldara Sunblade a prisoner of the satyr, and hurt. Except she wasn't. She'd been playing it up the whole time, waiting for her captors to get careless. Turns out I was the opening she'd been waiting for.\n\nAfter that the commander at Talrendis Point put me to work on the naga picking over the old kaldorei ruins, which kept me busy a good while. It ended with Warlord Krellian, hiding behind his guards in a temple. Guards only get you so far.\n\nThe commander held that head like a promise. Azshara might be kaldorei again yet."] = "A young sentinel in Darnassus hadn't heard from her sister in too long, so I went to Azshara to look. I found Keldara Sunblade a prisoner of the satyr, and hurt. Except she wasn't. She'd been playing it up the whole time, waiting for her captors to get careless. Turns out I was the opening she'd been waiting for.\n\nAfter that the commander at Talrendis Point put me to work on the naga picking over the old kaldorei ruins, which kept me busy a good while. It ended with Warlord Krellian, hiding behind his guards in a temple. Guards only get you so far.\n\nThe commander held that head like a promise. Azshara might be kaldorei again yet."
L["One of the sentinels had spotted a kaldorei woman alone on the Shattered Strand, plainly no fighter. Saria Fairmoon. An archaeologist, more or less, digging for highborne relics while the naga looted everything around her, and very glad to find an assistant who could fight.\n\nSo I assisted. A staff from under a naga lady's nose, a crystal off a murloc, a mark of the old queen's favor. And three highborne tablets called Creation, Manipulation and Power, which in hindsight should have told me something.\n\nThen Saria wanted to show me what it had all been for, and I found out what she'd really been after.\n\nI went back to Talrendis Point with her knapsack full of artifacts and news nobody wanted. Saria didn't come with me."] = "One of the sentinels had spotted a kaldorei woman alone on the Shattered Strand, plainly no fighter. Saria Fairmoon. An archaeologist, more or less, digging for highborne relics while the naga looted everything around her, and very glad to find an assistant who could fight.\n\nSo I assisted. A staff from under a naga lady's nose, a crystal off a murloc, a mark of the old queen's favor. And three highborne tablets called Creation, Manipulation and Power, which in hindsight should have told me something.\n\nThen Saria wanted to show me what it had all been for, and I found out what she'd really been after.\n\nI went back to Talrendis Point with her knapsack full of artifacts and news nobody wanted. Saria didn't come with me."
L["Belgrom Rockmaul had sent a dozen warriors to Azshara to guard a blood elf mage who'd promised him the riches of the highborne. When I got there the warriors were dead. The mage, Magus Rimtori, had killed them all.\n\nI found the camp: three sealed crystals feeding a summoning spell, and the seals in the pockets of Rimtori's officers. I took the seals and broke them, the crystals erupted, and while Rimtori was still reeling I finished it. The head went to Belgrom.\n\nThe mage's tome ended up with a warlock in Orgrimmar, who found a demon in its diagrams and wanted its heart. So I called the thing up at the Altar of Storms and brought the heart back. The warlock never said what it was for. I didn't ask."] = "Belgrom Rockmaul had sent a dozen warriors to Azshara to guard a blood elf mage who'd promised him the riches of the highborne. When I got there the warriors were dead. The mage, Magus Rimtori, had killed them all.\n\nI found the camp: three sealed crystals feeding a summoning spell, and the seals in the pockets of Rimtori's officers. I took the seals and broke them, the crystals erupted, and while Rimtori was still reeling I finished it. The head went to Belgrom.\n\nThe mage's tome ended up with a warlock in Orgrimmar, who found a demon in its diagrams and wanted its heart. So I called the thing up at the Altar of Storms and brought the heart back. The warlock never said what it was for. I didn't ask."
L["The Blackmaw are furbolgs without a home. The Legashi satyr drove them out of their den, and they've been living in makeshift camps ever since, getting sicker.\n\nTheir gatekeeper had sent scouts to spy on the satyr stronghold and hadn't heard back. I found one of them, Korsa, alone outside the walls. One scout dead, one taken, and Korsa too ashamed to go home and say so.\n\nSo we fixed it. We cut down Master Feardred, who served the satyr lord, thinned out the stronghold, and broke Graal out of a satyr cage.\n\nThe scouts walked back into Ursolan with their heads up. That was the whole point."] = "The Blackmaw are furbolgs without a home. The Legashi satyr drove them out of their den, and they've been living in makeshift camps ever since, getting sicker.\n\nTheir gatekeeper had sent scouts to spy on the satyr stronghold and hadn't heard back. I found one of them, Korsa, alone outside the walls. One scout dead, one taken, and Korsa too ashamed to go home and say so.\n\nSo we fixed it. We cut down Master Feardred, who served the satyr lord, thinned out the stronghold, and broke Graal out of a satyr cage.\n\nThe scouts walked back into Ursolan with their heads up. That was the whole point."
L["A Blackmaw named Furze was burning up with a fever that looked like it was unmaking him from the inside, and he wasn't the first. The tribe's elder had a theory about a cure, and it was the last place anybody wanted it to be: the Legashi's own firewater.\n\nSo I went into the satyr camp for a drink. They weren't sharing, so I took the recipe off one of them and brewed my own batch in their cauldron, satyrweed and a mote of fel power. I've smelled worse. Not much worse.\n\nThe elder turned it into a tincture, and I tested it on corrupted beasts out east: knock one down, dose it, watch. It worked well enough to give the elder hope.\n\nThe first real dose went to Furze. He'd waited long enough."] = "A Blackmaw named Furze was burning up with a fever that looked like it was unmaking him from the inside, and he wasn't the first. The tribe's elder had a theory about a cure, and it was the last place anybody wanted it to be: the Legashi's own firewater.\n\nSo I went into the satyr camp for a drink. They weren't sharing, so I took the recipe off one of them and brewed my own batch in their cauldron, satyrweed and a mote of fel power. I've smelled worse. Not much worse.\n\nThe elder turned it into a tincture, and I tested it on corrupted beasts out east: knock one down, dose it, watch. It worked well enough to give the elder hope.\n\nThe first real dose went to Furze. He'd waited long enough."
L["The Blackmaw needed warriors, so I went to Timbermaw Hold to ask their cousins. Funny thing: when the satyr overran the Blackmaw, the rest of the Timbermaw sealed their passage and never knew their own kin had made it out.\n\nGorn One Eye was glad to help, and couldn't. The Timbermaw had their own war on with the Deadwood. So I brought back the Deadwood chieftain's mace, with nobody holding it, and that freed up some warriors.\n\nI planted the Timbermaw War Banner in the satyr prince's summoning circle, the reinforcements came, and the prince fell. The demon who'd moved into Blackmaw Hold went the same way.\n\nFor the first time in a long while, the Blackmaw had something to plan besides the next retreat."] = "The Blackmaw needed warriors, so I went to Timbermaw Hold to ask their cousins. Funny thing: when the satyr overran the Blackmaw, the rest of the Timbermaw sealed their passage and never knew their own kin had made it out.\n\nGorn One Eye was glad to help, and couldn't. The Timbermaw had their own war on with the Deadwood. So I brought back the Deadwood chieftain's mace, with nobody holding it, and that freed up some warriors.\n\nI planted the Timbermaw War Banner in the satyr prince's summoning circle, the reinforcements came, and the prince fell. The demon who'd moved into Blackmaw Hold went the same way.\n\nFor the first time in a long while, the Blackmaw had something to plan besides the next retreat."
