L["Years after Archimonde fell, Mount Hyjal is still scarred. Fel ash poisons its slopes, warlocks pick through the ruins of the war, and the Wild Gods who watch over the mountain have begun to falter.\n\nWhen a dying god presses a corrupted branch of the World Tree into your hands, a hermit druid, a meddling crow and the wild spirits of the mountain all have questions about it, and none of them are simple."] = "Years after Archimonde fell, Mount Hyjal is still scarred. Fel ash poisons its slopes, warlocks pick through the ruins of the war, and the Wild Gods who watch over the mountain have begun to falter.\n\nWhen a dying god presses a corrupted branch of the World Tree into your hands, a hermit druid, a meddling crow and the wild spirits of the mountain all have questions about it, and none of them are simple."
