L["Master Mathias Shaw does not teach by lecture. SI:7 sends its rogues into guarded places, locked boxes, and situations where an antidote matters as much as a blade.\n\nBegin with the work Shaw hands you, then follow the hints that lead beyond city trainers into a wider trade of signals and reputation."] = "Master Mathias Shaw does not teach by lecture. SI:7 sends its rogues into guarded places, locked boxes, and situations where an antidote matters as much as a blade.\n\nBegin with the work Shaw hands you, then follow the hints that lead beyond city trainers into a wider trade of signals and reputation."
L["Shenthul does not teach by lecture. The Shattered Hand sends its rogues into guarded places, locked boxes, and situations where an antidote matters as much as a blade.\n\nBegin with the work Shenthul hands you, then follow the hints that lead beyond city trainers into a wider trade of signals and reputation."] = "Shenthul does not teach by lecture. The Shattered Hand sends its rogues into guarded places, locked boxes, and situations where an antidote matters as much as a blade.\n\nBegin with the work Shenthul hands you, then follow the hints that lead beyond city trainers into a wider trade of signals and reputation."
L["Aramis Hammerhand in Tirisfal Glades believes the Light still answers you, whatever anyone else thinks. A paladin's lessons are not only prayers; they ask for aid given, judgment shown, and materials gathered with care.\n\nFollow the order's tests from your first doubts to the rites reserved for those who have carried the Light long enough to be trusted with more."] = "Aramis Hammerhand in Tirisfal Glades believes the Light still answers you, whatever anyone else thinks. A paladin's lessons are not only prayers; they ask for aid given, judgment shown, and materials gathered with care.\n\nFollow the order's tests from your first doubts to the rites reserved for those who have carried the Light long enough to be trusted with more."
L["In the Burning Steppes, Helendis Riverhorn has orders against the black dragonkin gathering near Morgan's Vigil.\n\nTake the first report and follow the chain of summons, proofs, and dangerous names wherever it leads. The amulet at the end of the road is not given to anyone who has only heard rumors of dragons."] = "In the Burning Steppes, Helendis Riverhorn has orders against the black dragonkin gathering near Morgan's Vigil.\n\nTake the first report and follow the chain of summons, proofs, and dangerous names wherever it leads. The amulet at the end of the road is not given to anyone who has only heard rumors of dragons."
L["In Kargath, Warlord Goretooth has a command that points into Blackrock Spire.\n\nTake the first order and follow the chain of summons, proofs, and dangerous names wherever it leads. The amulet at the end of the road is not given to anyone who has only heard rumors of dragons."] = "In Kargath, Warlord Goretooth has a command that points into Blackrock Spire.\n\nTake the first order and follow the chain of summons, proofs, and dangerous names wherever it leads. The amulet at the end of the road is not given to anyone who has only heard rumors of dragons."
L["When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Deliana in Ironforge will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."] = "When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Deliana in Ironforge will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."
L["When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Mokvar in Orgrimmar will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."] = "When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Mokvar in Orgrimmar will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."
L["Jaina Proudmoore's marines have brought in a man found washed up on the shore, and his claim is one SI:7 cannot ignore. Master Mathias Shaw wants someone discreet in Theramore to learn the truth.\n\nThe trail bends toward Alcaz Island, an old ruin off the marsh's coast that hardly anyone thinks about. Whatever waits beneath its keep, someone has gone to great lengths to hide it."] = "Jaina Proudmoore's marines have brought in a man found washed up on the shore, and his claim is one SI:7 cannot ignore. Master Mathias Shaw wants someone discreet in Theramore to learn the truth.\n\nThe trail bends toward Alcaz Island, an old ruin off the marsh's coast that hardly anyone thinks about. Whatever waits beneath its keep, someone has gone to great lengths to hide it."
L["In Orgrimmar, Eitrigg has a worry: a band of Kor'kron Elite sent into Dustwallow Marsh is long overdue, and nobody has heard a word from them.\n\nThe trail bends toward Alcaz Island, an old ruin off the marsh's coast that hardly anyone thinks about. Whatever waits beneath its keep, someone has gone to great lengths to hide it."] = "In Orgrimmar, Eitrigg has a worry: a band of Kor'kron Elite sent into Dustwallow Marsh is long overdue, and nobody has heard a word from them.\n\nThe trail bends toward Alcaz Island, an old ruin off the marsh's coast that hardly anyone thinks about. Whatever waits beneath its keep, someone has gone to great lengths to hide it."
L["Azshara's broken towers still hold the secrets of the highborne, and everyone has come to dig for them. Night elf sentinels at Talrendis Point fight the Spitelash naga for the ruins of Eldarath.\n\nTo the north, the Blackmaw furbolgs shelter in the camps of Ursolan, driven from their home by the Legashi satyr and sickening from the corruption the demons spread. Their gatekeeper is looking for allies."] = "Azshara's broken towers still hold the secrets of the highborne, and everyone has come to dig for them. Night elf sentinels at Talrendis Point fight the Spitelash naga for the ruins of Eldarath.\n\nTo the north, the Blackmaw furbolgs shelter in the camps of Ursolan, driven from their home by the Legashi satyr and sickening from the corruption the demons spread. Their gatekeeper is looking for allies."
L["Azshara's broken towers still hold the secrets of the highborne, and everyone has come to dig for them. At Valormok, the Horde has paid in blood for trusting a blood elf mage.\n\nTo the north, the Blackmaw furbolgs shelter in the camps of Ursolan, driven from their home by the Legashi satyr and sickening from the corruption the demons spread. Their gatekeeper is looking for allies."] = "Azshara's broken towers still hold the secrets of the highborne, and everyone has come to dig for them. At Valormok, the Horde has paid in blood for trusting a blood elf mage.\n\nTo the north, the Blackmaw furbolgs shelter in the camps of Ursolan, driven from their home by the Legashi satyr and sickening from the corruption the demons spread. Their gatekeeper is looking for allies."
L["No one has held the Riverglades for long. The humans of Farholde Keep, who feel Stormwind has forgotten them, have fought the orcs of Rog'mar across the river for years. Now the Twilight's Hammer has burned the village of Sunnyglade and started digging under the hills.\n\nFarholde needs to know what the cult is looking for."] = "No one has held the Riverglades for long. The humans of Farholde Keep, who feel Stormwind has forgotten them, have fought the orcs of Rog'mar across the river for years. Now the Twilight's Hammer has burned the village of Sunnyglade and started digging under the hills.\n\nFarholde needs to know what the cult is looking for."
L["No one has held the Riverglades for long. The orcs of Rog'mar have fought the humans of Farholde Keep across the river for years. Now the Twilight's Hammer has burned the village of Sunnyglade and started digging under the hills.\n\nRog'mar needs to know what the cult is looking for, and the answer may lie with ogres who have already turned their backs on it."] = "No one has held the Riverglades for long. The orcs of Rog'mar have fought the humans of Farholde Keep across the river for years. Now the Twilight's Hammer has burned the village of Sunnyglade and started digging under the hills.\n\nRog'mar needs to know what the cult is looking for, and the answer may lie with ogres who have already turned their backs on it."
