L["Lorekeeper Nok at Ursolan wanted two totems brought out of Blackmaw Hold, one for Ursoc and one for Ursol, the twin bears every furbolg looks up to. I found both and carried them very carefully. Losing a fight in there is one thing. Dropping a demigod on the way home is another."] = "Lorekeeper Nok at Ursolan wanted two totems brought out of Blackmaw Hold, one for Ursoc and one for Ursol, the twin bears every furbolg looks up to. I found both and carried them very carefully. Losing a fight in there is one thing. Dropping a demigod on the way home is another."
L["Ekkal wanted five Blackmaw pouches fetched out of the hold. Not weapons, not treasure. Pouches. I didn't look inside. Some things you carry without asking, and a furbolg's pouch is one of them."] = "Ekkal wanted five Blackmaw pouches fetched out of the hold. Not weapons, not treasure. Pouches. I didn't look inside. Some things you carry without asking, and a furbolg's pouch is one of them."
L["Ogtinc, out by the Ruins of Eldarath, wanted the claws of the Great Bear and the tusks of the Unbroken from inside the hold. Both came attached to their owners, who had opinions about that. Claws that rend and tusks that gore, I'd been warned. I can confirm both."] = "Ogtinc, out by the Ruins of Eldarath, wanted the claws of the Great Bear and the tusks of the Unbroken from inside the hold. Both came attached to their owners, who had opinions about that. Claws that rend and tusks that gore, I'd been warned. I can confirm both."
L["In the hold I came across a feathered charm necklace that plainly belonged to somebody. Somebody turned out to be Unele, back at Ursolan, so I gave it back. Some loot is worth more returned than sold."] = "In the hold I came across a feathered charm necklace that plainly belonged to somebody. Somebody turned out to be Unele, back at Ursolan, so I gave it back. Some loot is worth more returned than sold."
L["Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus wanted ten Nordrassil root caps, and the place to pick them, of all places, was Blackmaw Hold. I picked ten. I didn't ask what a druid wants with them. Ask a druid a question and the answer takes the rest of the afternoon."] = "Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus wanted ten Nordrassil root caps, and the place to pick them, of all places, was Blackmaw Hold. I picked ten. I didn't ask what a druid wants with them. Ask a druid a question and the answer takes the rest of the afternoon."
L["Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff wanted ten Nordrassil root caps, and the place to pick them, of all places, was Blackmaw Hold. I picked ten, between fights. I didn't ask what they were for. Up on the Elder Rise a question turns into a lesson, and the lesson turns into the evening."] = "Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff wanted ten Nordrassil root caps, and the place to pick them, of all places, was Blackmaw Hold. I picked ten, between fights. I didn't ask what they were for. Up on the Elder Rise a question turns into a lesson, and the lesson turns into the evening."
L["Archmage Timear of the Kirin Tor wanted a Blackmaw ritual totem brought out of the hold. I found one and carried it all the way to Dalaran. Mages will study anything that sits still long enough. Totems are very good at sitting still."] = "Archmage Timear of the Kirin Tor wanted a Blackmaw ritual totem brought out of the hold. I found one and carried it all the way to Dalaran. Mages will study anything that sits still long enough. Totems are very good at sitting still."
L["Muln Earthfury of the Earthen Ring wanted a Blackmaw ritual totem brought out of the hold. I found one and carried it home to Mulgore. I didn't ask what it had to say. With the Earthen Ring, the totems do most of the talking."] = "Muln Earthfury of the Earthen Ring wanted a Blackmaw ritual totem brought out of the hold. I found one and carried it home to Mulgore. I didn't ask what it had to say. With the Earthen Ring, the totems do most of the talking."
L["Ashe Amberhall had one more use for the satchel of cult trinkets from Krol'dok: send it across the keep to Melanie Sable, the enchanter. Curios, Ashe called them. I'd have called them evidence. I suppose to an enchanter it's all just material."] = "Ashe Amberhall had one more use for the satchel of cult trinkets from Krol'dok: send it across the keep to Melanie Sable, the enchanter. Curios, Ashe called them. I'd have called them evidence. I suppose to an enchanter it's all just material."
L["Before I went into Krol'dok, Ranath Nightstride in Dalaran gave me a name to look for: Zalfan Moonshadow. Ranath is Highborne, and undead, and called it vengeance. I didn't ask for the history. With the Highborne there's always history, and it's always long. Zalfan didn't come out of Krol'dok."] = "Before I went into Krol'dok, Ranath Nightstride in Dalaran gave me a name to look for: Zalfan Moonshadow. Ranath is Highborne, and undead, and called it vengeance. I didn't ask for the history. With the Highborne there's always history, and it's always long. Zalfan didn't come out of Krol'dok."
L["Deathguard Kristof had reports of an unholy fog over the ruins, with the Scourge moving about inside it and a new necromancer called Rath'mael behind it all. I took friends, and we put Rath'mael down. Kristof expects another one along soon, because deathguards are not optimists."] = "Deathguard Kristof had reports of an unholy fog over the ruins, with the Scourge moving about inside it and a new necromancer called Rath'mael behind it all. I took friends, and we put Rath'mael down. Kristof expects another one along soon, because deathguards are not optimists."
L["Tabitha Heartweaver at the Sepulcher had a husband, Edward, who walked to a graveyard in the ruins every week to look for the son they lost when the city fell. One week he didn't come home. I went in and found out why, and that part stays between Tabitha and me."] = "Tabitha Heartweaver at the Sepulcher had a husband, Edward, who walked to a graveyard in the ruins every week to look for the son they lost when the city fell. One week he didn't come home. I went in and found out why, and that part stays between Tabitha and me."
L["Morbin Lightbane serves the Light and the Dark Lady both and sees no trouble in it. What Morbin wanted was twenty-five intact limbs off the Scourge in the ruins: spare parts, for Forsaken whose own were wearing out. The Scourge had no further use for theirs by the time I left."] = "Morbin Lightbane serves the Light and the Dark Lady both and sees no trouble in it. What Morbin wanted was twenty-five intact limbs off the Scourge in the ruins: spare parts, for Forsaken whose own were wearing out. The Scourge had no further use for theirs by the time I left."
L["Somewhere in the ruins I picked up an old crest with Lordaeron's mark on it, and Oran Snakewrithe in the Undercity was glad to have it. Oran checked it was genuine by biting it. I've seen people test gold that way, never history."] = "Somewhere in the ruins I picked up an old crest with Lordaeron's mark on it, and Oran Snakewrithe in the Undercity was glad to have it. Oran checked it was genuine by biting it. I've seen people test gold that way, never history."
L["The thing I put down in the ruins lost its head, and Faranell knew whose it was: a grand marshal the Dark Lady had killed personally. Faranell found the head a new body, and it woke up calling me an abomination, which was rich, coming from it. I put a serum in the drip above it, and now it simmers in its new home while Faranell makes plans."] = "The thing I put down in the ruins lost its head, and Faranell knew whose it was: a grand marshal the Dark Lady had killed personally. Faranell found the head a new body, and it woke up calling me an abomination, which was rich, coming from it. I put a serum in the drip above it, and now it simmers in its new home while Faranell makes plans."
L["Alba Fairmoon at Sentinel Hill had traced the poison in Westfall's soil to a forge hidden in the Deadmines, and handed me something labeled Extra-Destructive Explosives. I found the forge and tucked them in close. Then I walked back out at a very respectful pace."] = "Alba Fairmoon at Sentinel Hill had traced the poison in Westfall's soil to a forge hidden in the Deadmines, and handed me something labeled Extra-Destructive Explosives. I found the forge and tucked them in close. Then I walked back out at a very respectful pace."
L["Wilder Thistlenettle got out when the tunnel came down in the mine under Moonbrook, but the foreman, Wilder's brother, didn't. Wilder asked me for the Explorers' League badge the foreman never went anywhere without. I brought the badge back, and Wilder had already guessed what that meant."] = "Wilder Thistlenettle got out when the tunnel came down in the mine under Moonbrook, but the foreman, Wilder's brother, didn't. Wilder asked me for the Explorers' League badge the foreman never went anywhere without. I brought the badge back, and Wilder had already guessed what that meant."
L["Wilder Thistlenettle lost a good many workmates in the collapsed wing of the mine under Moonbrook, and wanted their Miners' Union Cards brought out so the families would know. I brought out four. Wilder took them like letters nobody wants to deliver."] = "Wilder Thistlenettle lost a good many workmates in the collapsed wing of the mine under Moonbrook, and wanted their Miners' Union Cards brought out so the families would know. I brought out four. Wilder took them like letters nobody wants to deliver."
L["Motley Garmason at Dun Modr hates the Dark Irons in general and Kam Deepfury in particular, since Deepfury helped plan the attack on the Thandol Span. Stormwind kept Deepfury tucked away in the Stockade for reasons of politics. Motley had no use for politics, and after my visit, neither did Deepfury."] = "Motley Garmason at Dun Modr hates the Dark Irons in general and Kam Deepfury in particular, since Deepfury helped plan the attack on the Thandol Span. Stormwind kept Deepfury tucked away in the Stockade for reasons of politics. Motley had no use for politics, and after my visit, neither did Deepfury."
L["Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wanted Dextren Ward's hand. Ward had sold bodies out of Duskwood's cemetery, and Darkshire sentenced him to death, but the nobles in Stormwind kept him in the Stockade instead. I carried out Darkshire's sentence, and the councilman took the hand as a message to the nobles."] = "Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wanted Dextren Ward's hand. Ward had sold bodies out of Duskwood's cemetery, and Darkshire sentenced him to death, but the nobles in Stormwind kept him in the Stockade instead. I carried out Darkshire's sentence, and the councilman took the hand as a message to the nobles."
L["Nikova Raskol's grandson Mac was fourteen and a guard in the Stockade, and he got a knife in the back for telling the Defias to stop tearing their blankets into bandanas. Nikova wanted ten of those bandanas, and I brought them. They didn't bring Mac back, and Nikova knew that better than I did."] = "Nikova Raskol's grandson Mac was fourteen and a guard in the Stockade, and he got a knife in the back for telling the Defias to stop tearing their blankets into bandanas. Nikova wanted ten of those bandanas, and I brought them. They didn't bring Mac back, and Nikova knew that better than I did."
L["Guard Berton in Lakeshire remembered Targorr the Dread, who tortured Stormwind's soldiers for Gath'Ilzogg, and didn't trust the noble who kept putting off the execution. So Berton skipped the courts and sent me. Berton called it justice beyond the reach of politics, and Targorr didn't get a say."] = "Guard Berton in Lakeshire remembered Targorr the Dread, who tortured Stormwind's soldiers for Gath'Ilzogg, and didn't trust the noble who kept putting off the execution. So Berton skipped the courts and sent me. Berton called it justice beyond the reach of politics, and Targorr didn't get a say."
L["Lethtendris had built a web in Dire Maul to soak up the magic leaking out of the place, and fancied herself its master. Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon thought otherwise and wanted the web, to let the magic out over the wilds and then smash the thing. I settled the argument for them."] = "Lethtendris had built a web in Dire Maul to soak up the magic leaking out of the place, and fancied herself its master. Latronicus Moonspear at Feathermoon thought otherwise and wanted the web, to let the magic out over the wilds and then smash the thing. I settled the argument for them."
L["Lethtendris had built a web in Dire Maul to soak up the magic leaking out of the place, and meant to aim it at her enemies. Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache reckoned she'd never hand it over alive, and Talo was right. The web went off to someone more responsible, which by then was nearly anybody."] = "Lethtendris had built a web in Dire Maul to soak up the magic leaking out of the place, and meant to aim it at her enemies. Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache reckoned she'd never hand it over alive, and Talo was right. The web went off to someone more responsible, which by then was nearly anybody."
L["Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon was after an old elven master whose trail ran from Quel'Thalas all the way to Dire Maul, along with a cartload of lost artifacts. I found where the trail ended. Runethorn took the news hard, and the lack of artifacts harder."] = "Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon was after an old elven master whose trail ran from Quel'Thalas all the way to Dire Maul, along with a cartload of lost artifacts. I found where the trail ended. Runethorn took the news hard, and the lack of artifacts harder."
L["Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache was after an old elven master whose trail ran from Quel'Thalas all the way to Dire Maul, along with a cartload of lost artifacts. I found where the trail ended. Korolusk took the news hard, and the lack of artifacts harder."] = "Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache was after an old elven master whose trail ran from Quel'Thalas all the way to Dire Maul, along with a cartload of lost artifacts. I found where the trail ended. Korolusk took the news hard, and the lack of artifacts harder."
L["Azj'Tordin, an old Shen'dralar lying low at the Lariss Pavilion, had been robbed by an imp called Pusillin: one Book of Incantations, with the key to Dire Maul thrown in. Getting the book back meant chasing Pusillin all over the Warpwood Quarter. Azj'Tordin regretted nothing, and I only regretted the running."] = "Azj'Tordin, an old Shen'dralar lying low at the Lariss Pavilion, had been robbed by an imp called Pusillin: one Book of Incantations, with the key to Dire Maul thrown in. Getting the book back meant chasing Pusillin all over the Warpwood Quarter. Azj'Tordin regretted nothing, and I only regretted the running."
L["The Shen'dralar Ancient in the courtyard wanted the madness in Dire Maul ended, which meant five pylons, one caged demon, and finally Prince Tortheldrin. I'd been warned the Prince was persuasive, and he wasn't persuasive enough. The reward was a chest tucked under the library stairs, which is exactly where I'd hide treasure too."] = "The Shen'dralar Ancient in the courtyard wanted the madness in Dire Maul ended, which meant five pylons, one caged demon, and finally Prince Tortheldrin. I'd been warned the Prince was persuasive, and he wasn't persuasive enough. The reward was a chest tucked under the library stairs, which is exactly where I'd hide treasure too."
L["Prince Tortheldrin looked a great deal older dead than he had alive, as if the centuries had all caught up with him at once. One of his glaives lay beside him, snapped in two. I took the pieces to the Shen'dralar Ancients, who wanted to hear every detail."] = "Prince Tortheldrin looked a great deal older dead than he had alive, as if the centuries had all caught up with him at once. One of his glaives lay beside him, snapped in two. I took the pieces to the Shen'dralar Ancients, who wanted to hear every detail."
L["I returned Nostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the library, and Lorekeeper Lydros mentioned what it would have fetched on the black market. Then I showed Lydros a dull, flat elven blade and got instructions back: heat it in a certain dragon's breath and temper it in her blood. Lydros said it like a recipe."] = "I returned Nostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the library, and Lorekeeper Lydros mentioned what it would have fetched on the black market. Then I showed Lydros a dull, flat elven blade and got instructions back: heat it in a certain dragon's breath and temper it in her blood. Lydros said it like a recipe."
L["Knot Thimblejack, a goblin chained up in the Gordok wing, offered to sew me an ogre suit if I brought the runecloth, leather and ogre tannin. It would hold together for ten minutes. Knot reckoned that was plenty to fool an ogre captain, and Knot has had a long time to study ogres."] = "Knot Thimblejack, a goblin chained up in the Gordok wing, offered to sew me an ogre suit if I brought the runecloth, leather and ogre tannin. It would hold together for ten minutes. Knot reckoned that was plenty to fool an ogre captain, and Knot has had a long time to study ogres."
L["Knot Thimblejack had been chained up by the ogres long enough to have pet names for them. One of them was carrying the shackle key, so I let Knot go. Knot said a goblin's life was meant for more than being an ogre's appetizer, and I didn't argue."] = "Knot Thimblejack had been chained up by the ogres long enough to have pet names for them. One of them was carrying the shackle key, so I let Knot go. Knot said a goblin's life was meant for more than being an ogre's appetizer, and I didn't argue."
L["Captain Kromcrush had an old story about a creepy elf calling himself a prince, who stole the Gauntlet of Gordok Might from an ogre king. The story was true, and the gauntlet was sitting in the prince's own chest. Kromcrush put the magic back into it and handed it to the new king, long live me."] = "Captain Kromcrush had an old story about a creepy elf calling himself a prince, who stole the Gauntlet of Gordok Might from an ogre king. The story was true, and the gauntlet was sitting in the prince's own chest. Kromcrush put the magic back into it and handed it to the new king, long live me."
L["Being king of the Gordok came with one perk worth mentioning: Stomper Kreeg, who keeps the brews, brought me free samples of the good stuff. One of them was called Kreeg's Stout Beatdown. Honest name."] = "Being king of the Gordok came with one perk worth mentioning: Stomper Kreeg, who keeps the brews, brought me free samples of the good stuff. One of them was called Kreeg's Stout Beatdown. Honest name."
L["I found the Codex of Defense in a pile of dust in Dire Maul and gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. Never read it. Didn't need to."] = "I found the Codex of Defense in a pile of dust in Dire Maul and gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. Never read it. Didn't need to."
L["The Light and How To Swing It was gathering dust in Dire Maul, so I returned it, because that's what you do with a library book. The librarians gave me a royal seal. The title had already told me everything inside."] = "The Light and How To Swing It was gathering dust in Dire Maul, so I returned it, because that's what you do with a library book. The librarians gave me a royal seal. The title had already told me everything inside."
L["The librarians paid a royal seal for The Greatest Race of Hunters, which I'd found in the dust in Dire Maul. My pet wanted to chew it first. I said no, mostly."] = "The librarians paid a royal seal for The Greatest Race of Hunters, which I'd found in the dust in Dire Maul. My pet wanted to chew it first. I said no, mostly."
L["Garona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery was lying in the dust in Dire Maul, unguarded. I could have sold it, but the librarians offered a royal seal, and for once honest work paid better."] = "Garona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery was lying in the dust in Dire Maul, unguarded. I could have sold it, but the librarians offered a royal seal, and for once honest work paid better."
L["There was a book in the dust at Dire Maul called Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You. I gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. They didn't ask whether I'd read it, and I didn't say."] = "There was a book in the dust at Dire Maul called Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You. I gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. They didn't ask whether I'd read it, and I didn't say."
L["Frost Shock and You turned up in the dust in Dire Maul, and the librarians gave me a royal seal to have it back. The elements had opinions about that title. For once I agreed with them."] = "Frost Shock and You turned up in the dust in Dire Maul, and the librarians gave me a royal seal to have it back. The elements had opinions about that title. For once I agreed with them."
L["Somebody had left The Arcanist's Cookbook lying in the dust in Dire Maul, so I returned it to the librarians for a royal seal. Did I try any of the recipes first? I'm not saying."] = "Somebody had left The Arcanist's Cookbook lying in the dust in Dire Maul, so I returned it to the librarians for a royal seal. Did I try any of the recipes first? I'm not saying."
L["A tome called Harnessing Shadows was lying in the dust in Dire Maul. I gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. Some of the company I keep would have kept it, but they're not the sort you lend books to."] = "A tome called Harnessing Shadows was lying in the dust in Dire Maul. I gave it back to the librarians for a royal seal. Some of the company I keep would have kept it, but they're not the sort you lend books to."
L["I found The Emerald Dream lying in the dust in Dire Maul and took my time returning it. The librarians gave me a royal seal anyway. They'd waited this long; another afternoon did them no harm."] = "I found The Emerald Dream lying in the dust in Dire Maul and took my time returning it. The librarians gave me a royal seal anyway. They'd waited this long; another afternoon did them no harm."
L["Tabetha keeps a farm out in the Dustwallow muck, and while she was away somebody raided it and made off with her Tiara of the Deep. It turned up on Hydromancer Velratha, a sand troll in Zul'Farrak. I brought it home, and Tabetha apologized for having been so sharp with me, which almost never happens."] = "Tabetha keeps a farm out in the Dustwallow muck, and while she was away somebody raided it and made off with her Tiara of the Deep. It turned up on Hydromancer Velratha, a sand troll in Zul'Farrak. I brought it home, and Tabetha apologized for having been so sharp with me, which almost never happens."
L["Tran'rek in Gadgetzan had promised a cousin in Booty Bay a load of scarab shells weeks ago and was still telling stories instead of delivering. The last scarabs in Tanaris live in Zul'Farrak, so I went and got five. Uncracked, as ordered, though the scarabs had their own ideas about that."] = "Tran'rek in Gadgetzan had promised a cousin in Booty Bay a load of scarab shells weeks ago and was still telling stories instead of delivering. The last scarabs in Tanaris live in Zul'Farrak, so I went and got five. Uncracked, as ordered, though the scarabs had their own ideas about that."
L["Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan had lent a Divino-matic Rod, a gadget for finding water, to a Sergeant Bly, who took it into Zul'Farrak with a band of adventurers and kept it. I found Bly and asked nicely. Then I asked the other way, which the engineer liked a lot better."] = "Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan had lent a Divino-matic Rod, a gadget for finding water, to a Sergeant Bly, who took it into Zul'Farrak with a band of adventurers and kept it. I found Bly and asked nicely. Then I asked the other way, which the engineer liked a lot better."
L["Trenton Lighthammer in Gadgetzan wanted twenty vials of troll temper, which the Sandfury brew out of sandstone. They carry it on them, so gathering it was mostly a matter of gathering trolls. Trenton called it very nice temper indeed, and I've never thought about temper since."] = "Trenton Lighthammer in Gadgetzan wanted twenty vials of troll temper, which the Sandfury brew out of sandstone. They carry it on them, so gathering it was mostly a matter of gathering trolls. Trenton called it very nice temper indeed, and I've never thought about temper since."
L["Wizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway wanted an electrified scale off Gahz'rilla to power a racing car. Gahz'rilla is a hydra the Zul'Farrak trolls keep in a sacred pool, and they don't lend it out. Wizzle's only question when I got back was how big it really was, and the honest answer is bigger than whatever you're picturing."] = "Wizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway wanted an electrified scale off Gahz'rilla to power a racing car. Gahz'rilla is a hydra the Zul'Farrak trolls keep in a sacred pool, and they don't lend it out. Wizzle's only question when I got back was how big it really was, and the honest answer is bigger than whatever you're picturing."
L["Mallet of Zul'Farrak"] = "Mallet of Zul'Farrak"
L["the Altar of Zul, The Hinterlands"] = "the Altar of Zul, The Hinterlands"
L["Take the Sacred Mallet from Qiaga the Keeper at the top of the Altar of Zul. Then use it at the altar at the top of Jintha'Alor to make the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, which rings the gong at Gahz'rilla's pool."] = "Take the Sacred Mallet from Qiaga the Keeper at the top of the Altar of Zul. Then use it at the altar at the top of Jintha'Alor to make the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, which rings the gong at Gahz'rilla's pool."
L["The gong at Gahz'rilla's pool in Zul'Farrak answers to one mallet, and nobody sells it. Qiaga the Keeper had the Sacred Mallet at the top of the Altar of Zul and no plans to give it up. I took it anyway. It still had to go to the altar at the top of Jintha'Alor, and one use there made it the Mallet of Zul'Farrak.\n\nIt doesn't break and it doesn't get used up, so I can ring for that hydra whenever I like. Whether I'd like to is another matter."] = "The gong at Gahz'rilla's pool in Zul'Farrak answers to one mallet, and nobody sells it. Qiaga the Keeper had the Sacred Mallet at the top of the Altar of Zul and no plans to give it up. I took it anyway. It still had to go to the altar at the top of Jintha'Alor, and one use there made it the Mallet of Zul'Farrak.\n\nIt doesn't break and it doesn't get used up, so I can ring for that hydra whenever I like. Whether I'd like to is another matter."
L["Venom Bottle"] = "Venom Bottle"
L["In a Witherbark village in the Hinterlands there were more bottles of vile green venom than any troll needs, so I took one to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Lydon wanted better than a bottle: an undamaged venom sac, and undamaged was the hard part. Once Lydon had it, the question was what kind of spider the trolls had been milking, and Lydon sent me to ask Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, who knows trolls."] = "In a Witherbark village in the Hinterlands there were more bottles of vile green venom than any troll needs, so I took one to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Lydon wanted better than a bottle: an undamaged venom sac, and undamaged was the hard part. Once Lydon had it, the question was what kind of spider the trolls had been milking, and Lydon sent me to ask Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, who knows trolls."
L["Gryphon Master Talonaxe at Aerie Peak had lost a young gryphon called Sharpbeak and suspected the Witherbark trolls. I searched the cages in both of their villages and found no gryphon. At the top of the Altar of Zul I found one of Sharpbeak's feathers, and no Sharpbeak. Talonaxe sent me off with the feather to Thadius Grimshade at Nethergarde Keep, who finds things by other means."] = "Gryphon Master Talonaxe at Aerie Peak had lost a young gryphon called Sharpbeak and suspected the Witherbark trolls. I searched the cages in both of their villages and found no gryphon. At the top of the Altar of Zul I found one of Sharpbeak's feathers, and no Sharpbeak. Talonaxe sent me off with the feather to Thadius Grimshade at Nethergarde Keep, who finds things by other means."
L["Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village needed the true name of the spider god the Witherbark worship, and it was written on a tablet in Zul'Farrak that Theka the Martyr was guarding. Theka stopped guarding it. The name is Elortha no Shadra, and I'm told to say it only in whispers, so lean in."] = "Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village needed the true name of the spider god the Witherbark worship, and it was written on a tablet in Zul'Farrak that Theka the Martyr was guarding. Theka stopped guarding it. The name is Elortha no Shadra, and I'm told to say it only in whispers, so lean in."
L["Mazu'kon, out in Mulgore, wanted the head of Witch Doctor Zum'rah, who keeps the graveyard in Zul'Farrak and doesn't welcome visitors. Zum'rah raised the dead at us by the handful. The head came back with me anyway, which was the only part Mazu'kon cared about."] = "Mazu'kon, out in Mulgore, wanted the head of Witch Doctor Zum'rah, who keeps the graveyard in Zul'Farrak and doesn't welcome visitors. Zum'rah raised the dead at us by the handful. The head came back with me anyway, which was the only part Mazu'kon cared about."
L["Thadius Grimshade at Nethergarde Keep offered to find a lost gryphon named Sharpbeak by magic, in exchange for Nekrum Gutchewer's medallion out of Zul'Farrak. Rumor said it gave its wearer an unnaturally long life at a price, and Grimshade was confident the price could be avoided. They always are."] = "Thadius Grimshade at Nethergarde Keep offered to find a lost gryphon named Sharpbeak by magic, in exchange for Nekrum Gutchewer's medallion out of Zul'Farrak. Rumor said it gave its wearer an unnaturally long life at a price, and Grimshade was confident the price could be avoided. They always are."
L["Archmage Lan'dalock of Dalaran wanted the head of Witch Doctor Zum'rah, who keeps the graveyard in Zul'Farrak. Zum'rah's reply was to wake the graveyard up. The archmage got the head all the same, and I learned that the dead there stay down only once their witch doctor does."] = "Archmage Lan'dalock of Dalaran wanted the head of Witch Doctor Zum'rah, who keeps the graveyard in Zul'Farrak. Zum'rah's reply was to wake the graveyard up. The archmage got the head all the same, and I learned that the dead there stay down only once their witch doctor does."
L["Marvon Rivetseeker, a goblin who studies troll ruins, had been inside the Sunken Temple once and nearly died poking a serpent statue. Marvon's theory was that the altar at the bottom of the round room held the secret, so down I went with a stone circle to test it. It fit exactly and locked in place, which in that temple is never the end of it."] = "Marvon Rivetseeker, a goblin who studies troll ruins, had been inside the Sunken Temple once and nearly died poking a serpent statue. Marvon's theory was that the altar at the bottom of the round room held the secret, so down I went with a stone circle to test it. It fit exactly and locked in place, which in that temple is never the end of it."
L["Marvon Rivetseeker had a hazy memory of lights over the ring of serpent statues in the Sunken Temple, and a hunch they guarded treasure. Light them in the right order and something does happen: a very large guardian turns up to object. Behind the idol's glass eye sat the Atal'ai treasure, worth every bit of the argument."] = "Marvon Rivetseeker had a hazy memory of lights over the ring of serpent statues in the Sunken Temple, and a hunch they guarded treasure. Light them in the right order and something does happen: a very large guardian turns up to object. Behind the idol's glass eye sat the Atal'ai treasure, worth every bit of the argument."
L["Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind had one last assignment for the Explorers' League before retiring: ten Atal'ai tablets out of the Sunken Temple. Pride kept him from asking for help, right up until he asked me. I brought the tablets, and Brohann said both our names would go into the League's history, though I've never gone to check."] = "Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind had one last assignment for the Explorers' League before retiring: ten Atal'ai tablets out of the Sunken Temple. Pride kept him from asking for help, right up until he asked me. I brought the tablets, and Brohann said both our names would go into the League's history, though I've never gone to check."
L["Fel'zerul in Stonard didn't trust the Atal'ai or their talk of Hakkar making them immortal, and wanted twenty of their Fetishes of Hakkar to learn what they were for. Twenty is a lot of fetishes. Every one of them came off an Atal'ai who believed very sincerely."] = "Fel'zerul in Stonard didn't trust the Atal'ai or their talk of Hakkar making them immortal, and wanted twenty of their Fetishes of Hakkar to learn what they were for. Twenty is a lot of fetishes. Every one of them came off an Atal'ai who believed very sincerely."
L["An Atal'ai exile out in the Hinterlands, cast out by the tribe, wanted the head of Jammal'an the Prophet, who had convinced them all that Hakkar would make them immortal. I brought the head. The exile had hoped it might free the tribe, and mourned them anyway."] = "An Atal'ai exile out in the Hinterlands, cast out by the tribe, wanted the head of Jammal'an the Prophet, who had convinced them all that Hakkar would make them immortal. I brought the head. The exile had hoped it might free the tribe, and mourned them anyway."
L["When the shade of Eranikus fell, it left a gem holding part of the dragon's essence, and a voice asking me to set it in the font in its lair so it could finally rest. I did, and the font turned out to be tainted as well, and the last I heard was Eranikus begging me to find the green dragonflight. I've done favors that went better."] = "When the shade of Eranikus fell, it left a gem holding part of the dragon's essence, and a voice asking me to set it in the font in its lair so it could finally rest. I did, and the font turned out to be tainted as well, and the last I heard was Eranikus begging me to find the green dragonflight. I've done favors that went better."
L["Olana Brighthoof, a sun priest near Thunder Bluff, had seen it in a vision: past Earth Song Falls, a chamber of white crystals with giants on guard, and at the very top, the right eye of the Earthmother. The vision was right about everything, giants included. I carried it back to Mulgore, where it belongs, under the open sky."] = "Olana Brighthoof, a sun priest near Thunder Bluff, had seen it in a vision: past Earth Song Falls, a chamber of white crystals with giants on guard, and at the very top, the right eye of the Earthmother. The vision was right about everything, giants included. I carried it back to Mulgore, where it belongs, under the open sky."
L["In the lower Spire a goblin named Bijou, who doesn't usually deal with my sort, traded me a map for her lost belongings. Marshal Maxwell picked three names off it, a war master, a highlord and an overlord, and sent me back to cross them out. That bought the Alliance precious, precious time, he said, precious enough to say twice."] = "In the lower Spire a goblin named Bijou, who doesn't usually deal with my sort, traded me a map for her lost belongings. Marshal Maxwell picked three names off it, a war master, a highlord and an overlord, and sent me back to cross them out. That bought the Alliance precious, precious time, he said, precious enough to say twice."
L["A dead serpent in the lower Spire turned out to be carrying a letter: General Drakkisath's own orders, mostly about protocol. Marshal Maxwell read it, said the plot thickened, and sent me back up to destroy the general. I was going anyway, but I let him think it was his idea."] = "A dead serpent in the lower Spire turned out to be carrying a letter: General Drakkisath's own orders, mostly about protocol. Marshal Maxwell read it, said the plot thickened, and sent me back up to destroy the general. I was going anyway, but I let him think it was his idea."
L["On the way up to the Spire, a quartermaster was carrying a letter from Rend Blackhand, mostly insults, saying only those with the Mark of Drakkisath could use the Orb of Command into Blackwing Lair, and the general guards the brand himself. With the general past guarding anything, I pressed my hand to the smoldering brand. I didn't flinch, much."] = "On the way up to the Spire, a quartermaster was carrying a letter from Rend Blackhand, mostly insults, saying only those with the Mark of Drakkisath could use the Orb of Command into Blackwing Lair, and the general guards the brand himself. With the general past guarding anything, I pressed my hand to the smoldering brand. I didn't flinch, much."
L["Helendis Riverhorn at the Vigil had noticed that killing worgs never left fewer worgs, and sent me into the Spire to find out why. The why was Halycon, their gigantic den mother, and I put her down. Helendis told me not to dwell on her suffering, which I hadn't planned to."] = "Helendis Riverhorn at the Vigil had noticed that killing worgs never left fewer worgs, and sent me into the Spire to find out why. The why was Halycon, their gigantic den mother, and I put her down. Helendis told me not to dwell on her suffering, which I hadn't planned to."
L["Mayara Brightwing hunts art for Count Remington Ridgewell's family museum and had found a piece in the Spire: Doomrigger's Clasp, a jeweled relic said to make dwarves weep. I dug it out of the old Hall of Fortune and took it to the count in a crate. His gratitude, I was told, is nigh worth a king's ransom, and nigh is doing a lot of work there."] = "Mayara Brightwing hunts art for Count Remington Ridgewell's family museum and had found a piece in the Spire: Doomrigger's Clasp, a jeweled relic said to make dwarves weep. I dug it out of the old Hall of Fortune and took it to the count in a crate. His gratitude, I was told, is nigh worth a king's ransom, and nigh is doing a lot of work there."
L["Vaelan, in the lower Spire, wanted a gemstone from each of three generals and an old seal to set them in. Forging it took black dragonfire, so I wore Emberstrife down in the Wyrmbog and borrowed his mind just long enough to make him breathe on it. That seal is the key to the upper Spire, and not many keys get made that way."] = "Vaelan, in the lower Spire, wanted a gemstone from each of three generals and an old seal to set them in. Forging it took black dragonfire, so I wore Emberstrife down in the Wyrmbog and borrowed his mind just long enough to make him breathe on it. That seal is the key to the upper Spire, and not many keys get made that way."
L["Tinkee Steamboil at Flame Crest had built a gadget for freezing black dragon eggs solid and needed someone to try it in the Rookery atop the Spire. It worked, so I went back up and collected eight. Freeze them first, Tinkee said, or they might hatch before you get them, which is advice you only need once."] = "Tinkee Steamboil at Flame Crest had built a gadget for freezing black dragon eggs solid and needed someone to try it in the Rookery atop the Spire. It worked, so I went back up and collected eight. Freeze them first, Tinkee said, or they might hatch before you get them, which is advice you only need once."
L["Kibler at Flame Crest tames exotic beasts for rich clients, and wanted a Bloodaxe worg pup out of the Spire before it grew too old to train. I carried one back in a cage, and Kibler gave me a tame one of my own. It is very ferocious and about the size of a boot."] = "Kibler at Flame Crest tames exotic beasts for rich clients, and wanted a Bloodaxe worg pup out of the Spire before it grew too old to train. I carried one back in a cage, and Kibler gave me a tame one of my own. It is very ferocious and about the size of a boot."
L["Kibler's helper had gone into the Spire for spider eggs weeks before and still wasn't back, so I fetched fifteen myself. Some people, Kibler says, will pay good gold for the most vile of domesticated beasts. I got one free, a little Smolderweb spider, along with a warning not to get bitten."] = "Kibler's helper had gone into the Spire for spider eggs weeks before and still wasn't back, so I fetched fifteen myself. Some people, Kibler says, will pay good gold for the most vile of domesticated beasts. I got one free, a little Smolderweb spider, along with a warning not to get bitten."
L["Ragged John wanted Mother Smolderweb's venom, and not in a jar: he wanted it live, in my veins. So I let the biggest spider in the Spire bite me, walked back feeling awful, and he milked it out of me for the best ale he'd ever brewed. You thought I wanted it for poison, he said, crazy kids."] = "Ragged John wanted Mother Smolderweb's venom, and not in a jar: he wanted it live, in my veins. So I let the biggest spider in the Spire bite me, walked back feeling awful, and he milked it out of me for the best ale he'd ever brewed. You thought I wanted it for poison, he said, crazy kids."
L["Urok Doomhowl had cursed Warosh mute, so all Warosh could do was hand me a scroll that came down to: get my mojo. I got the mojo, and with a voice again Warosh told me I was a fool to think I'd reach the top of the Spire, but that my bravery was beyond question. I've had warmer thanks, and worse."] = "Urok Doomhowl had cursed Warosh mute, so all Warosh could do was hand me a scroll that came down to: get my mojo. I got the mojo, and with a voice again Warosh told me I was a fool to think I'd reach the top of the Spire, but that my bravery was beyond question. I've had warmer thanks, and worse."
L["Deep in the Spire, Awbee gave me a scale and sent me to Winterspring, where you stand on a cobalt rune in the caves of Mazthoril and end up in front of Haleh. Haleh scried what Awbee had seen in that doomed place. Dragons, I learned, are forbidden to meddle in mortal affairs, unless one of their own starts it."] = "Deep in the Spire, Awbee gave me a scale and sent me to Winterspring, where you stand on a cobalt rune in the caves of Mazthoril and end up in front of Haleh. Haleh scried what Awbee had seen in that doomed place. Dragons, I learned, are forbidden to meddle in mortal affairs, unless one of their own starts it."
L["We skinned the Beast in the upper Spire, and out climbed a gnome named Pip Quickwit, in a suit, delighted with how the suit had held up. Pip sent me to Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook with the news and a glowing lump of the Beast's insides. Malyfous asked if Pip was alive, if the suit worked, and then mostly about the lump."] = "We skinned the Beast in the upper Spire, and out climbed a gnome named Pip Quickwit, in a suit, delighted with how the suit had held up. Pip sent me to Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook with the news and a glowing lump of the Beast's insides. Malyfous asked if Pip was alive, if the suit worked, and then mostly about the lump."
L["Lorax, out in the snows of Winterspring, had bought the soul of a Spire smith named Goraluk Anvilcrack and sent me to collect it with a fel-soaked pike. Goraluk died, the pike drank him up, and I brought back the breastplate he'd stolen too. Lorax thanked me in rhyme, which somehow made it worse."] = "Lorax, out in the snows of Winterspring, had bought the soul of a Spire smith named Goraluk Anvilcrack and sent me to collect it with a fel-soaked pike. Goraluk died, the pike drank him up, and I brought back the breastplate he'd stolen too. Lorax thanked me in rhyme, which somehow made it worse."
L["Warlord Goretooth was recruiting in Kargath for the Expeditionary Force and wanted the Horde's best, with a speech to match. The cowards were invited to leave. I stayed, and got a grin and my orders, which from Goretooth is about as warm as it gets."] = "Warlord Goretooth was recruiting in Kargath for the Expeditionary Force and wanted the Horde's best, with a speech to match. The cowards were invited to leave. I stayed, and got a grin and my orders, which from Goretooth is about as warm as it gets."
L["Grandmaster Lexlort in Kargath warned me never to trust a goblin, then sent me into the Spire to bring one back: Bijou, an operative who'd been spending Horde gold on side jobs. Bijou had lost her spy gear fleeing an alarm, so I found it, and the reports came back to Kargath without her. Lexlort had to hand it to her: weaseled out again."] = "Grandmaster Lexlort in Kargath warned me never to trust a goblin, then sent me into the Spire to bring one back: Bijou, an operative who'd been spending Horde gold on side jobs. Bijou had lost her spy gear fleeing an alarm, so I found it, and the reports came back to Kargath without her. Lexlort had to hand it to her: weaseled out again."
L["Galamav the Marksman in Kargath said the Blackrock worgs were no demons, just the brood of Halycon and her mate, so I went into the Spire and killed Halycon. Galamav asked whether I'd survived the rabid pups and Gizrul the Slavener too. I was standing right there, so I let the question answer itself."] = "Galamav the Marksman in Kargath said the Blackrock worgs were no demons, just the brood of Halycon and her mate, so I went into the Spire and killed Halycon. Galamav asked whether I'd survived the rabid pups and Gizrul the Slavener too. I was standing right there, so I let the question answer itself."
L["Word came from the Undercity that Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath wanted a tablet out of the Spire. Urheld Darkstone, a dwarven alchemist thought mad in his day, had carved his formulae into stone rather than share them, and I found one in what was once the Hall of Fortune. Mad or not, the man kept good notes."] = "Word came from the Undercity that Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath wanted a tablet out of the Spire. Urheld Darkstone, a dwarven alchemist thought mad in his day, had carved his formulae into stone rather than share them, and I found one in what was once the Hall of Fortune. Mad or not, the man kept good notes."
L["Franclorn Forgewright, the architect of the Dark Iron city, only appears to the dead, so the first thing I had to do was die. Franclorn's hammer, Ironfel, was in the hands of Fineous Darkvire. I took it back and laid it in the hands of Franclorn's statue, and a little door in the base opened on the key to the city."] = "Franclorn Forgewright, the architect of the Dark Iron city, only appears to the dead, so the first thing I had to do was die. Franclorn's hammer, Ironfel, was in the hands of Fineous Darkvire. I took it back and laid it in the hands of Franclorn's statue, and a little door in the base opened on the key to the city."
L["Cyrus Therepentous, out in the Burning Steppes, wanted to taste the fire of Blackrock. Not a request I get often. The fire was Bael'Gar, a giant of pure flame down in the depths. Once Bael'Gar was dead, a scrap of altered dragon molt drew out the essence. Cyrus snatched it from me and told me to take my reward and get out of sight."] = "Cyrus Therepentous, out in the Burning Steppes, wanted to taste the fire of Blackrock. Not a request I get often. The fire was Bael'Gar, a giant of pure flame down in the depths. Once Bael'Gar was dead, a scrap of altered dragon molt drew out the essence. Cyrus snatched it from me and told me to take my reward and get out of sight."
L["Yuka Screwspigot at Flame Crest had a relative to collect: Ribbly, who'd spent the family's money on one scheme after another and was hiding in Blackrock Depths. Booty Bay had put a bounty on Ribbly, and the family was delighted. Ribbly was finally worth something. Yuka wanted Ribbly back alive, if possible. It wasn't."] = "Yuka Screwspigot at Flame Crest had a relative to collect: Ribbly, who'd spent the family's money on one scheme after another and was hiding in Blackrock Depths. Booty Bay had put a bounty on Ribbly, and the family was delighted. Ribbly was finally worth something. Yuka wanted Ribbly back alive, if possible. It wasn't."
L["Maxwort Uberglint at Flame Crest had wanted the Heart of the Mountain for years, a gem the size of your fist, and the Dark Irons wouldn't sell. So I let myself into their vault. You open every coffer in the place before the safe's watchman turns up, and then the watchman has to go. Maxwort was delighted. The Dark Irons, less so."] = "Maxwort Uberglint at Flame Crest had wanted the Heart of the Mountain for years, a gem the size of your fist, and the Dark Irons wouldn't sell. So I let myself into their vault. You open every coffer in the place before the safe's watchman turns up, and then the watchman has to go. Maxwort was delighted. The Dark Irons, less so."
L["Jalinda Sprig at Morgan's Vigil couldn't get a team into the mountain while Lord Incendius kept raising Overmaster Pyron from the ashes. So Incendius had to go. When I reported that Incendius had said the name Ragnaros, Jalinda asked if I was sure, patted my wrist and drifted off into deep thought. I was sure. I'd rather not have been."] = "Jalinda Sprig at Morgan's Vigil couldn't get a team into the mountain while Lord Incendius kept raising Overmaster Pyron from the ashes. So Incendius had to go. When I reported that Incendius had said the name Ragnaros, Jalinda asked if I was sure, patted my wrist and drifted off into deep thought. I was sure. I'd rather not have been."
L["Oralius at Morgan's Vigil talks like a pirate and was convinced the Dark Irons kept the good stuff in their fanny packs. I brought back twenty. Oralius sniffed through the pile, very happy with the goodies, and let me keep one. I'm still not sure what the good stuff was. I'm not sure I want to know."] = "Oralius at Morgan's Vigil talks like a pirate and was convinced the Dark Irons kept the good stuff in their fanny packs. I brought back twenty. Oralius sniffed through the pile, very happy with the goodies, and let me keep one. I'm still not sure what the good stuff was. I'm not sure I want to know."
L["Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos had a grievance: the Dark Irons had stolen the family lager recipe. Ragnar wanted every keg of it in Blackrock Depths smashed and the recipe brought home, and called the thieves villains who didn't deserve such a fine brew. Hurley Blackbreath, who had it, disagreed. Briefly. Part of my pay was lager."] = "Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos had a grievance: the Dark Irons had stolen the family lager recipe. Ragnar wanted every keg of it in Blackrock Depths smashed and the recipe brought home, and called the thieves villains who didn't deserve such a fine brew. Hurley Blackbreath, who had it, disagreed. Briefly. Part of my pay was lager."
L["Mistress Nagmara, a succubus working the Grim Guzzler, had one customer immune to her charms: Private Rocknot. So she wanted a love potion, and I did the shopping. Gromsblood, silver veins out of the cliff giants of Azshara, and spring water from Un'Goro. Last I saw, Nagmara was mixing it and Rocknot was still drinking. Poor Rocknot."] = "Mistress Nagmara, a succubus working the Grim Guzzler, had one customer immune to her charms: Private Rocknot. So she wanted a love potion, and I did the shopping. Gromsblood, silver veins out of the cliff giants of Azshara, and spring water from Un'Goro. Last I saw, Nagmara was mixing it and Rocknot was still drinking. Poor Rocknot."
L["Somewhere in the depths there's a chalice floating in the air, and it takes offerings: two star rubies, twenty gold bars and ten of truesilver. They made no sound going in. For that, Gloom'rel agreed to teach me to smelt dark iron. Easily the most expensive lesson I've ever taken."] = "Somewhere in the depths there's a chalice floating in the air, and it takes offerings: two star rubies, twenty gold bars and ten of truesilver. They made no sound going in. For that, Gloom'rel agreed to teach me to smelt dark iron. Easily the most expensive lesson I've ever taken."
L["Lokhtos Darkbargainer sells the Thorium Brotherhood's secrets out of the Grim Guzzler, and everything comes with a contract. Mine had me swear my sulfuron ingot was genuine and not a facsimile, and that TB Ltd. was not responsible for anything that happened if I went looking for Sulfuras. I signed. I got hammer plans and a cheerful good luck."] = "Lokhtos Darkbargainer sells the Thorium Brotherhood's secrets out of the Grim Guzzler, and everything comes with a contract. Mine had me swear my sulfuron ingot was genuine and not a facsimile, and that TB Ltd. was not responsible for anything that happened if I went looking for Sulfuras. I signed. I got hammer plans and a cheerful good luck."
L["Kargath has its own way of hiring: a poster that says KILL ON SIGHT. The first one listed the Dark Iron rank and file, guardsmen, wardens and footmen. Once Warlord Goretooth had counted those, a second poster went up for the medics, soldiers and officers. I appreciate an employer who puts it in writing."] = "Kargath has its own way of hiring: a poster that says KILL ON SIGHT. The first one listed the Dark Iron rank and file, guardsmen, wardens and footmen. Once Warlord Goretooth had counted those, a second poster went up for the medics, soldiers and officers. I appreciate an employer who puts it in writing."
L["Lexlort in Kargath wanted a traitor, Grark Lorkrub, who'd been feeding our plans to the Blackrock orcs. I shackled Grark in a Blackrock fortress and walked him out through the mountain, hearing all the way that I'd never make it. I made it. Then Warlord Goretooth sent me after General Angerforge, who'd planned the slaughter of the 109th. Also done."] = "Lexlort in Kargath wanted a traitor, Grark Lorkrub, who'd been feeding our plans to the Blackrock orcs. I shackled Grark in a Blackrock fortress and walked him out through the mountain, hearing all the way that I'd never make it. I made it. Then Warlord Goretooth sent me after General Angerforge, who'd planned the slaughter of the 109th. Also done."
L["Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath wanted a lager recipe the Dark Irons had stolen from some dwarven brewers. The ale is said to make the drinker stronger and braver, and the Forsaken would like to know how. I fetched it, and off it went to the Apothecarium for study. It's the first time I've felt sorry for a beer."] = "Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath wanted a lager recipe the Dark Irons had stolen from some dwarven brewers. The ale is said to make the drinker stronger and braver, and the Forsaken would like to know how. I fetched it, and off it went to the Apothecarium for study. It's the first time I've felt sorry for a beer."
L["The Dark Irons' golems run on something special, and Vivian Lagrave wanted ten essences of it for some Forsaken abominations. Turn the city upside down if you must, I was told. I started with the golems and the dwarves who build them, and never needed to turn anything else over."] = "The Dark Irons' golems run on something special, and Vivian Lagrave wanted ten essences of it for some Forsaken abominations. Turn the city upside down if you must, I was told. I started with the golems and the dwarves who build them, and never needed to turn anything else over."
L["Thunderheart in Kargath felt something foul seeping out of Blackrock Mountain, and wanted Lord Incendius dead on the theory that the servant leads you to the master. Incendius died, and I brought back the Tablet of Kurniya. Thunderheart took it, said the name Ragnaros, and told Kargath to decide whether to stand or run. I've had warmer welcomes."] = "Thunderheart in Kargath felt something foul seeping out of Blackrock Mountain, and wanted Lord Incendius dead on the theory that the servant leads you to the master. Incendius died, and I brought back the Tablet of Kurniya. Thunderheart took it, said the name Ragnaros, and told Kargath to decide whether to stand or run. I've had warmer welcomes."
L["Lotwil Veriatus was sure Golem Lord Argelmach had died ten years ago, so new machines bearing Argelmach's marks had Lotwil rattled. I brought back Argelmach's head and ten elemental cores from the golems around him. The head was metal, a Dark Iron construct. Lotwil now expects another one, and frankly so do I."] = "Lotwil Veriatus was sure Golem Lord Argelmach had died ten years ago, so new machines bearing Argelmach's marks had Lotwil rattled. I brought back Argelmach's head and ten elemental cores from the golems around him. The head was metal, a Dark Iron construct. Lotwil now expects another one, and frankly so do I."
L["Alaana Stormwalker near Thunder Bluff had word that the wall between our world and the Firelands had cracked somewhere under Blackrock Mountain, and that giants of molten rock were walking through. Alaana called that thrilling and terrifying and wanted a piece of one to study. I brought back a fragment. I'd have gone with terrifying."] = "Alaana Stormwalker near Thunder Bluff had word that the wall between our world and the Firelands had cracked somewhere under Blackrock Mountain, and that giants of molten rock were walking through. Alaana called that thrilling and terrifying and wanted a piece of one to study. I brought back a fragment. I'd have gone with terrifying."
L["Betina Bigglezink at Light's Hope has studied the plague for years and thinks the rest of us don't worry enough. Twenty samples of fresh plagued flesh said the plague had changed, so it was back into Stratholme to search the ziggurats for Scourge data. Betina called it astonishing and months of work, which to a scientist is good news."] = "Betina Bigglezink at Light's Hope has studied the plague for years and thinks the rest of us don't worry enough. Twenty samples of fresh plagued flesh said the plague had changed, so it was back into Stratholme to search the ziggurats for Scourge data. Betina called it astonishing and months of work, which to a scientist is good news."
L["Smokey LaRue at Light's Hope hadn't had a decent smoke since Stratholme fell, and said so, often. The tobacconist there had vowed to burn every leaf before the Scourge got any, and missed a box. Smokey got the stogies back, and I got Smokey's lighter, which seemed fair."] = "Smokey LaRue at Light's Hope hadn't had a decent smoke since Stratholme fell, and said so, often. The tobacconist there had vowed to burn every leaf before the Scourge got any, and missed a box. Smokey got the stogies back, and I got Smokey's lighter, which seemed fair."
L["Leonid Barthalomew the Revered calls undeath an illness, Leonid's own included, and gets on with the work regardless. The work this time was the Argent Dawn's spare holy water, sitting in supply crates in Stratholme. The Scourge won't touch holy water, but the vermin in those crates hadn't heard."] = "Leonid Barthalomew the Revered calls undeath an illness, Leonid's own included, and gets on with the work regardless. The work this time was the Argent Dawn's spare holy water, sitting in supply crates in Stratholme. The Scourge won't touch holy water, but the vermin in those crates hadn't heard."
L["Egan lives out in Terrordale on hatred of the Scourge, and handed me a blaster for the ghosts in Stratholme's streets. Blast a ghost and the soul steps out of it, blast it again and it's free. After fifteen of those, Egan asked whether I'd seen his mother."] = "Egan lives out in Terrordale on hatred of the Scourge, and handed me a blaster for the ghosts in Stratholme's streets. Blast a ghost and the soul steps out of it, blast it again and it's free. After fifteen of those, Egan asked whether I'd seen his mother."
L["Nathanos Blightcaller has a grudge with a face on it: Ramstein the Gorger stood over him when he died defending his own farm, and he hunted it across the wastes until it hid in Stratholme. I brought him the head. He spat and said it was going on his wall."] = "Nathanos Blightcaller has a grudge with a face on it: Ramstein the Gorger stood over him when he died defending his own farm, and he hunted it across the wastes until it hid in Stratholme. I brought him the head. He spat and said it was going on his wall."
L["Aurius was holed up in a Stratholme chapel, the only thing keeping him from turning death knight. With the Medallion of Faith back from a Scarlet zealot he could leave, and he went straight for Baron Rivendare. He was dying when it was over, but he said his soul was saved, and seemed to think that the better bargain."] = "Aurius was holed up in a Stratholme chapel, the only thing keeping him from turning death knight. With the Medallion of Faith back from a Scarlet zealot he could leave, and he went straight for Baron Rivendare. He was dying when it was over, but he said his soul was saved, and seemed to think that the better bargain."
L["Leonid Barthalomew sent me over to Betina Bigglezink with some frozen eggs, and Betina sent me back into Scholomance with something called Dawn's Gambit, to set down in the Viewing Room. A gambit, as I understand it, means giving up a piece to win the game. I made sure the piece was Vectus."] = "Leonid Barthalomew sent me over to Betina Bigglezink with some frozen eggs, and Betina sent me back into Scholomance with something called Dawn's Gambit, to set down in the Viewing Room. A gambit, as I understand it, means giving up a piece to win the game. I made sure the piece was Vectus."
L["Betina Bigglezink at Light's Hope wanted twenty plagued dragon hatchlings put down in Scholomance. Somewhere in all that plague I found one healthy dragon scale, and brought that back too. I don't know what Betina wanted it for. In Scholomance, anything healthy is worth a second look."] = "Betina Bigglezink at Light's Hope wanted twenty plagued dragon hatchlings put down in Scholomance. Somewhere in all that plague I found one healthy dragon scale, and brought that back too. I don't know what Betina wanted it for. In Scholomance, anything healthy is worth a second look."
L["Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan had lost a prospector named Agmond, whose last report mentioned carved stone urns at the dig outside Uldaman, and Ironband suspected the urns were what had stirred up the troggs. I brought back four. The troggs did seem to feel strongly about them."] = "Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan had lost a prospector named Agmond, whose last report mentioned carved stone urns at the dig outside Uldaman, and Ironband suspected the urns were what had stirred up the troggs. I brought back four. The troggs did seem to feel strongly about them."
L["When the troggs overran Uldaman, Krom Stoutarm left his greatest treasure behind in a chest at the end of the North Common Hall. I fought my way to it and carried it home to Ironforge, and it was a beer stein. A Stoutarm without a stein, Krom explained with feeling, is hardly a Stoutarm at all."] = "When the troggs overran Uldaman, Krom Stoutarm left his greatest treasure behind in a chest at the end of the North Common Hall. I fought my way to it and carried it home to Ironforge, and it was a beer stein. A Stoutarm without a stein, Krom explained with feeling, is hardly a Stoutarm at all."
L["Prospector Stormpike of the Explorers' League sent me after Baelog, whose band had gone into Uldaman and got stuck there. Baelog couldn't go anywhere, but his journal told me how to open a hidden chamber behind a huge locked door, and the chamber was real. Stormpike admitted to having had doubts, which Baelog never had."] = "Prospector Stormpike of the Explorers' League sent me after Baelog, whose band had gone into Uldaman and got stuck there. Baelog couldn't go anywhere, but his journal told me how to open a hidden chamber behind a huge locked door, and the chamber was real. Stormpike admitted to having had doubts, which Baelog never had."
L["In the end Talvash del Kissel let me keep the necklace, on two conditions: that I tell everyone, loudly and often, who made it, and that I mention it really isn't cursed. Talvash made it, and it isn't cursed, as far as I know."] = "In the end Talvash del Kissel let me keep the necklace, on two conditions: that I tell everyone, loudly and often, who made it, and that I mention it really isn't cursed. Talvash made it, and it isn't cursed, as far as I know."
L["Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar sent me into the Badlands with a shopping list: buzzard gizzards, crag coyote fangs and shards from the rock elementals. The buzzards and the coyotes gave theirs up easily enough. The elementals argued the point. Ghak went over every piece, decided I could be trusted with reagents, and had a harder errand ready before I'd sat down."] = "Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar sent me into the Badlands with a shopping list: buzzard gizzards, crag coyote fangs and shards from the rock elementals. The buzzards and the coyotes gave theirs up easily enough. The elementals argued the point. Ghak went over every piece, decided I could be trusted with reagents, and had a harder errand ready before I'd sat down."
L["Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath wanted reagents from the Badlands outside the walls: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs and five shards of rock elemental. Out there everything bites, so I collected from whatever bit first. Jarkal counted it all twice and said the ingredient that really mattered was down in Uldaman."] = "Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath wanted reagents from the Badlands outside the walls: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs and five shards of rock elemental. Out there everything bites, so I collected from whatever bit first. Jarkal counted it all twice and said the ingredient that really mattered was down in Uldaman."
L["Ghak Healtouch, the alchemist in Thelsamar, wanted a dozen magenta fungus caps from the Uldaman tunnels, with a warning that they puff poison spores when jostled. They do. Ghak paid me with a restorative potion and called the caps an interesting study, yon verily, and I still don't know what yon verily means."] = "Ghak Healtouch, the alchemist in Thelsamar, wanted a dozen magenta fungus caps from the Uldaman tunnels, with a warning that they puff poison spores when jostled. They do. Ghak paid me with a restorative potion and called the caps an interesting study, yon verily, and I still don't know what yon verily means."
L["Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath wanted a dozen magenta fungus caps out of the Uldaman tunnels, which let off poison spores if you disturb them, so a little care was called for. I took a little care and a lot of poison. Jarkal paid me with a restorative potion, which was exactly the right reward."] = "Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath wanted a dozen magenta fungus caps out of the Uldaman tunnels, which let off poison spores if you disturb them, so a little care was called for. I took a little care and a lot of poison. Jarkal paid me with a restorative potion, which was exactly the right reward."
L["Patrick Garrett swept the bat pens in the Undercity and felt it was beneath a Garrett. The family weapon was still in their old chest in Uldaman's South Common Hall, from back when the Garretts dug there. I brought it back, and Patrick turned straight to the bats and told them to tremble, which they didn't."] = "Patrick Garrett swept the bat pens in the Undercity and felt it was beneath a Garrett. The family weapon was still in their old chest in Uldaman's South Common Hall, from back when the Garretts dug there. I brought it back, and Patrick turned straight to the bats and told them to tremble, which they didn't."
L["Odd Jobs in the Badlands"] = "Odd Jobs in the Badlands"
L["Theldurin's Doom"] = "Theldurin's Doom"
L["Plenty of people want something out of the Badlands or Uldaman, and few of them want to fetch it themselves. Prospector Ironband has lost a prospector, Krom Stoutarm a treasure, Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar needs reagents, and a tinkerer called Rigglefuzz is after power stones. None of it is urgent. All of it pays."] = "Plenty of people want something out of the Badlands or Uldaman, and few of them want to fetch it themselves. Prospector Ironband has lost a prospector, Krom Stoutarm a treasure, Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar needs reagents, and a tinkerer called Rigglefuzz is after power stones. None of it is urgent. All of it pays."
L["Plenty of people want something out of the Badlands or Uldaman, and few of them want to fetch it themselves. Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath needs reagents, Patrick Garrett in the Undercity wants the family weapon back, and a tinkerer called Rigglefuzz is after power stones. None of it is urgent. All of it pays."] = "Plenty of people want something out of the Badlands or Uldaman, and few of them want to fetch it themselves. Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath needs reagents, Patrick Garrett in the Undercity wants the family weapon back, and a tinkerer called Rigglefuzz is after power stones. None of it is urgent. All of it pays."
L["Between the big jobs, the Badlands kept me busy with small ones. Everybody out there wanted something fetched, found or carried home from Uldaman, and nobody wanted to go down and get it themselves. So I did."] = "Between the big jobs, the Badlands kept me busy with small ones. Everybody out there wanted something fetched, found or carried home from Uldaman, and nobody wanted to go down and get it themselves. So I did."
L["Out in the Badlands, Theldurin the Lost is sure a doom is coming. He won't say its name in case it hears him, but he knows what he needs to stop it, and it's somewhere down in Uldaman."] = "Out in the Badlands, Theldurin the Lost is sure a doom is coming. He won't say its name in case it hears him, but he knows what he needs to stop it, and it's somewhere down in Uldaman."
L["Theldurin the Lost, a jumpy dwarf out in the Badlands, was sure a doom was coming and wouldn't say its name in case it heard him. He needed the Tablet of Ryun'eh, from a chest in Uldaman older than anything dwarves ever made. I brought it, and he said it might hold the secret to saving us all, though he still wouldn't say from what.\n\nThe tablet from Uldaman told Theldurin a lot, but not enough. He wanted Yagyin's Digest, a book kept by the very people he'd fled, and he gave me their sigil so they would take me for one of their own.\n\nThey did. Their contact in the city decided I was off to found a new chapter of their order and was glad to help, once I'd brought him three relics he wouldn't say out loud. He wrote them down instead. I brought them.\n\nThe book came with a warning that the truth can burn. Theldurin said they should build me a monument and praise my name until my grandchildren had grandchildren. Then he added that if THEY ever get loose, I can forget the grandchildren. We're all worm food."] = "Theldurin the Lost, a jumpy dwarf out in the Badlands, was sure a doom was coming and wouldn't say its name in case it heard him. He needed the Tablet of Ryun'eh, from a chest in Uldaman older than anything dwarves ever made. I brought it, and he said it might hold the secret to saving us all, though he still wouldn't say from what.\n\nThe tablet from Uldaman told Theldurin a lot, but not enough. He wanted Yagyin's Digest, a book kept by the very people he'd fled, and he gave me their sigil so they would take me for one of their own.\n\nThey did. Their contact in the city decided I was off to found a new chapter of their order and was glad to help, once I'd brought him three relics he wouldn't say out loud. He wrote them down instead. I brought them.\n\nThe book came with a warning that the truth can burn. Theldurin said they should build me a monument and praise my name until my grandchildren had grandchildren. Then he added that if THEY ever get loose, I can forget the grandchildren. We're all worm food."
L["Rigglefuzz, a tinkerer in the Badlands, had once shown the Shadowforge dwarves how to use the power stones they dig out of Uldaman, and was thanked by being thrown out. Now Rigglefuzz wanted sixteen of them, to run a robotic rodent forever. The Shadowforge were no better at sharing the second time."] = "Rigglefuzz, a tinkerer in the Badlands, had once shown the Shadowforge dwarves how to use the power stones they dig out of Uldaman, and was thanked by being thrown out. Now Rigglefuzz wanted sixteen of them, to run a robotic rodent forever. The Shadowforge were no better at sharing the second time."
L["A Bit of Wet Work"] = "A Bit of Wet Work"
L["Sully had been watching Alcaz through his looking glass and saw naga coming ashore, led by a sorceress barking orders. He asked me to thin them out while I was in there and bring back her head. I did both. As Sully put it, the enemy of your enemy is still a naga."] = "Sully had been watching Alcaz through his looking glass and saw naga coming ashore, led by a sorceress barking orders. He asked me to thin them out while I was in there and bring back her head. I did both. As Sully put it, the enemy of your enemy is still a naga."
L["The Dragon's Journal"] = "The Dragon's Journal"
L["Archmage Lan'dalock had been scrying Alcaz Island from Dalaran until someone on the island noticed and shut the spell down. Just before that, it caught a journal written in old draconic, and Lan'dalock wanted it. I found it. I can't read a word of draconic, so I'm taking the archmage's word that it was worth the trip."] = "Archmage Lan'dalock had been scrying Alcaz Island from Dalaran until someone on the island noticed and shut the spell down. Just before that, it caught a journal written in old draconic, and Lan'dalock wanted it. I found it. I can't read a word of draconic, so I'm taking the archmage's word that it was worth the trip."
L["A Little Payback"] = "A Little Payback"
L["Sergeant Ulka had lost good orcs on Alcaz and wanted it squared, naga for orc, starting with the sorceress giving the orders. I came back with her head and a long list of naga who wouldn't be needing theirs. Ulka didn't smile, exactly. From the Kor'kron, that's practically a hug."] = "Sergeant Ulka had lost good orcs on Alcaz and wanted it squared, naga for orc, starting with the sorceress giving the orders. I came back with her head and a long list of naga who wouldn't be needing theirs. Ulka didn't smile, exactly. From the Kor'kron, that's practically a hug."
L["Blood Red Bandanas"] = "Blood Red Bandanas"
L["Ulka's people had been fighting humans in red bandanas on Alcaz, which put Ulka in mind of a gang from the Eastern Kingdoms. I collected the bandanas and carried them to Eitrigg in Orgrimmar. Eitrigg confirmed it: Defias, a very long way from Westfall. Nobody could tell me what they were doing there."] = "Ulka's people had been fighting humans in red bandanas on Alcaz, which put Ulka in mind of a gang from the Eastern Kingdoms. I collected the bandanas and carried them to Eitrigg in Orgrimmar. Eitrigg confirmed it: Defias, a very long way from Westfall. Nobody could tell me what they were doing there."
L["Krol'dok No More!"] = "Krol'dok No More!"
L["Marcus Tilwell"] = "Marcus Tilwell"
L["Somewhere in Krol'dok I found Marcus Tilwell, who wouldn't explain how any of it had happened and only wanted out. So we left together, me in front. Apparently I wouldn't believe the story anyway. Having seen the place, I'd believe almost anything."] = "Somewhere in Krol'dok I found Marcus Tilwell, who wouldn't explain how any of it had happened and only wanted out. So we left together, me in front. Apparently I wouldn't believe the story anyway. Having seen the place, I'd believe almost anything."
L["Magus Olvek"] = "Magus Olvek"
L["Past Due"] = "Past Due"
L["Magus Olvek in Dalaran needed a book for a thesis, and Arcanist Doan had borrowed it from the old Dalaran library before the Third War and never brought it back. Doan lives in the Scarlet Monastery now, so I collected it the hard way. Considering the late fees, Doan got off lightly."] = "Magus Olvek in Dalaran needed a book for a thesis, and Arcanist Doan had borrowed it from the old Dalaran library before the Third War and never brought it back. Doan lives in the Scarlet Monastery now, so I collected it the hard way. Considering the late fees, Doan got off lightly."
L["the gates of Stormwind, Elwynn Forest"] = "the gates of Stormwind, Elwynn Forest"
L["Major Mattingly"] = "Major Mattingly"
L["the Valley of Strength, Orgrimmar"] = "the Valley of Strength, Orgrimmar"
L["Overlord Runthak"] = "Overlord Runthak"
L["The Drakefire Amulet opens the way into Onyxia's Lair, in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Behind it waits the dragon who sat at Stormwind's court for years as Lady Prestor. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon would very much like a word with her, or failing that, her head."] = "The Drakefire Amulet opens the way into Onyxia's Lair, in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Behind it waits the dragon who sat at Stormwind's court for years as Lady Prestor. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon would very much like a word with her, or failing that, her head."
L["The Drakefire Amulet opens the way into Onyxia's Lair, in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Behind it waits the brood mother of the black dragonflight, Deathwing's own daughter. Thrall would like all of Orgrimmar to see how that meeting ends."] = "The Drakefire Amulet opens the way into Onyxia's Lair, in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Behind it waits the brood mother of the black dragonflight, Deathwing's own daughter. Thrall would like all of Orgrimmar to see how that meeting ends."
L["The amulet got us through the door of Onyxia's Lair, down in the south of Dustwallow Marsh, and after that it was up to us. Onyxia had spent years in Stormwind as Lady Prestor, at the king's table, steering the kingdom wherever she liked. In her own home she didn't bother with manners. There were whelps. There were a great many whelps.\n\nWe came out with her head, and I carried it to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep. Bolvar had it hung over the city gates, where everyone passing through could see what had been whispering to their king. The whole city stood a little straighter that day.\n\nMajor Mattingly at the gates had a reward for me afterwards, and a speech to go with it: the journey, he said, had only just begun. I've been walking ever since, so he may have had a point."] = "The amulet got us through the door of Onyxia's Lair, down in the south of Dustwallow Marsh, and after that it was up to us. Onyxia had spent years in Stormwind as Lady Prestor, at the king's table, steering the kingdom wherever she liked. In her own home she didn't bother with manners. There were whelps. There were a great many whelps.\n\nWe came out with her head, and I carried it to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep. Bolvar had it hung over the city gates, where everyone passing through could see what had been whispering to their king. The whole city stood a little straighter that day.\n\nMajor Mattingly at the gates had a reward for me afterwards, and a speech to go with it: the journey, he said, had only just begun. I've been walking ever since, so he may have had a point."
L["The amulet got us through the door of Onyxia's Lair, down in the south of Dustwallow Marsh, and after that it was up to us. Onyxia didn't greet us. She breathed on us, which is how dragons say hello. Then came the whelps, a great many whelps, as if she'd been saving them for company.\n\nWe came out with her head, and I carried it to Thrall in Orgrimmar. Thrall sent me on to Overlord Runthak, who had it raised over the Valley of Strength for all to see. Every orc in the city stood a little taller that day, and so did I.\n\nRunthak had a reward for me afterwards, and a speech to go with it: the journey, he said, had only just begun. Easy for him to say. He wasn't the one who carried the head."] = "The amulet got us through the door of Onyxia's Lair, down in the south of Dustwallow Marsh, and after that it was up to us. Onyxia didn't greet us. She breathed on us, which is how dragons say hello. Then came the whelps, a great many whelps, as if she'd been saving them for company.\n\nWe came out with her head, and I carried it to Thrall in Orgrimmar. Thrall sent me on to Overlord Runthak, who had it raised over the Valley of Strength for all to see. Every orc in the city stood a little taller that day, and so did I.\n\nRunthak had a reward for me afterwards, and a speech to go with it: the journey, he said, had only just begun. Easy for him to say. He wasn't the one who carried the head."
