L["Lorekeeper Lydros had said the blade wasn't finished until a dragon breathed on it, which is an odd way to temper steel and a very common way to die. So in the middle of all that, I laid Quel'Serrar on the floor of Onyxia's Lair and let her do the forging. Lydros was right. It came out of the fire a proper sword."] = "Lorekeeper Lydros had said the blade wasn't finished until a dragon breathed on it, which is an odd way to temper steel and a very common way to die. So in the middle of all that, I laid Quel'Serrar on the floor of Onyxia's Lair and let her do the forging. Lydros was right. It came out of the fire a proper sword."
L["Sprite Jumpsprocket"] = "Sprite Jumpsprocket"
L["Jasper Fel"] = "Jasper Fel"
L["Toxic Soil"] = "Toxic Soil"
L["Alba Fairmoon, at Sentinel Hill, says something is poisoning Westfall. The crops are failing, the wells taste of metal, and if nobody finds the source, nothing will grow there for decades. Alba has a sample kit and a great many questions."] = "Alba Fairmoon, at Sentinel Hill, says something is poisoning Westfall. The crops are failing, the wells taste of metal, and if nobody finds the source, nothing will grow there for decades. Alba has a sample kit and a great many questions."
L["Alba Fairmoon turned up at Sentinel Hill with a sample kit and a theory: something was poisoning Westfall. I drew water from the farm wells and pulled gills off the murlocs along the shore, because murlocs, it turns out, are very sensitive souls. The wells came back full of metal. Not the good kind.\n\nThe Defias held the mines, so I ran their miners out of the Jangolode and the Gold Coast Quarry. Wrong mines. The poison came from somewhere deeper, and the crates lying around Moonbrook said where: the Deadmines, busy again after all these years.\n\nAlba wanted it blown up. A gnome called Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District was thrilled to hear it, and SI:7 already knew all about it, which I found less thrilling. Jasper Fel handed me a remote detonator and asked me not to mention him to the elf. So I won't."] = "Alba Fairmoon turned up at Sentinel Hill with a sample kit and a theory: something was poisoning Westfall. I drew water from the farm wells and pulled gills off the murlocs along the shore, because murlocs, it turns out, are very sensitive souls. The wells came back full of metal. Not the good kind.\n\nThe Defias held the mines, so I ran their miners out of the Jangolode and the Gold Coast Quarry. Wrong mines. The poison came from somewhere deeper, and the crates lying around Moonbrook said where: the Deadmines, busy again after all these years.\n\nAlba wanted it blown up. A gnome called Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District was thrilled to hear it, and SI:7 already knew all about it, which I found less thrilling. Jasper Fel handed me a remote detonator and asked me not to mention him to the elf. So I won't."
