L["Barnil Stonepot greets visitors at Nesingwary's Expedition, in the north of Stranglethorn Vale. The camp belongs to Hemet Nesingwary, a famous big game hunter who doesn't usually welcome strangers. Barnil thinks you look like you've seen enough action to meet him."] = "Barnil Stonepot greets visitors at Nesingwary's Expedition, in the north of Stranglethorn Vale. The camp belongs to Hemet Nesingwary, a famous big game hunter who doesn't usually welcome strangers. Barnil thinks you look like you've seen enough action to meet him."
L["So there's a camp up in the north of Stranglethorn, and the first face you meet there is Barnil Stonepot. Barnil told me whose camp it was. Hemet Nesingwary's: war hero, big game hunter, not one for welcoming strangers. Then Barnil looked me over and decided I'd seen enough action to risk an introduction.\n\nHemet turned out friendlier than his reputation. He'd come to the jungle for a rare beast, he said, and I could join the hunt once I'd proved myself. Raptors with him. Tigers and panthers with two of his hunters.\n\nI'd come to Stranglethorn looking for paid work. I'd found three teachers and an exam."] = "So there's a camp up in the north of Stranglethorn, and the first face you meet there is Barnil Stonepot. Barnil told me whose camp it was. Hemet Nesingwary's: war hero, big game hunter, not one for welcoming strangers. Then Barnil looked me over and decided I'd seen enough action to risk an introduction.\n\nHemet turned out friendlier than his reputation. He'd come to the jungle for a rare beast, he said, and I could join the hunt once I'd proved myself. Raptors with him. Tigers and panthers with two of his hunters.\n\nI'd come to Stranglethorn looking for paid work. I'd found three teachers and an exam."
L["Kravel Koalbeard, at the Mirage Raceway, had a crate for an old customer who'd long since left for Stranglethorn. Hemet's a rich dwarf, Kravel explained, and it's a good idea to keep up with the rich ones. The crate held special-gauge ammunition. Hemet paid me, asked after crusty old Kravel, and answered the question himself: still up to no good, he'd wager."] = "Kravel Koalbeard, at the Mirage Raceway, had a crate for an old customer who'd long since left for Stranglethorn. Hemet's a rich dwarf, Kravel explained, and it's a good idea to keep up with the rich ones. The crate held special-gauge ammunition. Hemet paid me, asked after crusty old Kravel, and answered the question himself: still up to no good, he'd wager."
L["Roon Wildmane, in Shadowprey Village, once spent many days hunting Desolace with a dwarf named Hemet, long enough for the old enmity between their peoples to be forgotten. Roon sent me to Stranglethorn with a kodo horn. Hemet knew whose it was at a glance, and what it meant: come back and hunt again. His next expedition might take him to Desolace, he said. Hunters always say that about the next expedition."] = "Roon Wildmane, in Shadowprey Village, once spent many days hunting Desolace with a dwarf named Hemet, long enough for the old enmity between their peoples to be forgotten. Roon sent me to Stranglethorn with a kodo horn. Hemet knew whose it was at a glance, and what it meant: come back and hunt again. His next expedition might take him to Desolace, he said. Hunters always say that about the next expedition."
L["Hunting in Stranglethorn"] = "Hunting in Stranglethorn"
L["Tiger Mastery"] = "Tiger Mastery"
L["Ajeck Rouack, at Nesingwary's Expedition, learned tiger hunting from her father as a girl, and she teaches it the same way: start easy, on the young tigers near camp. It gets harder from there."] = "Ajeck Rouack, at Nesingwary's Expedition, learned tiger hunting from her father as a girl, and she teaches it the same way: start easy, on the young tigers near camp. It gets harder from there."
L["Ajeck Rouack learned to hunt tigers from her father when she was a girl, and she teaches it the way he must have: start small. The young ones live near camp. From there you work your way up the family tree, and the elders take it personally.\n\nThen the real lesson. The party had been tracking one tigress for weeks without getting near her. They called her Sin'Dall. Ajeck wanted her paw, and wanted me to do what nobody of my kind had done before.\n\nTracking her was no easy task, exactly as promised. But I came back with the paw, and Ajeck named me a Master Tiger Hunter. Most impressive, I do say, was how she put it.\n\nNo certificate, mind you. Just the title, and a paw nobody asked to have back."] = "Ajeck Rouack learned to hunt tigers from her father when she was a girl, and she teaches it the way he must have: start small. The young ones live near camp. From there you work your way up the family tree, and the elders take it personally.\n\nThen the real lesson. The party had been tracking one tigress for weeks without getting near her. They called her Sin'Dall. Ajeck wanted her paw, and wanted me to do what nobody of my kind had done before.\n\nTracking her was no easy task, exactly as promised. But I came back with the paw, and Ajeck named me a Master Tiger Hunter. Most impressive, I do say, was how she put it.\n\nNo certificate, mind you. Just the title, and a paw nobody asked to have back."
L["Young Tigers"] = "Young Tigers"
L["Stranglethorn Tigers"] = "Stranglethorn Tigers"
L["Elder Tigers"] = "Elder Tigers"
L["Sin'Dall"] = "Sin'Dall"
L["Panther Mastery"] = "Panther Mastery"
L["Sir S. J. Erlgadin, at Nesingwary's Expedition, won't let anyone into Hemet's crack hunting party who can't handle a panther. The lessons start easy, with the young ones. Tracking them down, the knight warns, is only half the challenge."] = "Sir S. J. Erlgadin, at Nesingwary's Expedition, won't let anyone into Hemet's crack hunting party who can't handle a panther. The lessons start easy, with the young ones. Tracking them down, the knight warns, is only half the challenge."
L["Sir S. J. Erlgadin handles the panthers, and in the knight's view Hemet has assembled a crack group, and nobody joins a crack group without proving it. So: panthers. They start you easy, on the young ones, and work you up to the shadowmaws.\n\nTracking them down is only half the challenge, Erlgadin says. I can tell you what the other half is. It's the panther.\n\nAt the top of the list sat Bhag'thera, a great panther who'd been prowling the jungle and slipping the whole expedition. His fang would earn me Erlgadin's respect. I spent a good while learning why everyone else had come home empty-handed. Then I didn't.\n\nErlgadin cheered and called me mighty. I've been living up to it ever since, mostly sitting down."] = "Sir S. J. Erlgadin handles the panthers, and in the knight's view Hemet has assembled a crack group, and nobody joins a crack group without proving it. So: panthers. They start you easy, on the young ones, and work you up to the shadowmaws.\n\nTracking them down is only half the challenge, Erlgadin says. I can tell you what the other half is. It's the panther.\n\nAt the top of the list sat Bhag'thera, a great panther who'd been prowling the jungle and slipping the whole expedition. His fang would earn me Erlgadin's respect. I spent a good while learning why everyone else had come home empty-handed. Then I didn't.\n\nErlgadin cheered and called me mighty. I've been living up to it ever since, mostly sitting down."
L["Young Panthers"] = "Young Panthers"
L["Panthers"] = "Panthers"
L["Shadowmaw Panthers"] = "Shadowmaw Panthers"
L["Bhag'thera"] = "Bhag'thera"
L["Raptor Mastery"] = "Raptor Mastery"
L["Hemet Nesingwary teaches the raptor lessons himself, at his camp in northern Stranglethorn. He'll tell you which raptors to hunt. He won't tell you where to find them. Locating the beasts, he says, is half the challenge."] = "Hemet Nesingwary teaches the raptor lessons himself, at his camp in northern Stranglethorn. He'll tell you which raptors to hunt. He won't tell you where to find them. Locating the beasts, he says, is half the challenge."
L["Hemet teaches raptors himself, and his first lesson is that he won't tell you where they are. Locating the beasts is half the challenge, he says. Raptors, in my experience, are happy to help with that half.\n\nThree breeds of raptor later, he told me about the one that kept getting away from him. Tethis, Ajeck calls him, a wily old raptor that even Hemet had failed to kill. Prove yourself a true master, Hemet said, and bring back the talon.\n\nTethis was elusive right up until the moment he wasn't. I'll leave it there.\n\nHemet took the talon and tried a title out on me: Master Raptor Slayer. Has a nice ring to it, eh? It does. I'd never once managed to work it into conversation. Until now."] = "Hemet teaches raptors himself, and his first lesson is that he won't tell you where they are. Locating the beasts is half the challenge, he says. Raptors, in my experience, are happy to help with that half.\n\nThree breeds of raptor later, he told me about the one that kept getting away from him. Tethis, Ajeck calls him, a wily old raptor that even Hemet had failed to kill. Prove yourself a true master, Hemet said, and bring back the talon.\n\nTethis was elusive right up until the moment he wasn't. I'll leave it there.\n\nHemet took the talon and tried a title out on me: Master Raptor Slayer. Has a nice ring to it, eh? It does. I'd never once managed to work it into conversation. Until now."
L["Stranglethorn Raptors"] = "Stranglethorn Raptors"
L["Lashtail Raptors"] = "Lashtail Raptors"
L["Jungle Stalkers"] = "Jungle Stalkers"
L["Tethis"] = "Tethis"
L["The Missing Pages"] = "The Missing Pages"
L["Barnil Stonepot, at Nesingwary's Expedition, was trusted to proofread Hemet's novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, right up until a gust of wind scattered it across the jungle. Barnil needs the missing pages back before Master Nesingwary finds out."] = "Barnil Stonepot, at Nesingwary's Expedition, was trusted to proofread Hemet's novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, right up until a gust of wind scattered it across the jungle. Barnil needs the missing pages back before Master Nesingwary finds out."
L["Barnil Stonepot was proofreading Hemet's novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, when a gust of wind went through camp and took the novel with it. Barnil got most of it back. The rest was out in the jungle, and Master Nesingwary, I was told firmly, must never find out.\n\nHere's what nobody tells you about collecting a book one page at a time. The pages don't share. A page only stacks with copies of itself, and I got copies of every page except the one I needed. For weeks I carried more of that novel than its author did. Somewhere in Booty Bay, someone is still asking for page fourteen.\n\nI read a few on the walk back. The sentences were short. The hunts were long. Somebody was always having a drink and being brave about it.\n\nBarnil says the ending is quite something. I'll take Barnil's word for it."] = "Barnil Stonepot was proofreading Hemet's novel, The Green Hills of Stranglethorn, when a gust of wind went through camp and took the novel with it. Barnil got most of it back. The rest was out in the jungle, and Master Nesingwary, I was told firmly, must never find out.\n\nHere's what nobody tells you about collecting a book one page at a time. The pages don't share. A page only stacks with copies of itself, and I got copies of every page except the one I needed. For weeks I carried more of that novel than its author did. Somewhere in Booty Bay, someone is still asking for page fourteen.\n\nI read a few on the walk back. The sentences were short. The hunts were long. Somebody was always having a drink and being brave about it.\n\nBarnil says the ending is quite something. I'll take Barnil's word for it."
L["Chapter I"] = "Chapter I"
L["Chapter II"] = "Chapter II"
L["Chapter III"] = "Chapter III"
L["Chapter IV"] = "Chapter IV"
L["King Bangalash"] = "King Bangalash"
L["You've proved yourself against the expedition's tigers, panthers and raptors, and Hemet Nesingwary is finally ready to tell you why he came to Stranglethorn: a great white tiger he has had in his sights for a long time."] = "You've proved yourself against the expedition's tigers, panthers and raptors, and Hemet Nesingwary is finally ready to tell you why he came to Stranglethorn: a great white tiger he has had in his sights for a long time."
L["With the tigers, the panthers and the raptors behind me, Hemet finally told me about the big hunt. King Bangalash, a great white tiger. Hemet had had his sights on that tiger for a long time. He was the reason the whole expedition was in Stranglethorn.\n\nI won't tell you where the king holds court. Locating the beast is half the challenge, as a dwarf once told me. I'll tell you he was well named, and that I came back with his head.\n\nHemet was delighted. Bloody well done, right-o, cheers, I say, cheers. He said he was honored to count me a comrade of his great hunting party, which is a thing I now get to say in taverns.\n\nIn the morning the sun also rose, over a jungle with one king fewer in it."] = "With the tigers, the panthers and the raptors behind me, Hemet finally told me about the big hunt. King Bangalash, a great white tiger. Hemet had had his sights on that tiger for a long time. He was the reason the whole expedition was in Stranglethorn.\n\nI won't tell you where the king holds court. Locating the beast is half the challenge, as a dwarf once told me. I'll tell you he was well named, and that I came back with his head.\n\nHemet was delighted. Bloody well done, right-o, cheers, I say, cheers. He said he was honored to count me a comrade of his great hunting party, which is a thing I now get to say in taverns.\n\nIn the morning the sun also rose, over a jungle with one king fewer in it."
L["Big Game Hunter"] = "Big Game Hunter"
L["Waking Naralex"] = "Waking Naralex"
L["Beneath the Barrens, in the Wailing Caverns, a druid named Naralex lies asleep. He went down to dream the dry land green again, and the dream went wrong. Strange beasts crawl out of the caves now, and the oases carry a taint nobody can name.\n\nFind his disciples above the caverns' entrance, and follow the trouble down into the dark to where the dreamer sleeps."] = "Beneath the Barrens, in the Wailing Caverns, a druid named Naralex lies asleep. He went down to dream the dry land green again, and the dream went wrong. Strange beasts crawl out of the caves now, and the oases carry a taint nobody can name.\n\nFind his disciples above the caverns' entrance, and follow the trouble down into the dark to where the dreamer sleeps."
L["Above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, in the Barrens, the disciples of a druid named Naralex keep a lonely watch. Their master went down to dream the dry land green again, and strange beasts have been crawling up out of the caves ever since.\n\nLend the disciples a hand, and follow the trouble down into the dark to where the dreamer sleeps."] = "Above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, in the Barrens, the disciples of a druid named Naralex keep a lonely watch. Their master went down to dream the dry land green again, and strange beasts have been crawling up out of the caves ever since.\n\nLend the disciples a hand, and follow the trouble down into the dark to where the dreamer sleeps."
L["New oases have sprung up across the Barrens, and the druids of Thunder Bluff can feel a strange power seeping up beneath them. Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, wants to know where it comes from.\n\nFollow the water down to the Wailing Caverns, where a druid named Naralex went to dream the Barrens green again and never came back up."] = "New oases have sprung up across the Barrens, and the druids of Thunder Bluff can feel a strange power seeping up beneath them. Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, wants to know where it comes from.\n\nFollow the water down to the Wailing Caverns, where a druid named Naralex went to dream the Barrens green again and never came back up."
