L["The Dreaming Oases"] = "The Dreaming Oases"
L["New oases have been springing up across the Barrens, and the druids can feel a strange power seeping up from beneath them. Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, wants someone to go and look into the water. Closely."] = "New oases have been springing up across the Barrens, and the druids can feel a strange power seeping up from beneath them. Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, wants someone to go and look into the water. Closely."
L["Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, had a problem most places would envy: the Barrens kept growing new oases. Tonga didn't trust it. The druids could feel some power seeping up from below, and a druid who feels something will not rest until somebody else has gone and poked it.\n\nI poked. There were cracks in the bottoms of the pools, with gas bubbling up out of them. Tonga gave me a handful of seeds, dead and dry, and had me drop them into the crack at the Stagnant Oasis. They grew. Right there, out of nothing.\n\nA few snapjaw shells later, Tonga had an answer and didn't like it. The land was dreaming and couldn't wake, and the dream was coming from the Wailing Caverns. Before I went anywhere near them, I was to see Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. Druids always want a second opinion."] = "Tonga Runetotem, at the Crossroads, had a problem most places would envy: the Barrens kept growing new oases. Tonga didn't trust it. The druids could feel some power seeping up from below, and a druid who feels something will not rest until somebody else has gone and poked it.\n\nI poked. There were cracks in the bottoms of the pools, with gas bubbling up out of them. Tonga gave me a handful of seeds, dead and dry, and had me drop them into the crack at the Stagnant Oasis. They grew. Right there, out of nothing.\n\nA few snapjaw shells later, Tonga had an answer and didn't like it. The land was dreaming and couldn't wake, and the dream was coming from the Wailing Caverns. Before I went anywhere near them, I was to see Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. Druids always want a second opinion."
L["The Barrens Oases"] = "The Barrens Oases"
L["The Stagnant Oasis"] = "The Stagnant Oasis"
L["Altered Beings"] = "Altered Beings"
L["Hamuul Runetotem"] = "Hamuul Runetotem"
L["Disciples of Naralex"] = "Disciples of Naralex"
L["Above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, in the Barrens, two disciples of the druid Naralex keep watch: Nalpak and Ebru. Their master went down into the caverns to heal the land, and strange beasts have been coming up ever since."] = "Above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, in the Barrens, two disciples of the druid Naralex keep watch: Nalpak and Ebru. Their master went down into the caverns to heal the land, and strange beasts have been coming up ever since."
L["Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem, on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, has walked in the land of dreams and seen what waits in the Wailing Caverns. Above the caverns' entrance, two disciples of the druid Naralex could use a hand too."] = "Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem, on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, has walked in the land of dreams and seen what waits in the Wailing Caverns. Above the caverns' entrance, two disciples of the druid Naralex could use a hand too."
L["There's a cave above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, and in it two disciples of a druid named Naralex. Naralex had a lovely plan: enter the Emerald Dream and grow the Barrens back into a forest. Somewhere along the way the dream went bad, and the caverns filled up with whatever crawled out of it.\n\nDeviates, the disciples call them. Nalpak looks on the bright side and thought their hides would make good leather. Ebru just wanted them dead, seven each of four kinds, and was very particular about the count. Happily, the hides came off the same beasts, so I did both jobs at once.\n\nEbru called it the first step toward a restored Barrens. Their master, I gathered, was still down there somewhere, asleep."] = "There's a cave above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, and in it two disciples of a druid named Naralex. Naralex had a lovely plan: enter the Emerald Dream and grow the Barrens back into a forest. Somewhere along the way the dream went bad, and the caverns filled up with whatever crawled out of it.\n\nDeviates, the disciples call them. Nalpak looks on the bright side and thought their hides would make good leather. Ebru just wanted them dead, seven each of four kinds, and was very particular about the count. Happily, the hides came off the same beasts, so I did both jobs at once.\n\nEbru called it the first step toward a restored Barrens. Their master, I gathered, was still down there somewhere, asleep."
L["Hamuul Runetotem does his scouting asleep. He'd gone into the land of dreams and seen a cult of druids in the Wailing Caverns, druids who had meant to heal the Barrens and lost their way. He was too old to stay long. Nara Wildmane had stayed, and Nara had seen their faces.\n\nThe Druids of the Fang, she called them. Four leaders, a dream gem apiece, and all four haunting her sleep. She wanted the gems. I understood that to include the leaders.\n\nAbove the cave mouth, two disciples of Naralex had requests of their own, hides and a body count, and the caverns supplied both. When I came back with the gems, Nara said her dreams were finally free of those faces. Somebody slept well that night. Not me."] = "Hamuul Runetotem does his scouting asleep. He'd gone into the land of dreams and seen a cult of druids in the Wailing Caverns, druids who had meant to heal the Barrens and lost their way. He was too old to stay long. Nara Wildmane had stayed, and Nara had seen their faces.\n\nThe Druids of the Fang, she called them. Four leaders, a dream gem apiece, and all four haunting her sleep. She wanted the gems. I understood that to include the leaders.\n\nAbove the cave mouth, two disciples of Naralex had requests of their own, hides and a body count, and the caverns supplied both. When I came back with the gems, Nara said her dreams were finally free of those faces. Somebody slept well that night. Not me."
L["Leaders of the Fang"] = "Leaders of the Fang"
L["Deviate Hides"] = "Deviate Hides"
L["Deviate Eradication"] = "Deviate Eradication"
L["Apothecary Zamah, sent out to Thunder Bluff by the Royal Apothecary Society, wanted ten serpentbloom from the darkest corners of the Wailing Caverns, in the service of the Dark Lady. I picked them between snakes. Zamah called them splendid specimens, which from an apothecary is practically a hug."] = "Apothecary Zamah, sent out to Thunder Bluff by the Royal Apothecary Society, wanted ten serpentbloom from the darkest corners of the Wailing Caverns, in the service of the Dark Lady. I picked them between snakes. Zamah called them splendid specimens, which from an apothecary is practically a hug."
L["Serpentbloom"] = "Serpentbloom"
L["Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet had tried to unload a huge shipment from Booty Bay all at once and brought the lot down, and in the confusion Mad Magglish ran off with a bottle of 99-year-old port and hid in the Wailing Caverns. I brought the bottle back. Bigglefuzz, who had been about to lose the job over it, hurried it off to Gazlowe as a gift."] = "Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet had tried to unload a huge shipment from Booty Bay all at once and brought the lot down, and in the confusion Mad Magglish ran off with a bottle of 99-year-old port and hid in the Wailing Caverns. I brought the bottle back. Bigglefuzz, who had been about to lose the job over it, hurried it off to Gazlowe as a gift."
L["Trouble at the Docks"] = "Trouble at the Docks"
L["Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet is convinced the raptors of the Barrens are cleverer than other raptors, that the cleverness lives in their horns, and that ground horn in wine makes a smart drink worth a fortune. I brought back horns off the sunscale scytheclaws. Mebok was grinding them before I'd let go."] = "Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet is convinced the raptors of the Barrens are cleverer than other raptors, that the cleverness lives in their horns, and that ground horn in wine makes a smart drink worth a fortune. I brought back horns off the sunscale scytheclaws. Mebok was grinding them before I'd let go."
L["Raptor Horns"] = "Raptor Horns"
L["The horns didn't work. Mebok wasn't discouraged, since nobody gets rich on the first try, and had moved on to Wailing Essence, which gathers in the ectoplasmic things down in the Wailing Caverns and might be what makes the Barrens so strange. I brought six portions. Mebok promised to send me more once the fortune came in. I'm still waiting."] = "The horns didn't work. Mebok wasn't discouraged, since nobody gets rich on the first try, and had moved on to Wailing Essence, which gathers in the ectoplasmic things down in the Wailing Caverns and might be what makes the Barrens so strange. I brought six portions. Mebok promised to send me more once the fortune came in. I'm still waiting."
L["Smart Drinks"] = "Smart Drinks"
L["Just inside the Wailing Caverns, a Disciple of Naralex waits for the four Fanglords to fall. Once they have, the disciple means to walk all the way down to the sleeping druid and wake him, and will need protecting every step."] = "Just inside the Wailing Caverns, a Disciple of Naralex waits for the four Fanglords to fall. Once they have, the disciple means to walk all the way down to the sleeping druid and wake him, and will need protecting every step."
L["With the Fanglords dead, the disciple waiting inside the caverns finally had a clear road and someone to stand in front. We walked all the way down. Every time the disciple stopped to cast, the caverns sent something to interrupt, and I interrupted back.\n\nNaralex lay at the bottom, tossing in his sleep. The disciple reached into the dream after him, and Naralex, not helping, dreamed up something huge and hungry that climbed out of the water. It went down. Naralex woke with a shout, thanked us kindly, and left to find the rest of his disciples.\n\nThe beast left a glowing green shard behind. Someone in Ratchet sent me back toward the caverns to Falla Sagewind, who called it a nightmare and said it belonged with a wise druid. Mathrengyl Bearwalker, all the way over in Darnassus, looked into it, said things in the Emerald Dream were not as anyone had thought, and that the Cenarion druids alone would attend to it. I took the hint."] = "With the Fanglords dead, the disciple waiting inside the caverns finally had a clear road and someone to stand in front. We walked all the way down. Every time the disciple stopped to cast, the caverns sent something to interrupt, and I interrupted back.\n\nNaralex lay at the bottom, tossing in his sleep. The disciple reached into the dream after him, and Naralex, not helping, dreamed up something huge and hungry that climbed out of the water. It went down. Naralex woke with a shout, thanked us kindly, and left to find the rest of his disciples.\n\nThe beast left a glowing green shard behind. Someone in Ratchet sent me back toward the caverns to Falla Sagewind, who called it a nightmare and said it belonged with a wise druid. Mathrengyl Bearwalker, all the way over in Darnassus, looked into it, said things in the Emerald Dream were not as anyone had thought, and that the Cenarion druids alone would attend to it. I took the hint."
L["With the Fanglords dead, the disciple waiting inside the caverns finally had a clear road and someone to stand in front. We walked all the way down. Every time the disciple stopped to cast, the caverns sent something to interrupt, and I interrupted back.\n\nNaralex lay at the bottom, tossing in his sleep. The disciple reached into the dream after him, and Naralex, not helping, dreamed up something huge and hungry that climbed out of the water. It went down. Naralex woke with a shout, thanked us kindly, and left to find the rest of his disciples.\n\nThe beast left a glowing green shard behind. Someone in Ratchet sent me back toward the caverns to Falla Sagewind, who called it a nightmare and said it belonged with a wise druid. Hamuul Runetotem looked into it, said things in the Emerald Dream were not as anyone had thought, and told me not to concern myself with it. I'm trying."] = "With the Fanglords dead, the disciple waiting inside the caverns finally had a clear road and someone to stand in front. We walked all the way down. Every time the disciple stopped to cast, the caverns sent something to interrupt, and I interrupted back.\n\nNaralex lay at the bottom, tossing in his sleep. The disciple reached into the dream after him, and Naralex, not helping, dreamed up something huge and hungry that climbed out of the water. It went down. Naralex woke with a shout, thanked us kindly, and left to find the rest of his disciples.\n\nThe beast left a glowing green shard behind. Someone in Ratchet sent me back toward the caverns to Falla Sagewind, who called it a nightmare and said it belonged with a wise druid. Hamuul Runetotem looked into it, said things in the Emerald Dream were not as anyone had thought, and told me not to concern myself with it. I'm trying."
L["The Glowing Shard"] = "The Glowing Shard"
L["Glowing Shard"] = "Glowing Shard"
L["the depths of the Wailing Caverns"] = "the depths of the Wailing Caverns"
L["In Nightmares"] = "In Nightmares"
L["Are We There, Yeti?"] = "Are We There, Yeti?"
L["Everlook sits at the cold end of Winterspring, a goblin trading town where travelers come in out of the snow. Umi Rumplesnicker has been drawing up plans there, and she'll let you in on them if you promise not to tell.\n\nUmi's friends always seem to have the great ideas. This time she has one of her own. It needs a few things from the snowfields outside town, and someone who can keep a straight face."] = "Everlook sits at the cold end of Winterspring, a goblin trading town where travelers come in out of the snow. Umi Rumplesnicker has been drawing up plans there, and she'll let you in on them if you promise not to tell.\n\nUmi's friends always seem to have the great ideas. This time she has one of her own. It needs a few things from the snowfields outside town, and someone who can keep a straight face."
L["Winterspring / Tanaris / Un'Goro Crater"] = "Winterspring / Tanaris / Un'Goro Crater"
L["Umi Rumplesnicker"] = "Umi Rumplesnicker"
L["Legacki"] = "Legacki"
L["Sprinkle"] = "Sprinkle"
L["Quixxil"] = "Quixxil"
L["Umi's Secret"] = "Umi's Secret"
L["Umi Rumplesnicker, in Everlook in Winterspring, has plans for something great and is bursting to tell someone. Promise to keep it quiet and she'll let you in on the secret, and on the shopping list that comes with it."] = "Umi Rumplesnicker, in Everlook in Winterspring, has plans for something great and is bursting to tell someone. Promise to keep it quiet and she'll let you in on the secret, and on the shopping list that comes with it."
L["So there's a tinkerer in Everlook called Umi Rumplesnicker, and she had a secret. She'd let me in on it if I promised not to tell. I promised, and I've kept my word right up until now.\n\nHer friends, she said, always had the great ideas. Well, now she had one. A mechanical yeti. They'd be frightened out of their wits, and then, once they'd stopped shaking, terribly impressed.\n\nA yeti needs a coat, so I went southeast and collected ten thick furs from the ice thistle yetis, who were still wearing them. Then it needed horns, the big ones off the patriarchs and matriarchs in their cave. Only the best-looking ones, Umi said. No beat up or broken horns, please.\n\nTry asking a yeti patriarch to hold still so you don't scuff the goods."] = "So there's a tinkerer in Everlook called Umi Rumplesnicker, and she had a secret. She'd let me in on it if I promised not to tell. I promised, and I've kept my word right up until now.\n\nHer friends, she said, always had the great ideas. Well, now she had one. A mechanical yeti. They'd be frightened out of their wits, and then, once they'd stopped shaking, terribly impressed.\n\nA yeti needs a coat, so I went southeast and collected ten thick furs from the ice thistle yetis, who were still wearing them. Then it needed horns, the big ones off the patriarchs and matriarchs in their cave. Only the best-looking ones, Umi said. No beat up or broken horns, please.\n\nTry asking a yeti patriarch to hold still so you don't scuff the goods."
L["Thick Yeti Fur"] = "Thick Yeti Fur"
L["Pristine Yeti Horns"] = "Pristine Yeti Horns"
L["Umi Rumplesnicker's project is finished, and she has already written to her friends in Everlook, Gadgetzan and Un'Goro Crater to say a surprise is coming. Somebody has to deliver it. Umi, in Everlook, is looking at you."] = "Umi Rumplesnicker's project is finished, and she has already written to her friends in Everlook, Gadgetzan and Un'Goro Crater to say a surprise is coming. Somebody has to deliver it. Umi, in Everlook, is looking at you."
L["Umi had written ahead to tell her friends a surprise was coming. The surprise was me, with her mechanical yeti in my pack.\n\nFirst stop, right there in Everlook: Legacki. I switched the yeti on, it went stomping over roaring its head off, and Legacki jumped a foot in the air, called me a big meanie and guessed who'd put me up to it in one try. Umi, it turns out, is always playing jokes on Legacki.\n\nThen the long road south. In Gadgetzan the next friend also guessed Umi. At Marshal's Refuge in Un'Goro, Quixxil didn't guess anything. Quixxil ran. The yeti followed. Quixxil asked it why. It roared, which I suppose is an answer.\n\nBack in Everlook, Umi was thrilled. That would teach them to make fun of her ideas, she said. I didn't mention what Legacki had told me. Some secrets you keep."] = "Umi had written ahead to tell her friends a surprise was coming. The surprise was me, with her mechanical yeti in my pack.\n\nFirst stop, right there in Everlook: Legacki. I switched the yeti on, it went stomping over roaring its head off, and Legacki jumped a foot in the air, called me a big meanie and guessed who'd put me up to it in one try. Umi, it turns out, is always playing jokes on Legacki.\n\nThen the long road south. In Gadgetzan the next friend also guessed Umi. At Marshal's Refuge in Un'Goro, Quixxil didn't guess anything. Quixxil ran. The yeti followed. Quixxil asked it why. It roared, which I suppose is an answer.\n\nBack in Everlook, Umi was thrilled. That would teach them to make fun of her ideas, she said. I didn't mention what Legacki had told me. Some secrets you keep."
L["Umi's Friends"] = "Umi's Friends"
L["The Shards of Myzrael"] = "The Shards of Myzrael"
L["High in the northern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, a cluster of crystals pulses with a voice. It belongs to Myzrael, a princess of the earth, held deep beneath the Highlands by the giants.\n\nFind the Shards of Myzrael and hear her out. Freeing a princess is the stuff of old songs, though the songs never mention how much walking is involved."] = "High in the northern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, a cluster of crystals pulses with a voice. It belongs to Myzrael, a princess of the earth, held deep beneath the Highlands by the giants.\n\nFind the Shards of Myzrael and hear her out. Freeing a princess is the stuff of old songs, though the songs never mention how much walking is involved."
