L["The Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn is a band of deserters holding out against Colonel Kurzen, their old commander. Private Thorsen, on the road near camp, could use a hand right now, and Sergeant Yohwa has work for anyone who can fight."] = "The Rebel Camp in northern Stranglethorn is a band of deserters holding out against Colonel Kurzen, their old commander. Private Thorsen, on the road near camp, could use a hand right now, and Sergeant Yohwa has work for anyone who can fight."
L["So there's a camp of deserters in northern Stranglethorn, outnumbered ten to one by their old colonel. I pulled one of them, Private Thorsen, out of a scrap with Kurzen's men on the road. Thorsen had been sent back to spy on Kurzen. Kurzen, it turned out, knew.\n\nSo somebody in camp was talking. Lieutenant Doren sent me into Kurzen's Compound for his logistics officer's papers. Nothing about Thorsen, but a little brass key hidden in a ledger's binding, and a strongbox in the caves out back that it opened. Inside was a muddy note with Thorsen's whole routine, signed with one letter. M.\n\nBetween errands, the sergeant had me thin out Kurzen's men and rob his medicine men of their remedies. Then the corporal who keeps the patrol schedules told me who'd walked with Thorsen last week. I took that back to Doren and let him do the arithmetic."] = "So there's a camp of deserters in northern Stranglethorn, outnumbered ten to one by their old colonel. I pulled one of them, Private Thorsen, out of a scrap with Kurzen's men on the road. Thorsen had been sent back to spy on Kurzen. Kurzen, it turned out, knew.\n\nSo somebody in camp was talking. Lieutenant Doren sent me into Kurzen's Compound for his logistics officer's papers. Nothing about Thorsen, but a little brass key hidden in a ledger's binding, and a strongbox in the caves out back that it opened. Inside was a muddy note with Thorsen's whole routine, signed with one letter. M.\n\nBetween errands, the sergeant had me thin out Kurzen's men and rob his medicine men of their remedies. Then the corporal who keeps the patrol schedules told me who'd walked with Thorsen last week. I took that back to Doren and let him do the arithmetic."
