L["Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp has a question nobody else is asking: what turned a once-noble man into the colonel they're fighting? Sergeant Yohwa and Lieutenant Doren, meanwhile, are ready to go after Kurzen's best troops, and the colonel himself."] = "Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp has a question nobody else is asking: what turned a once-noble man into the colonel they're fighting? Sergeant Yohwa and Lieutenant Doren, meanwhile, are ready to go after Kurzen's best troops, and the colonel himself."
L["The sergeant sent me after Kurzen's special forces, down in the caves they call the Stockpile, and then the lieutenant sent me after the colonel himself. Kurzen commanded from the very back of it. I came out with his head, which settled the military side of things.\n\nBrother Nimetz was stuck on another side. Kurzen had once been a good man, and Nimetz wanted to know what turned him. So I copied four troll legends off tablets in the old ruins, and pried a handful of fetishes off the Skullsplitter witchdoctors down south.\n\nNimetz added a scout's report: the local trolls were all worked up, repeating one word. I'lalai. He bundled the lot and sent me to a friend of his in Southshore. Stranglethorn to Hillsbrad, with a parcel. Nobody in that camp does anything by halves."] = "The sergeant sent me after Kurzen's special forces, down in the caves they call the Stockpile, and then the lieutenant sent me after the colonel himself. Kurzen commanded from the very back of it. I came out with his head, which settled the military side of things.\n\nBrother Nimetz was stuck on another side. Kurzen had once been a good man, and Nimetz wanted to know what turned him. So I copied four troll legends off tablets in the old ruins, and pried a handful of fetishes off the Skullsplitter witchdoctors down south.\n\nNimetz added a scout's report: the local trolls were all worked up, repeating one word. I'lalai. He bundled the lot and sent me to a friend of his in Southshore. Stranglethorn to Hillsbrad, with a parcel. Nobody in that camp does anything by halves."
L["Kurzen's Mystery"] = "Kurzen's Mystery"
L["Troll Witchery"] = "Troll Witchery"
L["An Acquaintance in Southshore"] = "An Acquaintance in Southshore"
L["Special Forces"] = "Special Forces"
L["Nimetz had one more name for me later on. Kurzen was dead, but whatever had turned him was not: an ogre mage called Mai'Zoth, holed up in a mound in the eastern mountains and said to bend minds. Nimetz was positive Mai'Zoth had done it. I brought back the Mind's Eye, the thing the ogre used, and handed it over very carefully."] = "Nimetz had one more name for me later on. Kurzen was dead, but whatever had turned him was not: an ogre mage called Mai'Zoth, holed up in a mound in the eastern mountains and said to bend minds. Nimetz was positive Mai'Zoth had done it. I brought back the Mind's Eye, the thing the ogre used, and handed it over very carefully."
L["Mai'Zoth"] = "Mai'Zoth"
L["The Vile Reef"] = "The Vile Reef"
L["Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp wants a shard of an old tablet in the Vile Reef, a troll city the sea swallowed long ago. The tablet is sacred to the Darkspear. The murlocs living in the ruins don't care."] = "Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp wants a shard of an old tablet in the Vile Reef, a troll city the sea swallowed long ago. The tablet is sacred to the Darkspear. The murlocs living in the ruins don't care."
L["Kin'weelay wanted a shard of a tablet out of the Vile Reef, an old troll city an earthquake sank long ago. Murlocs live in it now. The tablet tells the tale of Gri'lek, a hero of troll legend, and Kin'weelay wanted a piece of it for Orgrimmar. I chipped one off and swam for it.\n\nKin'weelay found the shard odd. It spoke of a lost city, I'lalai, as a great sprawling civilization, and the reef ruins aren't nearly big enough. So I went up the coast to another old ruin with hide and charcoal and took a rubbing of a second legend.\n\nCommander Aggro'gosh had naga swarming the ruins on the sea floor and wanted their tridents. Kin'weelay remembered a cavern by the reef from diving there as a youngster. I found it, west of the reef, with naga gathered all around. Naga never gather anywhere for a good reason."] = "Kin'weelay wanted a shard of a tablet out of the Vile Reef, an old troll city an earthquake sank long ago. Murlocs live in it now. The tablet tells the tale of Gri'lek, a hero of troll legend, and Kin'weelay wanted a piece of it for Orgrimmar. I chipped one off and swam for it.\n\nKin'weelay found the shard odd. It spoke of a lost city, I'lalai, as a great sprawling civilization, and the reef ruins aren't nearly big enough. So I went up the coast to another old ruin with hide and charcoal and took a rubbing of a second legend.\n\nCommander Aggro'gosh had naga swarming the ruins on the sea floor and wanted their tridents. Kin'weelay remembered a cavern by the reef from diving there as a youngster. I found it, west of the reef, with naga gathered all around. Naga never gather anywhere for a good reason."
L["The Gurubashi Legends of Old"] = "The Gurubashi Legends of Old"
L["Locating the Lost City"] = "Locating the Lost City"
L["Enemies in the Water"] = "Enemies in the Water"
L["Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore has read the report from the Rebel Camp with shaking hands, and he believes a lost city has risen off Stranglethorn's coast. He wants its legends and its magic studied. Krazek in Booty Bay wants something from the place too."] = "Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore has read the report from the Rebel Camp with shaking hands, and he believes a lost city has risen off Stranglethorn's coast. He wants its legends and its magic studied. Krazek in Booty Bay wants something from the place too."
L["Beyond the cavern west of the Vile Reef lie ruins the naga are guarding, and Kin'weelay at Grom'gol thinks they may be the lost city. Commander Aggro'gosh wants to know what the naga are after. Krazek in Booty Bay has an interest in the place too."] = "Beyond the cavern west of the Vile Reef lie ruins the naga are guarding, and Kin'weelay at Grom'gol thinks they may be the lost city. Commander Aggro'gosh wants to know what the naga are after. Krazek in Booty Bay has an interest in the place too."
L["Loremaster Dibbs read the report with shaking hands. If the trolls were right, the lost city of I'lalai had risen off Stranglethorn's coast, which made it, in his words, the archeological discovery of the century. Could I possibly go back down there? With hide and charcoal?\n\nSo into the Drowned City I went, with friends. I took rubbings of four tablets and collected troll fetishes, since Dibbs suspected whatever magic raised the city might have something to do with what took the colonel's mind.\n\nKrazek in Booty Bay had me on a second job: a crew of Saltseer pirates had got there first and were looting magical things he'd rather loot himself. He especially wanted their captain, Dreadrise, out of the picture. Permanently. The picture is clearer now."] = "Loremaster Dibbs read the report with shaking hands. If the trolls were right, the lost city of I'lalai had risen off Stranglethorn's coast, which made it, in his words, the archeological discovery of the century. Could I possibly go back down there? With hide and charcoal?\n\nSo into the Drowned City I went, with friends. I took rubbings of four tablets and collected troll fetishes, since Dibbs suspected whatever magic raised the city might have something to do with what took the colonel's mind.\n\nKrazek in Booty Bay had me on a second job: a crew of Saltseer pirates had got there first and were looting magical things he'd rather loot himself. He especially wanted their captain, Dreadrise, out of the picture. Permanently. The picture is clearer now."
L["Past the cavern the naga were guarding stood the ruins Kin'weelay had hoped for: the lost city of I'lalai, up out of the sea after all that time. Kin'weelay was too old to go in, and wanted etchings of every tablet inside. Commander Aggro'gosh wanted the naga's leader dead before they found whatever they were looking for. I brought enough friends to manage both.\n\nKrazek in Booty Bay had me on a second job: a crew of Saltseer pirates had got there first and were looting magical things he'd rather loot himself. He especially wanted their captain out of the picture. Permanently. The picture is clearer now."] = "Past the cavern the naga were guarding stood the ruins Kin'weelay had hoped for: the lost city of I'lalai, up out of the sea after all that time. Kin'weelay was too old to go in, and wanted etchings of every tablet inside. Commander Aggro'gosh wanted the naga's leader dead before they found whatever they were looking for. I brought enough friends to manage both.\n\nKrazek in Booty Bay had me on a second job: a crew of Saltseer pirates had got there first and were looting magical things he'd rather loot himself. He especially wanted their captain out of the picture. Permanently. The picture is clearer now."
L["Take Two With Water"] = "Take Two With Water"
