L["Archmage Timear in Dalaran had heard about the ruin and wanted one of the idols the old Gurubashi witch doctors used to focus their blood magic. For its archeological value, the archmage said. I found one and handed it over to the Kirin Tor, who I'm sure will be very responsible with it."] = "Archmage Timear in Dalaran had heard about the ruin and wanted one of the idols the old Gurubashi witch doctors used to focus their blood magic. For its archeological value, the archmage said. I found one and handed it over to the Kirin Tor, who I'm sure will be very responsible with it."
L["Ancient Gurubashi Secrets"] = "Ancient Gurubashi Secrets"
L["Mazu'kon in Mulgore had heard the old Gurubashi channeled their blood magic through idols of pure truesilver and wanted one, strictly for academics. The advice was to kill the most impressive-looking priest in the place. It was good advice. Academics, I'm told, is a very broad field."] = "Mazu'kon in Mulgore had heard the old Gurubashi channeled their blood magic through idols of pure truesilver and wanted one, strictly for academics. The advice was to kill the most impressive-looking priest in the place. It was good advice. Academics, I'm told, is a very broad field."
L["Ancient Gurubashi Idol"] = "Ancient Gurubashi Idol"
L["Somewhere in the city I picked up a scrap of scroll covered in symbols I couldn't read. It didn't feel dangerous, so I took it to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay, a collector of odd magic. One less mystery in my pack."] = "Somewhere in the city I picked up a scrap of scroll covered in symbols I couldn't read. It didn't feel dangerous, so I took it to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay, a collector of odd magic. One less mystery in my pack."
L["Partial Mystical Notes"] = "Partial Mystical Notes"
L["the Drowned City"] = "the Drowned City"
L["A Tale Worth Telling"] = "A Tale Worth Telling"
L["Loremaster Dibbs calls what you brought back a discovery of historical proportions, and has written to the Explorers' League in Ironforge to say so. Someone has to carry the letter. He also has a friend in Dalaran who would love to see one of those fetishes."] = "Loremaster Dibbs calls what you brought back a discovery of historical proportions, and has written to the Explorers' League in Ironforge to say so. Someone has to carry the letter. He also has a friend in Dalaran who would love to see one of those fetishes."
L["The Darkspear keep their history by telling it. Kin'weelay at Grom'gol wants your etchings taken to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, one of the wisest of the Darkspear, who will want to hear this tale."] = "The Darkspear keep their history by telling it. Kin'weelay at Grom'gol wants your etchings taken to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, one of the wisest of the Darkspear, who will want to hear this tale."
L["Dibbs called it a discovery of historical proportions and wrote to his colleague at the Explorers' League straight away. I carried the letter to Historian Karnik in Ironforge, with a copy of Dibbs's translations of the tablets. A whole drowned city's worth of legend, in my pack.\n\nI'd gone to Stranglethorn to help a few rebels with their colonel. I came back with the archeological discovery of the century. That's the thing about discoveries of historical proportions: somebody still has to walk them to Ironforge."] = "Dibbs called it a discovery of historical proportions and wrote to his colleague at the Explorers' League straight away. I carried the letter to Historian Karnik in Ironforge, with a copy of Dibbs's translations of the tablets. A whole drowned city's worth of legend, in my pack.\n\nI'd gone to Stranglethorn to help a few rebels with their colonel. I came back with the archeological discovery of the century. That's the thing about discoveries of historical proportions: somebody still has to walk them to Ironforge."
L["The Darkspear keep their history by telling it, Kin'weelay explained: legends passed down to the younglings, lessons and cautionary tales. So the etchings went to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, their spiritual leader, to hear the truth of it. Kin'weelay even made me a copy of my own, and offered another if I ever lost it. For a small fee.\n\nSo the tale of I'lalai goes into the telling now, around the fire in Durotar. Somewhere a youngling is going to hear it and want to go diving. I know the feeling."] = "The Darkspear keep their history by telling it, Kin'weelay explained: legends passed down to the younglings, lessons and cautionary tales. So the etchings went to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village, their spiritual leader, to hear the truth of it. Kin'weelay even made me a copy of my own, and offered another if I ever lost it. For a small fee.\n\nSo the tale of I'lalai goes into the telling now, around the fire in Durotar. Somewhere a youngling is going to hear it and want to go diving. I know the feeling."
L["Findings for the Explorer's League"] = "Findings for the Explorer's League"
L["Dibbs also had a friend in Dalaran, Abra Cadabra, who studies troll magic and would want a look at one of the fetishes. The Kirin Tor are particular about who they let in. They let me in. Abra got the fetish, and I got to say I'd delivered a troll fetish to someone called Abra Cadabra, which I still enjoy."] = "Dibbs also had a friend in Dalaran, Abra Cadabra, who studies troll magic and would want a look at one of the fetishes. The Kirin Tor are particular about who they let in. They let me in. Abra got the fetish, and I got to say I'd delivered a troll fetish to someone called Abra Cadabra, which I still enjoy."
