-- WoW Forever: Highway Robbery
L["Highway Robbery"] = "Highway Robbery"
L["On a rise at the edge of the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace, a campfire has gone cold beside a camp that's been picked clean. The travelers who made it never left, and the marks on their bones don't match any centaur's weapon.\n\nIf the caravans' gossip is right, whoever did it has done it before. Following that gossip leads a long way out of Desolace, to the docks of Booty Bay and farther still."] = "On a rise at the edge of the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace, a campfire has gone cold beside a camp that's been picked clean. The travelers who made it never left, and the marks on their bones don't match any centaur's weapon.\n\nIf the caravans' gossip is right, whoever did it has done it before. Following that gossip leads a long way out of Desolace, to the docks of Booty Bay and farther still."
L["Desolace / Stranglethorn Vale / Arathi Highlands"] = "Desolace / Stranglethorn Vale / Arathi Highlands"
L["Extinguished Campfire"] = "Extinguished Campfire"
L["the Kodo Graveyard, Desolace"] = "the Kodo Graveyard, Desolace"
L["the inn, Booty Bay, Stranglethorn Vale"] = "the inn, Booty Bay, Stranglethorn Vale"
L["The Pillaged Camp"] = "The Pillaged Camp"
L["On a rise at the edge of the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace, a campfire has burned out and the camp around it has been stripped bare. Take a look at what's left. Whatever happened here, the scavengers of Desolace may have seen it before."] = "On a rise at the edge of the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace, a campfire has burned out and the camp around it has been stripped bare. Take a look at what's left. Whatever happened here, the scavengers of Desolace may have seen it before."
L["So I'm crossing Desolace, which is never anyone's first choice, and on a rise above the Kodo Graveyard there's a campfire gone cold. Around it lay two humans and a dwarf, or what was left of them. Their packs had been emptied, and the cuts on the bones didn't come from any centaur blade I know.\n\nI wanted someone who knew this country's bones, so I took it to the goblin bone collector at Kormek's Hut. Bibbly F'utzbuckle heard me out and said I'd found another one, in the tone you'd use for a cart that's thrown a wheel again."] = "So I'm crossing Desolace, which is never anyone's first choice, and on a rise above the Kodo Graveyard there's a campfire gone cold. Around it lay two humans and a dwarf, or what was left of them. Their packs had been emptied, and the cuts on the bones didn't come from any centaur blade I know.\n\nI wanted someone who knew this country's bones, so I took it to the goblin bone collector at Kormek's Hut. Bibbly F'utzbuckle heard me out and said I'd found another one, in the tone you'd use for a cart that's thrown a wheel again."
L["On the Lam"] = "On the Lam"
L["Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut has seen camps like this before. Caravan gossip blames a band of marauders who fled Desolace with an Alliance marshal on their trail. If one of them is trying to get a boat out, Booty Bay is the place to look."] = "Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut has seen camps like this before. Caravan gossip blames a band of marauders who fled Desolace with an Alliance marshal on their trail. If one of them is trying to get a boat out, Booty Bay is the place to look."
L["According to Bibbly, the caravans blamed a band of marauders who ran once a marshal got on their trail. People on the run end up in ports, so I went to Booty Bay and found one of them, Tokal, drinking at the inn. Tokal asked if I was with the marshal, looked me over and decided I wasn't. I'm still working out how to take that.\n\nThe rest of the story cost me a cherry grog. Tokal's crew had robbed those camps, yes, but for pay, not for the Horde. Their boss was a night elf named Illari Duskfeather. She told them which camps to hit and let them keep most of the loot. The rarer finds she kept for herself, and when the marshal closed in, she left them for dead.\n\nTokal isn't out for revenge, but won't stand in the way of anyone who is. Illari had once mentioned a hideout on the Arathi coast."] = "According to Bibbly, the caravans blamed a band of marauders who ran once a marshal got on their trail. People on the run end up in ports, so I went to Booty Bay and found one of them, Tokal, drinking at the inn. Tokal asked if I was with the marshal, looked me over and decided I wasn't. I'm still working out how to take that.\n\nThe rest of the story cost me a cherry grog. Tokal's crew had robbed those camps, yes, but for pay, not for the Horde. Their boss was a night elf named Illari Duskfeather. She told them which camps to hit and let them keep most of the loot. The rarer finds she kept for herself, and when the marshal closed in, she left them for dead.\n\nTokal isn't out for revenge, but won't stand in the way of anyone who is. Illari had once mentioned a hideout on the Arathi coast."
L["Bibbly F'utzbuckle"] = "Bibbly F'utzbuckle"
L["Cherry for Your Thoughts?"] = "Cherry for Your Thoughts?"
L["Tokal"] = "Tokal"
L["No Honor Among Thieves"] = "No Honor Among Thieves"
L["Tokal says the crew's old boss, Illari Duskfeather, once mentioned a hideout on the coast of the Arathi Highlands. Near the Arathi end of the Thandol Span, a rope bridge crosses to a hillside, and a rowboat waits at the water below."] = "Tokal says the crew's old boss, Illari Duskfeather, once mentioned a hideout on the coast of the Arathi Highlands. Near the Arathi end of the Thandol Span, a rope bridge crosses to a hillside, and a rowboat waits at the water below."
L["The rowboat below the Thandol Span goes where no road does, out to a lonely dock on the Arathi coast. Illari Duskfeather was waiting there, and she wanted to know what I was doing on her dock.\n\nShe has her reasons for what happened in Desolace, and how much of them you get to hear depends on who's asking. I'll keep my half of that conversation to myself. It ended with her key in my hand.\n\nThe key opened her cache at the other end of the dock. Inside were a small box and some coin, likely the rarer finds she'd kept from her crew. I took them. The people they were taken from won't be needing them."] = "The rowboat below the Thandol Span goes where no road does, out to a lonely dock on the Arathi coast. Illari Duskfeather was waiting there, and she wanted to know what I was doing on her dock.\n\nShe has her reasons for what happened in Desolace, and how much of them you get to hear depends on who's asking. I'll keep my half of that conversation to myself. It ended with her key in my hand.\n\nThe key opened her cache at the other end of the dock. Inside were a small box and some coin, likely the rarer finds she'd kept from her crew. I took them. The people they were taken from won't be needing them."
-- Dungeon stories: Hidden Enemies, Blackfathom Villainy, The Mad King, Thorns of the Razorfen, The City of Dalaran, Lost in the Thicket, An Ancient Grudge
L["The City of Dalaran"] = "The City of Dalaran"
L["An emissary from Dalaran has come to Southshore asking the Alliance for help, and the Kirin Tor's high council would prefer that it stayed quiet. Over in Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare has business at the mages' prison camp on Lordamere Lake, and questions about the city beyond it.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran after the Legion flattened it and have kept outsiders at arm's length ever since. Something has gone wrong inside, and for once they are asking for help."] = "An emissary from Dalaran has come to Southshore asking the Alliance for help, and the Kirin Tor's high council would prefer that it stayed quiet. Over in Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare has business at the mages' prison camp on Lordamere Lake, and questions about the city beyond it.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran after the Legion flattened it and have kept outsiders at arm's length ever since. Something has gone wrong inside, and for once they are asking for help."
L["An emissary of the Kirin Tor has come to the town hall in Southshore asking the Alliance for help, and the high council would prefer that it stayed quiet. Archmage Modera sent him, and she needs someone who can be discreet.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran after the Legion flattened it and have kept outsiders at arm's length ever since. Something has gone wrong inside, badly enough that they are asking anyway."] = "An emissary of the Kirin Tor has come to the town hall in Southshore asking the Alliance for help, and the high council would prefer that it stayed quiet. Archmage Modera sent him, and she needs someone who can be discreet.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran after the Legion flattened it and have kept outsiders at arm's length ever since. Something has gone wrong inside, badly enough that they are asking anyway."
L["Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to study, but the Undercity has more urgent work for him. Four Forsaken thieves are locked up in the mages' prison camp on Lordamere Lake, and Wordeen has questions about the city behind it.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran right on the Dark Lady's doorstep and have kept the Forsaken out ever since. Wordeen would very much like to know what they keep in there."] = "Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to study, but the Undercity has more urgent work for him. Four Forsaken thieves are locked up in the mages' prison camp on Lordamere Lake, and Wordeen has questions about the city behind it.\n\nThe Kirin Tor rebuilt Dalaran right on the Dark Lady's doorstep and have kept the Forsaken out ever since. Wordeen would very much like to know what they keep in there."
