L["Emissary Jacques has come down from Dalaran to the town hall in Southshore, asking the Alliance for help. The Kirin Tor rarely ask anyone for anything, and their high council would rather this stayed quiet."] = "Emissary Jacques has come down from Dalaran to the town hall in Southshore, asking the Alliance for help. The Kirin Tor rarely ask anyone for anything, and their high council would rather this stayed quiet."
L["Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to study, but has more pressing work. Four Forsaken robbed the Undercity and fled to Dalaran, where the mages locked them in a camp by Lordamere Lake. Wordeen is curious about the city, too."] = "Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to study, but has more pressing work. Four Forsaken robbed the Undercity and fled to Dalaran, where the mages locked them in a camp by Lordamere Lake. Wordeen is curious about the city, too."
L["There's a Kirin Tor emissary in the town hall in Southshore, Jacques, with the look of a man sent to ask for something his betters would rather not ask for. Something had knocked Dalaran's ley lines loose, and the city's constructs had started breaking things instead of minding them. The high council wanted it kept quiet. Archmage Modera wanted help, and had sent Jacques to find some.\n\nSo I went up to Lordamere Lake and found Modera, or a shimmering image of her, waiting by the water outside the city. The Kirin Tor don't let outsiders in, she told me, but just now they couldn't afford to turn anyone away. The guards on the walls looked calm. Modera warned me not to read anything into that."] = "There's a Kirin Tor emissary in the town hall in Southshore, Jacques, with the look of a man sent to ask for something his betters would rather not ask for. Something had knocked Dalaran's ley lines loose, and the city's constructs had started breaking things instead of minding them. The high council wanted it kept quiet. Archmage Modera wanted help, and had sent Jacques to find some.\n\nSo I went up to Lordamere Lake and found Modera, or a shimmering image of her, waiting by the water outside the city. The Kirin Tor don't let outsiders in, she told me, but just now they couldn't afford to turn anyone away. The guards on the walls looked calm. Modera warned me not to read anything into that."
L["Magus Wordeen came to Tarren Mill to study and ended up running the Dark Lady's errands. Four Forsaken had robbed a vault in the Undercity and fled to Dalaran, and the mages had locked them up in the Lordamere Internment Camp. So I broke into a prison to rob the prisoners. The last of them, Kegan Darkmar, was kept under guard in a house, and the warden's footlocker in there held a grimy key. \"A sewer key?\" said Wordeen, plainly glad he wouldn't be the one using it.\n\nOnce I'd thinned out the wizards patrolling the old ruins, Wordeen had news. Dalaran's barrier was down, and the sewers on the city's northern edge might not be warded. At the entrance stood an image of Archmage Modera, who told me to put my weapon away. She'd been counting on the Horde taking an interest, and she had a proposition."] = "Magus Wordeen came to Tarren Mill to study and ended up running the Dark Lady's errands. Four Forsaken had robbed a vault in the Undercity and fled to Dalaran, and the mages had locked them up in the Lordamere Internment Camp. So I broke into a prison to rob the prisoners. The last of them, Kegan Darkmar, was kept under guard in a house, and the warden's footlocker in there held a grimy key. \"A sewer key?\" said Wordeen, plainly glad he wouldn't be the one using it.\n\nOnce I'd thinned out the wizards patrolling the old ruins, Wordeen had news. Dalaran's barrier was down, and the sewers on the city's northern edge might not be warded. At the entrance stood an image of Archmage Modera, who told me to put my weapon away. She'd been counting on the Horde taking an interest, and she had a proposition."
L["Prison Break In"] = "Prison Break In"
