L["Blood in the Streets"] = "Blood in the Streets"
L["Archmage Modera's image, by Dalaran's sewers on Lordamere Lake, has a key for you and a quiet way into the city. In Stormwind, Shylamiir and High Sorcerer Andromath each have an errand in Dalaran as well."] = "Archmage Modera's image, by Dalaran's sewers on Lordamere Lake, has a key for you and a quiet way into the city. In Stormwind, Shylamiir and High Sorcerer Andromath each have an errand in Dalaran as well."
L["Archmage Modera's image, waiting outside Dalaran's sewers, has a proposition for the Horde. Melisara in Tarren Mill has Forsaken business in the city, and Doctor Martin Felben in the Undercity would like some samples."] = "Archmage Modera's image, waiting outside Dalaran's sewers, has a proposition for the Horde. Melisara in Tarren Mill has Forsaken business in the city, and Doctor Martin Felben in the Undercity would like some samples."
L["Modera's image handed me a sewer key and a plan. The trouble had started at the top of the Violet Citadel, the wards were barely holding, and the Kirin Tor were too busy propping them up to deal with anything else. I was to come in quietly through the sewers and meet her at the citadel.\n\nQuietly lasted as far as the sewers. The streets above were thick with loose magic and constructs that had forgotten whose side they were on. Modera herself, the real one, was waiting on the citadel steps, and she opened a portal up to the Violet Chamber for us.\n\nUp there the Shade of the Archmage was holding the Arcane Mote, and it took some persuading to let go. I carried the mote back out to the lake for her image to look over. It seemed pleased, as far as you can tell with an image."] = "Modera's image handed me a sewer key and a plan. The trouble had started at the top of the Violet Citadel, the wards were barely holding, and the Kirin Tor were too busy propping them up to deal with anything else. I was to come in quietly through the sewers and meet her at the citadel.\n\nQuietly lasted as far as the sewers. The streets above were thick with loose magic and constructs that had forgotten whose side they were on. Modera herself, the real one, was waiting on the citadel steps, and she opened a portal up to the Violet Chamber for us.\n\nUp there the Shade of the Archmage was holding the Arcane Mote, and it took some persuading to let go. I carried the mote back out to the lake for her image to look over. It seemed pleased, as far as you can tell with an image."
L["Modera's proposition was plain enough. She doubted the Horde had Dalaran's best interests at heart, and she'd take our help anyway, since if Dalaran fell the Undercity would go with it. She enchanted my sewer key to get past her wards and told me to meet her at the Violet Citadel. The Kirin Tor would be far too busy to stop me. I could help myself to what I found on the way, as long as I remembered what I'd come for.\n\nUnder the streets and up through the city we went, with every construct in Dalaran trying to tidy us away. Modera opened a portal from the citadel steps, and at the top the Shade of the Archmage gave up the Arcane Mote. I didn't hand it to Modera. I took it home to Wordeen in Tarren Mill."] = "Modera's proposition was plain enough. She doubted the Horde had Dalaran's best interests at heart, and she'd take our help anyway, since if Dalaran fell the Undercity would go with it. She enchanted my sewer key to get past her wards and told me to meet her at the Violet Citadel. The Kirin Tor would be far too busy to stop me. I could help myself to what I found on the way, as long as I remembered what I'd come for.\n\nUnder the streets and up through the city we went, with every construct in Dalaran trying to tidy us away. Modera opened a portal from the citadel steps, and at the top the Shade of the Archmage gave up the Arcane Mote. I didn't hand it to Modera. I took it home to Wordeen in Tarren Mill."
L["Heart of Disruption"] = "Heart of Disruption"
