L["Starving Arcane"] = "Starving Arcane"
L["The breach had scrambled the enchantments and factotums all over Dalaran, the ones keeping up its defenses included, and all that loose magic drew in rogue elementals looking for a free meal. Modera, busy with the wards, asked me to thin out what she called the elemental throng. I worked through the remnants and the mana echoes until the throng was a good deal thinner."] = "The breach had scrambled the enchantments and factotums all over Dalaran, the ones keeping up its defenses included, and all that loose magic drew in rogue elementals looking for a free meal. Modera, busy with the wards, asked me to thin out what she called the elemental throng. I worked through the remnants and the mana echoes until the throng was a good deal thinner."
L["A Green Sample"] = "A Green Sample"
L["Shylamiir"] = "Shylamiir"
L["Shylamiir, the herbalism trainer in Stormwind's park, was annoyed to be disturbed and decided I might as well be useful. Dalaran's mages had taken up botany, the Kirin Tor keep to themselves, and Shylamiir wanted a sample from the city's central garden. The garden had gone fel, with a fel ancient rooted in the middle of it. I came back with one Fel Infused Blossom and a low opinion of Dalaran's gardeners."] = "Shylamiir, the herbalism trainer in Stormwind's park, was annoyed to be disturbed and decided I might as well be useful. Dalaran's mages had taken up botany, the Kirin Tor keep to themselves, and Shylamiir wanted a sample from the city's central garden. The garden had gone fel, with a fel ancient rooted in the middle of it. I came back with one Fel Infused Blossom and a low opinion of Dalaran's gardeners."
L["Power Overwhelming"] = "Power Overwhelming"
L["High Sorcerer Andromath"] = "High Sorcerer Andromath"
L["High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind was worried about the Kirin Tor. They had kept to themselves since Archimonde flattened their city, and now they were rebuilding it with arcane energy leaking out everywhere. If the Alliance didn't help, it could lose one of its strongest allies. So I went after the worst of the leaks, a mana elemental called the Arcanic Enigma, and dispersed it."] = "High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind was worried about the Kirin Tor. They had kept to themselves since Archimonde flattened their city, and now they were rebuilding it with arcane energy leaking out everywhere. If the Alliance didn't help, it could lose one of its strongest allies. So I went after the worst of the leaks, a mana elemental called the Arcanic Enigma, and dispersed it."
L["The Grave Knight"] = "The Grave Knight"
L["Melisara"] = "Melisara"
L["Melisara in Tarren Mill didn't care what became of Dalaran. What she cared about was Atrexis, a traitor to the Forsaken and a frighteningly good necromancer, raising an army of the dead in the city's underbelly under the Kirin Tor's noses. She wanted it understood that the Dark Lady's reach goes everywhere. I found Atrexis down in the sewers and passed the message on."] = "Melisara in Tarren Mill didn't care what became of Dalaran. What she cared about was Atrexis, a traitor to the Forsaken and a frighteningly good necromancer, raising an army of the dead in the city's underbelly under the Kirin Tor's noses. She wanted it understood that the Dark Lady's reach goes everywhere. I found Atrexis down in the sewers and passed the message on."
L["Opportunistic Education"] = "Opportunistic Education"
L["Rexxie Copperclutch"] = "Rexxie Copperclutch"
L["just inside the Dalaran sewers"] = "just inside the Dalaran sewers"
L["Just inside the sewers I met Rexxie Copperclutch, a goblin who took one look at me and decided we were in the same line of work. Rexxie's plan was to lift a secret arcane tome from the mages' libraries and split the profits. I brought back The Founding of Dalaran. Rexxie said it would barely sell at a tourist stall and asked whether I'd just grabbed the first book on the shelf. I had. It's being gilded and sold as an archmage's anyway."] = "Just inside the sewers I met Rexxie Copperclutch, a goblin who took one look at me and decided we were in the same line of work. Rexxie's plan was to lift a secret arcane tome from the mages' libraries and split the profits. I brought back The Founding of Dalaran. Rexxie said it would barely sell at a tourist stall and asked whether I'd just grabbed the first book on the shelf. I had. It's being gilded and sold as an archmage's anyway."
L["Source of Power"] = "Source of Power"
L["Doctor Martin Felben"] = "Doctor Martin Felben"
L["Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium heard that Dalaran's own constructs were attacking it and saw an opportunity. An army of arcane-powered abominations, he reasoned, would impress the Dark Lady and might get him the Royal Apothecary Society to run. The constructs weren't going to hand over their cores, so I took six cracked ones without asking. Felben was delighted, which is never a good sign."] = "Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium heard that Dalaran's own constructs were attacking it and saw an opportunity. An army of arcane-powered abominations, he reasoned, would impress the Dark Lady and might get him the Royal Apothecary Society to run. The constructs weren't going to hand over their cores, so I took six cracked ones without asking. Felben was delighted, which is never a good sign."
L["The Arcane Mote"] = "The Arcane Mote"
L["Archmage Modera thinks it only fair that you carry the good word, and the mote, to Archmage Celindra in the Violet Citadel. The Council of Six may not like how Modera went about things."] = "Archmage Modera thinks it only fair that you carry the good word, and the mote, to Archmage Celindra in the Violet Citadel. The Council of Six may not like how Modera went about things."
L["Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill thinks the Kirin Tor will pay anything to get the mote back, and he knows what he wants for it. Take it to Archmage Modera's image outside Dalaran and see what the mages offer."] = "Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill thinks the Kirin Tor will pay anything to get the mote back, and he knows what he wants for it. Take it to Archmage Modera's image outside Dalaran and see what the mages offer."
L["Modera admitted the Council of Six wouldn't be pleased to hear what she'd been doing behind their backs. She also didn't think they could argue with the results. The city had settled enough for the wards to come down, and she thought it only fair that I be the one to deliver the good word, so this time I went in through the front with the mote in my pack.\n\nArchmage Celindra greeted me in the Violet Citadel with \"Yes? I am quite busy.\" The mote got her attention. I left the citadel a friend of the Kirin Tor, which is more than most people get for going in through the sewers."] = "Modera admitted the Council of Six wouldn't be pleased to hear what she'd been doing behind their backs. She also didn't think they could argue with the results. The city had settled enough for the wards to come down, and she thought it only fair that I be the one to deliver the good word, so this time I went in through the front with the mote in my pack.\n\nArchmage Celindra greeted me in the Violet Citadel with \"Yes? I am quite busy.\" The mote got her attention. I left the citadel a friend of the Kirin Tor, which is more than most people get for going in through the sewers."
L["Wordeen had been thinking while I was away. Sneaking into the city of mages was all very well, he said, but it was time to negotiate. The Kirin Tor knew things that made his own research look thin, and he wanted the Horde let into their order. The mote was his price, and he was sure they would pay anything to get it back.\n\nSo I carried it back out to Modera's image by the lake, under orders to drive a hard bargain with an archmage whose city I'd just helped save. The mote went back to its owners. The Horde got a promise that there might be room for it in Dalaran one day, and Wordeen will have to make that last."] = "Wordeen had been thinking while I was away. Sneaking into the city of mages was all very well, he said, but it was time to negotiate. The Kirin Tor knew things that made his own research look thin, and he wanted the Horde let into their order. The mote was his price, and he was sure they would pay anything to get it back.\n\nSo I carried it back out to Modera's image by the lake, under orders to drive a hard bargain with an archmage whose city I'd just helped save. The mote went back to its owners. The Horde got a promise that there might be room for it in Dalaran one day, and Wordeen will have to make that last."
L["Friend of the Kirin Tor"] = "Friend of the Kirin Tor"
L["Shrewd Negotiations"] = "Shrewd Negotiations"
L["Lost in the Thicket"] = "Lost in the Thicket"
L["A dig crew went up into the Wetlands highlands, and the news coming back down has dried up. In Menethil Harbor and in Lakeshire, families are waiting to hear from people who went up there. At Hammerfall there's a rumor that the Dragonmaw are planning something in the same hills.\n\nRethiel the Greenwarden says the land up there is sick. The Deathstalkers want someone to go and look before they move."] = "A dig crew went up into the Wetlands highlands, and the news coming back down has dried up. In Menethil Harbor and in Lakeshire, families are waiting to hear from people who went up there. At Hammerfall there's a rumor that the Dragonmaw are planning something in the same hills.\n\nRethiel the Greenwarden says the land up there is sick. The Deathstalkers want someone to go and look before they move."
L["Caitlin Grassman's husband went up into the Wetlands highlands to see a grass a dig crew had told him about, and he hasn't come home to Menethil Harbor. In Lakeshire, Dorin Songblade's brother took a crew of diggers into the same hills, and his letters have stopped coming.\n\nOut in the marsh, Rethiel the Greenwarden can feel something wrong with the land, and the creatures up in the hills are taking it badly."] = "Caitlin Grassman's husband went up into the Wetlands highlands to see a grass a dig crew had told him about, and he hasn't come home to Menethil Harbor. In Lakeshire, Dorin Songblade's brother took a crew of diggers into the same hills, and his letters have stopped coming.\n\nOut in the marsh, Rethiel the Greenwarden can feel something wrong with the land, and the creatures up in the hills are taking it badly."
L["Word has reached Hammerfall that the Dragonmaw are planning something in the Wetlands, and the Deathstalkers want to know more before they move. Their agent is waiting in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp for anyone with the nerve to help.\n\nIn Orgrimmar, Borstan has seen the size of the raptor talons coming back from a dig in the Wetlands highlands, and would like to know how the rest of the raptor tastes."] = "Word has reached Hammerfall that the Dragonmaw are planning something in the Wetlands, and the Deathstalkers want to know more before they move. Their agent is waiting in the hills above the Dragonmaw camp for anyone with the nerve to help.\n\nIn Orgrimmar, Borstan has seen the size of the raptor talons coming back from a dig in the Wetlands highlands, and would like to know how the rest of the raptor tastes."
