L["The Greenwarden"] = "The Greenwarden"
L["Out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road lives Rethiel the Greenwarden, who watches over the Wetlands and could use a hand. First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor knows the way, but would rather you didn't go."] = "Out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road lives Rethiel the Greenwarden, who watches over the Wetlands and could use a hand. First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor knows the way, but would rather you didn't go."
L["Rethiel the Greenwarden lives out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road, and told me the roots and ferns spoke well of me. I've had worse references. The land was weeping from festered wounds, Rethiel said, and I was to heal it.\n\nMost of the wound was Mosshide gnolls. There were more of them all the time, cutting down trees and warming themselves with the burning wood, so I thinned them out and took away the flints they used to start their fires. Rethiel meant to smash every one and throw the pieces into the sea.\n\nThe fen creepers were the rest of it. Rethiel called them blisters on the land and wanted them settled back into the marsh, and I obliged. By the end the Greenwarden's faith in my people, which had been tested before, was coming back."] = "Rethiel the Greenwarden lives out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road, and told me the roots and ferns spoke well of me. I've had worse references. The land was weeping from festered wounds, Rethiel said, and I was to heal it.\n\nMost of the wound was Mosshide gnolls. There were more of them all the time, cutting down trees and warming themselves with the burning wood, so I thinned them out and took away the flints they used to start their fires. Rethiel meant to smash every one and throw the pieces into the sea.\n\nThe fen creepers were the rest of it. Rethiel called them blisters on the land and wanted them settled back into the marsh, and I obliged. By the end the Greenwarden's faith in my people, which had been tested before, was coming back."
L["First Mate Fitzsimmons"] = "First Mate Fitzsimmons"
L["First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor knew where to find the Greenwarden, out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road, and seemed to hope I wasn't really going. I was. The first mate also told me to leave my money behind. I kept it, and the Greenwarden never mentioned it."] = "First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor knew where to find the Greenwarden, out in the marsh east of the Dun Modr road, and seemed to hope I wasn't really going. I was. The first mate also told me to leave my money behind. I kept it, and the Greenwarden never mentioned it."
L["Fire Taboo"] = "Fire Taboo"
