L["Young Crocolisk Skins"] = "Young Crocolisk Skins"
L["James Halloran"] = "James Halloran"
L["James Halloran, the tanner in Menethil Harbor, ships cured crocolisk skins to ports all over the world and was running short of the soft ones that come off young crocolisks. I went out into the marsh and came back with a stack. Halloran called them superb and wanted to start curing them at once, but had more work for me first."] = "James Halloran, the tanner in Menethil Harbor, ships cured crocolisk skins to ports all over the world and was running short of the soft ones that come off young crocolisks. I went out into the marsh and came back with a stack. Halloran called them superb and wanted to start curing them at once, but had more work for me first."
L["The Highland Dig"] = "The Highland Dig"
L["Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor hasn't seen her husband since he went up into the highlands, and Dorin Songblade in Lakeshire hasn't heard from his brother, who led a dig crew into the same hills. Rethiel the Greenwarden is worried about those hills too."] = "Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor hasn't seen her husband since he went up into the highlands, and Dorin Songblade in Lakeshire hasn't heard from his brother, who led a dig crew into the same hills. Rethiel the Greenwarden is worried about those hills too."
L["Zaruk at Hammerfall has heard the Dragonmaw are planning something in the Wetlands, and a Deathstalker agent is waiting in the hills above their camp for help. Borstan in Orgrimmar wants meat from the raptors at the dig in the highlands."] = "Zaruk at Hammerfall has heard the Dragonmaw are planning something in the Wetlands, and a Deathstalker agent is waiting in the hills above their camp for help. Borstan in Orgrimmar wants meat from the raptors at the dig in the highlands."
L["So there's an alchemist in Menethil Harbor, Caitlin Grassman, whose husband climbs mountains to pick her herbs. When a dig crew came through talking about towering grass in the highlands, he went to see it and stayed gone.\n\nDorin Songblade, the armorer in Lakeshire, had a brother up in those hills with diggers from Loch Modan. Dorin would have gone along if not for a pile of girdles to refit. His brother always wrote, and this time he hadn't.\n\nThe dig was in shambles after a run of accidents. Caitlin's husband was alive and very glad to see me. Dorin's brother was in a tent, dead. He had Dorin's face, and DLS carved into the stock of his gun.\n\nFor the Greenwarden I brought back the root core of a Highland Horror. Something ancient was stirring under those hills, Rethiel said, and the diggers should stop digging for their own good."] = "So there's an alchemist in Menethil Harbor, Caitlin Grassman, whose husband climbs mountains to pick her herbs. When a dig crew came through talking about towering grass in the highlands, he went to see it and stayed gone.\n\nDorin Songblade, the armorer in Lakeshire, had a brother up in those hills with diggers from Loch Modan. Dorin would have gone along if not for a pile of girdles to refit. His brother always wrote, and this time he hadn't.\n\nThe dig was in shambles after a run of accidents. Caitlin's husband was alive and very glad to see me. Dorin's brother was in a tent, dead. He had Dorin's face, and DLS carved into the stock of his gun.\n\nFor the Greenwarden I brought back the root core of a Highland Horror. Something ancient was stirring under those hills, Rethiel said, and the diggers should stop digging for their own good."
L["Word reached Hammerfall that the Dragonmaw were planning a show in the Wetlands, the kind where a dragon is made to do as it's told. The Deathstalkers won't move on a rumor, so I met their agent in the hills above the camp. She asked if I was the courageous few and told me to keep my voice down.\n\nThe Dragonmaw at the dig thought they'd found a way back to power. I cleared out enough of them for the Deathstalkers to slip in and took a dispatch off one of their casters, which the agent snatched out of my hand. They were hoping to win over Rend. She called that a waste of effort and the news well worth the Dark Lady's time. I'm not to talk about the mission, so I'll stop there.\n\nBorstan in Orgrimmar got the raptor meat and wondered what those raptors had been eating to marble like that."] = "Word reached Hammerfall that the Dragonmaw were planning a show in the Wetlands, the kind where a dragon is made to do as it's told. The Deathstalkers won't move on a rumor, so I met their agent in the hills above the camp. She asked if I was the courageous few and told me to keep my voice down.\n\nThe Dragonmaw at the dig thought they'd found a way back to power. I cleared out enough of them for the Deathstalkers to slip in and took a dispatch off one of their casters, which the agent snatched out of my hand. They were hoping to win over Rend. She called that a waste of effort and the news well worth the Dark Lady's time. I'm not to talk about the mission, so I'll stop there.\n\nBorstan in Orgrimmar got the raptor meat and wondered what those raptors had been eating to marble like that."
L["Seeking Caitlin"] = "Seeking Caitlin"
L["Llana"] = "Llana"
L["Llana, who sells reagents in Astranaar, swaps notes on rare plants with an alchemist in Menethil Harbor. The alchemist's last letter said her husband had joined a dig that was turning up signs of some long-lost grass, and then said nothing more about it. So I sailed to the Wetlands to ask. Caitlin Grassman guessed Llana was wondering about the seeds she'd been promised, but she had a bad feeling about that dig herself."] = "Llana, who sells reagents in Astranaar, swaps notes on rare plants with an alchemist in Menethil Harbor. The alchemist's last letter said her husband had joined a dig that was turning up signs of some long-lost grass, and then said nothing more about it. So I sailed to the Wetlands to ask. Caitlin Grassman guessed Llana was wondering about the seeds she'd been promised, but she had a bad feeling about that dig herself."
