L["Fallen in the Fen"] = "Fallen in the Fen"
L["Daewyn Songblade"] = "Daewyn Songblade"
L["Old Light"] = "Old Light"
L["Something at the far end of the dig is worth carrying out, if you can get to it. Prospector Whelgar's excavation site in the Wetlands is close by, and the prospector will want a close look at whatever you bring."] = "Something at the far end of the dig is worth carrying out, if you can get to it. Prospector Whelgar's excavation site in the Wetlands is close by, and the prospector will want a close look at whatever you bring."
L["Something at the far end of the dig is worth carrying out, if you can get to it. The elders on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise know old things better than anyone, and will want to see it."] = "Something at the far end of the dig is worth carrying out, if you can get to it. The elders on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise know old things better than anyone, and will want to see it."
L["The stone machine at the far end of the dig left a piece of itself behind when it went down. It was made of something I'd never handled and threw light around like a kaleidoscope, so I took it to Whelgar's camp outside. The prospector was impressed I'd lived and wanted a good look at it.\n\nThe marks on it looked like titan work. A find like that belonged in the Hall of Explorers, Whelgar said, with the finder's name written in the museum catalogue. High Explorer Magellas admired the keepers' marks on it and wrote my name down. There's a catalogue in Ironforge with me in it now, right next to a rock."] = "The stone machine at the far end of the dig left a piece of itself behind when it went down. It was made of something I'd never handled and threw light around like a kaleidoscope, so I took it to Whelgar's camp outside. The prospector was impressed I'd lived and wanted a good look at it.\n\nThe marks on it looked like titan work. A find like that belonged in the Hall of Explorers, Whelgar said, with the finder's name written in the museum catalogue. High Explorer Magellas admired the keepers' marks on it and wrote my name down. There's a catalogue in Ironforge with me in it now, right next to a rock."
L["The stone machine at the far end of the dig left a shard of itself behind when it went down. It threw light around like a kaleidoscope and felt older than anything I'd ever held, and the people who know about old things live on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.\n\nBashana Runetotem called it fascinating, more than a carving, and sent me on to Muln Earthfury of the Earthen Ring, up on the Skywatcher Plateau. Muln said there were memories in its light, and that it had waited lifetimes to be understood. The Earthen Ring will look after it and study it, and pass on what it has to say once they can hear it."] = "The stone machine at the far end of the dig left a shard of itself behind when it went down. It threw light around like a kaleidoscope and felt older than anything I'd ever held, and the people who know about old things live on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.\n\nBashana Runetotem called it fascinating, more than a carving, and sent me on to Muln Earthfury of the Earthen Ring, up on the Skywatcher Plateau. Muln said there were memories in its light, and that it had waited lifetimes to be understood. The Earthen Ring will look after it and study it, and pass on what it has to say once they can hear it."
