L["the bridge before the Hall of Thanes, Old Ironforge, Ironforge"] = "the bridge before the Hall of Thanes, Old Ironforge, Ironforge"
L["Farsen's Watch"] = "Farsen's Watch"
L["Beldin Steelgrill at Steelgrill's Depot in Kharanos has heard about a fire burning on the high ground above Gol'Bolar Quarry, to the east. It's probably a harmless camp, and Beldin would still like someone to climb up and say hello, one way or the other."] = "Beldin Steelgrill at Steelgrill's Depot in Kharanos has heard about a fire burning on the high ground above Gol'Bolar Quarry, to the east. It's probably a harmless camp, and Beldin would still like someone to climb up and say hello, one way or the other."
L["The camp on the hill above Gol'Bolar Quarry belonged to Earthseer Farsen, a Wildhammer visiting from Aerie Peak, who greeted me like an old friend. Farsen had noticed Dark Irons creeping around Dun Morogh and, instead of explaining, lent me far sight. I floated over the hills for a while looking down at spies and troggs. There were more of them, Farsen said, than you can see from the sky.\n\nSo I went east to Ironband's Compound and dealt with the spies. One carried a map of tunnels that all met under Ironforge, marked in Dark Iron runes I couldn't read. Then the wind spoke to me in a dwarf's voice and said Farsen needed to see it.\n\nI took it back up the hill. The spies had been scouts, according to the earthseer, and the Dark Irons meant to break into the city's vaults. I was told to hurry."] = "The camp on the hill above Gol'Bolar Quarry belonged to Earthseer Farsen, a Wildhammer visiting from Aerie Peak, who greeted me like an old friend. Farsen had noticed Dark Irons creeping around Dun Morogh and, instead of explaining, lent me far sight. I floated over the hills for a while looking down at spies and troggs. There were more of them, Farsen said, than you can see from the sky.\n\nSo I went east to Ironband's Compound and dealt with the spies. One carried a map of tunnels that all met under Ironforge, marked in Dark Iron runes I couldn't read. Then the wind spoke to me in a dwarf's voice and said Farsen needed to see it.\n\nI took it back up the hill. The spies had been scouts, according to the earthseer, and the Dark Irons meant to break into the city's vaults. I was told to hurry."
L["Beldin Steelgrill in Kharanos had heard from a mountaineer about a fire up on the hills above Gol'Bolar Quarry. Probably nothing, Beldin said. If the campers were friendly, no harm done, and if they weren't, I'd know how to handle it."] = "Beldin Steelgrill in Kharanos had heard from a mountaineer about a fire up on the hills above Gol'Bolar Quarry. Probably nothing, Beldin said. If the campers were friendly, no harm done, and if they weren't, I'd know how to handle it."
L["Earthseer Farsen"] = "Earthseer Farsen"
L["Nip 'Em in the Bud"] = "Nip 'Em in the Bud"
L["Underground Map"] = "Underground Map"
L["the Dark Iron Spies, Ironband's Compound, Dun Morogh"] = "the Dark Iron Spies, Ironband's Compound, Dun Morogh"
L["The Hall of Thanes"] = "The Hall of Thanes"
L["Earthseer Farsen is sure the Dark Irons are after Ironforge's vaults, and their map's tunnels meet in the Hall of Thanes, beneath the High Seat. Take friends and get there first. King Magni, an old friend of Farsen's, will want a report."] = "Earthseer Farsen is sure the Dark Irons are after Ironforge's vaults, and their map's tunnels meet in the Hall of Thanes, beneath the High Seat. Take friends and get there first. King Magni, an old friend of Farsen's, will want a report."
L["Off the High Seat, past a lot of cobwebs and a fair bit of lava, is the Hall of Thanes, where Ironforge keeps its old lords. Lorekeeper Afadra Dunwall had work to do down there and no patience for ghosts. Something had woken the dead, and I was to settle them.\n\nMost of them were just angry. One was polite. A ghostly attendant begged me to help Faldrim Anvilmar, the thane, who couldn't rest for an old grudge. Faldrim had no interest in resting. My friends and I insisted.\n\nI brought the Dark Iron commander's head up to King Magni, with the earthseer's regards, along with a tablet I'd found behind a vault door. It was the treaty that ended the War of the Three Hammers. Magni pointed out that the Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers both signed it, and the Dark Irons never did."] = "Off the High Seat, past a lot of cobwebs and a fair bit of lava, is the Hall of Thanes, where Ironforge keeps its old lords. Lorekeeper Afadra Dunwall had work to do down there and no patience for ghosts. Something had woken the dead, and I was to settle them.\n\nMost of them were just angry. One was polite. A ghostly attendant begged me to help Faldrim Anvilmar, the thane, who couldn't rest for an old grudge. Faldrim had no interest in resting. My friends and I insisted.\n\nI brought the Dark Iron commander's head up to King Magni, with the earthseer's regards, along with a tablet I'd found behind a vault door. It was the treaty that ended the War of the Three Hammers. Magni pointed out that the Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers both signed it, and the Dark Irons never did."
L["Old Ironforge Incursion"] = "Old Ironforge Incursion"
L["Afadra Dunwall"] = "Afadra Dunwall"
L["Important Heirlooms"] = "Important Heirlooms"
L["Thom Filch"] = "Thom Filch"
L["Thom Filch, a gnome by the bridge, claimed to have been patrolling the vaults when the Dark Irons came up from below in mole machines and left valuables lying about. Important cultural heirlooms, Thom called them, rubbing both hands together, and every one would be catalogued and returned to its proper place. I collected eight. Thom paid as promised, and afterward I found I was better thought of in Gadgetzan, which is a long way from Ironforge."] = "Thom Filch, a gnome by the bridge, claimed to have been patrolling the vaults when the Dark Irons came up from below in mole machines and left valuables lying about. Important cultural heirlooms, Thom called them, rubbing both hands together, and every one would be catalogued and returned to its proper place. I collected eight. Thom paid as promised, and afterward I found I was better thought of in Gadgetzan, which is a long way from Ironforge."
L["Ghostly Attendant"] = "Ghostly Attendant"
L["the Hall of Thanes, Ironforge"] = "the Hall of Thanes, Ironforge"
L["The Treaty of Understanding"] = "The Treaty of Understanding"
L["the Reliquary of Kings, the Hall of Thanes"] = "the Reliquary of Kings, the Hall of Thanes"
L["Blackfathom Villainy"] = "Blackfathom Villainy"
L["On Ashenvale's Zoram Strand, the ruins of an old night elf temple run down under the sea. The naga have moved into its flooded halls, and the rumors say they aren't alone down there.\n\nThe Argent Dawn wants to know what is going on in Blackfathom Deeps, and so does the Earthen Ring. Both could use someone willing to go in and look."] = "On Ashenvale's Zoram Strand, the ruins of an old night elf temple run down under the sea. The naga have moved into its flooded halls, and the rumors say they aren't alone down there.\n\nThe Argent Dawn wants to know what is going on in Blackfathom Deeps, and so does the Earthen Ring. Both could use someone willing to go in and look."
L["Rumors have reached Darnassus that the naga in Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned temple on the coast of Ashenvale, have joined forces with the Twilight's Hammer. The Argent Dawn sent a scout to look into it weeks ago and is still waiting for a report.\n\nStart with Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, at the Argent Dawn's embassy in Darnassus. Ironforge and Auberdine each have an errand down there as well."] = "Rumors have reached Darnassus that the naga in Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned temple on the coast of Ashenvale, have joined forces with the Twilight's Hammer. The Argent Dawn sent a scout to look into it weeks ago and is still waiting for a report.\n\nStart with Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, at the Argent Dawn's embassy in Darnassus. Ironforge and Auberdine each have an errand down there as well."
L["At Zoram'gar Outpost, on the coast of Ashenvale, Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needs help. A little way up the strand lies Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned temple full of naga, and the naga have been prying crystals out of its walls. Je'neu would like to know why.\n\nTsunaman, at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, can send you on your way."] = "At Zoram'gar Outpost, on the coast of Ashenvale, Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needs help. A little way up the strand lies Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned temple full of naga, and the naga have been prying crystals out of its walls. Je'neu would like to know why.\n\nTsunaman, at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, can send you on your way."
L["Ashenvale / Darnassus / Stonetalon Mountains / Thunder Bluff / Blackfathom Deeps"] = "Ashenvale / Darnassus / Stonetalon Mountains / Thunder Bluff / Blackfathom Deeps"
L["Blackfathom Deeps"] = "Blackfathom Deeps"
L["Trouble in the Deeps"] = "Trouble in the Deeps"
L["Tsunaman"] = "Tsunaman"
L["Sun Rock Retreat, Stonetalon Mountains"] = "Sun Rock Retreat, Stonetalon Mountains"
L["Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale"] = "Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale"
L["the Argent Dawn's embassy, Craftsmen's Terrace, Darnassus"] = "the Argent Dawn's embassy, Craftsmen's Terrace, Darnassus"
L["inside Blackfathom Deeps, Zoram Strand, Ashenvale"] = "inside Blackfathom Deeps, Zoram Strand, Ashenvale"
L["Tsunaman, at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, has word that Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needs help. Je'neu is at Zoram'gar Outpost, far off on the western shore of Ashenvale, where the Horde isn't especially welcome."] = "Tsunaman, at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains, has word that Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needs help. Je'neu is at Zoram'gar Outpost, far off on the western shore of Ashenvale, where the Horde isn't especially welcome."
L["Tsunaman, up at Sun Rock Retreat, had word that Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needed help on the coast of Ashenvale, and gave me directions to match. Through Windshear Crag or north through the Barrens, then west across the forest until it runs out at the sea. I was also told to be careful, which for the Horde in Ashenvale goes without saying.\n\nZoram'gar Outpost is a small camp on the Zoram Strand. Je'neu was there and pleased that Tsunaman had sent help. We had matters to discuss, he said, and most of them were up the beach in Blackfathom Deeps."] = "Tsunaman, up at Sun Rock Retreat, had word that Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring needed help on the coast of Ashenvale, and gave me directions to match. Through Windshear Crag or north through the Barrens, then west across the forest until it runs out at the sea. I was also told to be careful, which for the Horde in Ashenvale goes without saying.\n\nZoram'gar Outpost is a small camp on the Zoram Strand. Je'neu was there and pleased that Tsunaman had sent help. We had matters to discuss, he said, and most of them were up the beach in Blackfathom Deeps."
L["Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, at the Argent Dawn's embassy in Darnassus, sent a scout to Blackfathom Deeps weeks ago and is still waiting for a report. Argent Guard Manados, at the same embassy, wants the Twilight's Hammer down there paid a visit."] = "Dawnwatcher Shaedlass, at the Argent Dawn's embassy in Darnassus, sent a scout to Blackfathom Deeps weeks ago and is still waiting for a report. Argent Guard Manados, at the same embassy, wants the Twilight's Hammer down there paid a visit."
L["Je'neu Sancrea, at Zoram'gar Outpost, has heard that the naga of Blackfathom Deeps are prying sapphires off the walls of its first tunnels, and would rather they stopped. The Deeps lie a short way north along the Zoram Strand."] = "Je'neu Sancrea, at Zoram'gar Outpost, has heard that the naga of Blackfathom Deeps are prying sapphires off the walls of its first tunnels, and would rather they stopped. The Deeps lie a short way north along the Zoram Strand."
L["The Argent Dawn keeps an embassy in Darnassus, and one of its Dawnwatchers, Shaedlass, had mislaid a scout. Thaelrid had gone to Blackfathom Deeps weeks before to look into the naga and the Twilight's Hammer and hadn't reported back. A guard standing nearby asked me to bring back some cultists' pendants while I was at it.\n\nI found Thaelrid far inside, alive and out of strength. The place had been a temple of Elune, Thaelrid said, until the corruption of an Old God seeped up into its moonwell and the Old God's servant rose out of the water. Now the cult and the naga held it together, and the cult's leader, Kelris, was sacrificing innocents to that servant for power.\n\nI took the head of Kelris back to Darnassus. The Argent Dawn had long since put him down as dead or missing, and I'd made half of that true."] = "The Argent Dawn keeps an embassy in Darnassus, and one of its Dawnwatchers, Shaedlass, had mislaid a scout. Thaelrid had gone to Blackfathom Deeps weeks before to look into the naga and the Twilight's Hammer and hadn't reported back. A guard standing nearby asked me to bring back some cultists' pendants while I was at it.\n\nI found Thaelrid far inside, alive and out of strength. The place had been a temple of Elune, Thaelrid said, until the corruption of an Old God seeped up into its moonwell and the Old God's servant rose out of the water. Now the cult and the naga held it together, and the cult's leader, Kelris, was sacrificing innocents to that servant for power.\n\nI took the head of Kelris back to Darnassus. The Argent Dawn had long since put him down as dead or missing, and I'd made half of that true."
L["Je'neu Sancrea started me off just inside the Deeps, where the naga had been prying sapphires off the cave walls. I pried them off first. Je'neu could feel water spirits clinging to them, and wanted a fathom core from the flooded ruins too.\n\nIn the Deeps I also came by a damp note in very poor handwriting. All the priestesses were to bring the crystals to whoever wrote it, and with their power, one day, the world would return to the rule of the Old Gods. The note gave Je'neu a name to go with the trouble, Lorgus Jett of the Twilight's Hammer. I found Lorgus in the Deeps, and that was the end of that plan.\n\nFurther in, an Argent Dawn guard who could barely stand asked me to take the head of the cult's leader, Kelris, to Thunder Bluff. I did, and the tauren there were thoroughly disgusted with him."] = "Je'neu Sancrea started me off just inside the Deeps, where the naga had been prying sapphires off the cave walls. I pried them off first. Je'neu could feel water spirits clinging to them, and wanted a fathom core from the flooded ruins too.\n\nIn the Deeps I also came by a damp note in very poor handwriting. All the priestesses were to bring the crystals to whoever wrote it, and with their power, one day, the world would return to the rule of the Old Gods. The note gave Je'neu a name to go with the trouble, Lorgus Jett of the Twilight's Hammer. I found Lorgus in the Deeps, and that was the end of that plan.\n\nFurther in, an Argent Dawn guard who could barely stand asked me to take the head of the cult's leader, Kelris, to Thunder Bluff. I did, and the tauren there were thoroughly disgusted with him."
