L["Save Techbot's Brain!"] = "Save Techbot's Brain!"
L["Tinkmaster Overspark built Techbot to help out around Gnomeregan, and when the city fell a stray spark flipped its positronic brain to negatronic, so every kind habit it had now runs backwards. I brought Overspark its memory core. Overspark told the core not to feel bad, promised to have it fixed, and went looking for the plug to a hydro-jack swivel spanner."] = "Tinkmaster Overspark built Techbot to help out around Gnomeregan, and when the city fell a stray spark flipped its positronic brain to negatronic, so every kind habit it had now runs backwards. I brought Overspark its memory core. Overspark told the core not to feel bad, promised to have it fixed, and went looking for the plug to a hydro-jack swivel spanner."
L["Klockmort's Essentials"] = "Klockmort's Essentials"
L["Mathiel"] = "Mathiel"
L["Essential Artificials"] = "Essential Artificials"
L["Klockmort Spannerspan"] = "Klockmort Spannerspan"
L["In the rush out of Gnomeregan, the gnomes left behind every last essential artificial, a little part their tinkers and smiths used in nearly everything. Klockmort Spannerspan in Tinker Town needed a dozen for some new experiments, and they were deep in the city, shut up in things called artificial extrapolators. I opened enough of them. Klockmort said my bravery had moved gnomish research forward by a leap and a bound."] = "In the rush out of Gnomeregan, the gnomes left behind every last essential artificial, a little part their tinkers and smiths used in nearly everything. Klockmort Spannerspan in Tinker Town needed a dozen for some new experiments, and they were deep in the city, shut up in things called artificial extrapolators. I opened enough of them. Klockmort said my bravery had moved gnomish research forward by a leap and a bound."
L["Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"] = "Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"
L["Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind had a whole fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators to get to Dun Morogh and nowhere near enough parts. By Shoni's account the robots in Gnomeregan roam about like cattle on an open range, so I went and rounded up two dozen sets of robo-mechanical guts. Shoni was pleased. That was one excavationator fixed, with 398 to go."] = "Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind had a whole fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators to get to Dun Morogh and nowhere near enough parts. By Shoni's account the robots in Gnomeregan roam about like cattle on an open range, so I went and rounded up two dozen sets of robo-mechanical guts. Shoni was pleased. That was one excavationator fixed, with 398 to go."
L["Castpipe's Task"] = "Castpipe's Task"
L["Gaxim Rustfizzle"] = "Gaxim Rustfizzle"
L["Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon, a proud member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, sent me to Ironforge to help Master Mechanic Castpipe. Castpipe wasn't in the Assembly, Gaxim conceded, but was smart enough that the job had an eighty-four percent chance of being important. Good odds, by Gaxim's reckoning."] = "Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon, a proud member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, sent me to Ironforge to help Master Mechanic Castpipe. Castpipe wasn't in the Assembly, Gaxim conceded, but was smart enough that the job had an eighty-four percent chance of being important. Good odds, by Gaxim's reckoning."
L["Data Rescue"] = "Data Rescue"
L["Master Mechanic Castpipe"] = "Master Mechanic Castpipe"
L["Master Mechanic Castpipe had left a great deal of data behind in Gnomeregan and wanted one piece of it back, on a prismatic punch card from a Matrix Punchograph 3005-D deep in the city. Getting into that terminal meant clearance from the lesser ones, and each of those wanted a punch card the gnomes had also left behind. I worked my way up from white to prismatic. Castpipe called the data immeasurably important and said my service would be long remembered. I couldn't tell you what was on it."] = "Master Mechanic Castpipe had left a great deal of data behind in Gnomeregan and wanted one piece of it back, on a prismatic punch card from a Matrix Punchograph 3005-D deep in the city. Getting into that terminal meant clearance from the lesser ones, and each of those wanted a punch card the gnomes had also left behind. I worked my way up from white to prismatic. Castpipe called the data immeasurably important and said my service would be long remembered. I couldn't tell you what was on it."
L["A Fine Mess"] = "A Fine Mess"
L["Kernobee"] = "Kernobee"
L["Kernobee woke up among the troggs, where some Dark Iron dwarves had thrown the poor wretch after a beating, and wanted out. I led the way to the Clockwerk Run exit, and from there Kernobee made for Ratchet with word that the Dark Irons had a hand in that super rig. Telling Scooty in Booty Bay was my part. Scooty rewarded me, a touch grudgingly, with gear meant to help against that good-for-nothing backstabber Thermaplugg."] = "Kernobee woke up among the troggs, where some Dark Iron dwarves had thrown the poor wretch after a beating, and wanted out. I led the way to the Clockwerk Run exit, and from there Kernobee made for Ratchet with word that the Dark Irons had a hand in that super rig. Telling Scooty in Booty Bay was my part. Scooty rewarded me, a touch grudgingly, with gear meant to help against that good-for-nothing backstabber Thermaplugg."
L["Grime-Encrusted Ring"] = "Grime-Encrusted Ring"
L["One of the Dark Iron dwarves in Gnomeregan was carrying a ring so caked in grime that I couldn't tell what it was made of, though something under there had a gleam. The gnomes holding out in the city have a machine for exactly that, the Sparklematic 5200. I put the ring in and paid. It ground and jerked about so violently I worried for it, then stopped with a cheerful ding and opened to show a small box tied with a red bow. It gift wraps, too."] = "One of the Dark Iron dwarves in Gnomeregan was carrying a ring so caked in grime that I couldn't tell what it was made of, though something under there had a gleam. The gnomes holding out in the city have a machine for exactly that, the Sparklematic 5200. I put the ring in and paid. It ground and jerked about so violently I worried for it, then stopped with a cheerful ding and opened to show a small box tied with a red bow. It gift wraps, too."
L["The Sparklematic 5200!"] = "The Sparklematic 5200!"
L["The Sparklematic 5200"] = "The Sparklematic 5200"
L["the Clean Zone, Gnomeregan"] = "the Clean Zone, Gnomeregan"
L["The plaque on the Sparklematic 5200 promises to put the shine back in shine-tastic, for three silver a go. I had a grime-encrusted find of my own from the city, so in it went with the coins. The machine surged to life, and its frame groaned as it lurched from side to side, as if it meant to wander off with my valuables."] = "The plaque on the Sparklematic 5200 promises to put the shine back in shine-tastic, for three silver a go. I had a grime-encrusted find of my own from the city, so in it went with the coins. The machine surged to life, and its frame groaned as it lurched from side to side, as if it meant to wander off with my valuables."
L["Return of the Ring"] = "Return of the Ring"
L["Inside the band of the cleaned ring were the seal of Ironforge and the initials TdK, which led me to Talvash del Kissel in the Mystic Ward. He knew it at once. He'd made several like it in a little shop in Gnomeregan before the city went up, and this one might have belonged to someone who never got out. When I said a Dark Iron had been carrying it, Talvash reckoned that put a new layer of conspiracy on the nine already floating about, and that the authorities ought to hear."] = "Inside the band of the cleaned ring were the seal of Ironforge and the initials TdK, which led me to Talvash del Kissel in the Mystic Ward. He knew it at once. He'd made several like it in a little shop in Gnomeregan before the city went up, and this one might have belonged to someone who never got out. When I said a Dark Iron had been carrying it, Talvash reckoned that put a new layer of conspiracy on the nine already floating about, and that the authorities ought to hear."
L["Gnome Improvement"] = "Gnome Improvement"
L["Talvash offered to improve the ring for thirty silver, which became thirty silver plus a silver bar and a moss agate, since his own stock had dried up. I brought them. He added a silver and agate lattice and swore he'd normally charge ten times as much. One day, once he's out of the hole he's unjustly in, he means to make the finest trinkets in Azeroth for everyone."] = "Talvash offered to improve the ring for thirty silver, which became thirty silver plus a silver bar and a moss agate, since his own stock had dried up. I brought them. He added a silver and agate lattice and swore he'd normally charge ten times as much. One day, once he's out of the hole he's unjustly in, he means to make the finest trinkets in Azeroth for everyone."
L["Inside the band of the cleaned ring were the seal of Orgrimmar and three letters still legible, NOG. I knew a Nogg in the Valley of Honor. It wasn't Nogg's ring, as it happened, but the Dark Iron part interested Nogg a great deal. Maybe, Nogg reckoned, the gnomes had stolen the Dark Irons' crazy golem plans to build that rig, and the Dark Irons would be wanting payback."] = "Inside the band of the cleaned ring were the seal of Orgrimmar and three letters still legible, NOG. I knew a Nogg in the Valley of Honor. It wasn't Nogg's ring, as it happened, but the Dark Iron part interested Nogg a great deal. Maybe, Nogg reckoned, the gnomes had stolen the Dark Irons' crazy golem plans to build that rig, and the Dark Irons would be wanting payback."
L["Nogg's Ring Redo"] = "Nogg's Ring Redo"
L["For the tip about the Dark Irons, Nogg offered to improve the ring, which was probably the simple work of some gnome. I brought the silver bar and moss agate Nogg asked for, plus thirty silver for the trouble, and got the ring back with a silver and agate lattice and more magic in it than before. Nogg reckoned the Dark Irons were a fair lead on how the gnomes had suddenly come down with goblin-like inspiration."] = "For the tip about the Dark Irons, Nogg offered to improve the ring, which was probably the simple work of some gnome. I brought the silver bar and moss agate Nogg asked for, plus thirty silver for the trouble, and got the ring back with a silver and agate lattice and more magic in it than before. Nogg reckoned the Dark Irons were a fair lead on how the gnomes had suddenly come down with goblin-like inspiration."
L["Hidden Enemies"] = "Hidden Enemies"
L["Thrall will not tolerate traitors in Orgrimmar, and he is sure there are some. The Burning Blade, an old demon-worshipping cult of the orcs, still keeps a cave in Durotar, and the Warchief suspects its reach goes much further into his city.\n\nHis own agents would be recognized, so he wants a new face for the work. Start in Grommash Hold, and follow the trail out to Skull Rock and down beneath the city into Ragefire Chasm."] = "Thrall will not tolerate traitors in Orgrimmar, and he is sure there are some. The Burning Blade, an old demon-worshipping cult of the orcs, still keeps a cave in Durotar, and the Warchief suspects its reach goes much further into his city.\n\nHis own agents would be recognized, so he wants a new face for the work. Start in Grommash Hold, and follow the trail out to Skull Rock and down beneath the city into Ragefire Chasm."
L["Orgrimmar / Durotar / Thunder Bluff / Undercity / Ragefire Chasm"] = "Orgrimmar / Durotar / Thunder Bluff / Undercity / Ragefire Chasm"
L["Ragefire Chasm"] = "Ragefire Chasm"
L["Skull Rock"] = "Skull Rock"
L["Thrall suspects there are traitors in Orgrimmar, and he'd rather not show his hand by sending agents they already know. He wants a new face for the job. Find the Warchief in Grommash Hold, where he has an errand for you at Skull Rock."] = "Thrall suspects there are traitors in Orgrimmar, and he'd rather not show his hand by sending agents they already know. He wants a new face for the job. Find the Warchief in Grommash Hold, where he has an errand for you at Skull Rock."
L["Thrall knows there are traitors in Orgrimmar, and he wanted a face the cult had never seen. I was young and unknown, which for once counted in my favor.\n\nThe Burning Blade keep a cave at Skull Rock, where one of them carried a small rune that marks a lieutenant. I brought it to Thrall, who said I reminded him of himself when he was younger.\n\nNext the rune went to Neeru Fireblade, a warlock in the Cleft of Shadow. Thrall knows Neeru leads the cult and leaves him in place on purpose. Neeru welcomed me in, his ranks growing too fast for him to remember faces, and called Thrall a fool. He sends Thrall's people into the chasm under the city against the Searing Blade, he said, which kills off Thrall's followers and tests the cultists. Two of the Searing Blade's leaders were the ones he valued.\n\nThrall wanted every word of it."] = "Thrall knows there are traitors in Orgrimmar, and he wanted a face the cult had never seen. I was young and unknown, which for once counted in my favor.\n\nThe Burning Blade keep a cave at Skull Rock, where one of them carried a small rune that marks a lieutenant. I brought it to Thrall, who said I reminded him of himself when he was younger.\n\nNext the rune went to Neeru Fireblade, a warlock in the Cleft of Shadow. Thrall knows Neeru leads the cult and leaves him in place on purpose. Neeru welcomed me in, his ranks growing too fast for him to remember faces, and called Thrall a fool. He sends Thrall's people into the chasm under the city against the Searing Blade, he said, which kills off Thrall's followers and tests the cultists. Two of the Searing Blade's leaders were the ones he valued.\n\nThrall wanted every word of it."
L["The Lieutenant's Insignia"] = "The Lieutenant's Insignia"
L["Neeru's Reaction"] = "Neeru's Reaction"
L["Thrall, in Grommash Hold, wants two leaders of the Searing Blade killed in Ragefire Chasm, under the Cleft of Shadow, without anyone in the Cleft finding out who did it. Rahauro in Thunder Bluff and Varimathras in the Undercity have business in the chasm too."] = "Thrall, in Grommash Hold, wants two leaders of the Searing Blade killed in Ragefire Chasm, under the Cleft of Shadow, without anyone in the Cleft finding out who did it. Rahauro in Thunder Bluff and Varimathras in the Undercity have business in the chasm too."
L["Neeru had let slip which two of the Searing Blade he valued, and Thrall decided they would go first. One was a satyr. The other was Jergosh, and Thrall had to stop and think what Jergosh was. A warlock, he believed. In Ragefire Chasm that narrows it down very little.\n\nThe way into the chasm is in the Cleft of Shadow, a short walk from Neeru's door, and Neeru was not to learn who had done it. So I strolled past his door on my way to kill his two favorites, doing my best impression of a lieutenant on cult business.\n\nBoth died down there. Back in Grommash Hold, Thrall's people had already told him the caverns were in disarray and Neeru was more than agitated. Thrall allowed that he wasn't displeased, and called it a dent in Neeru's armor."] = "Neeru had let slip which two of the Searing Blade he valued, and Thrall decided they would go first. One was a satyr. The other was Jergosh, and Thrall had to stop and think what Jergosh was. A warlock, he believed. In Ragefire Chasm that narrows it down very little.\n\nThe way into the chasm is in the Cleft of Shadow, a short walk from Neeru's door, and Neeru was not to learn who had done it. So I strolled past his door on my way to kill his two favorites, doing my best impression of a lieutenant on cult business.\n\nBoth died down there. Back in Grommash Hold, Thrall's people had already told him the caverns were in disarray and Neeru was more than agitated. Thrall allowed that he wasn't displeased, and called it a dent in Neeru's armor."
L["Bazzalan and Jergosh"] = "Bazzalan and Jergosh"
L["Slaying the Beast"] = "Slaying the Beast"
L["Neeru Fireblade"] = "Neeru Fireblade"
L["Neeru Fireblade had a job of his own for me in the chasm. The Warchief, he explained, had charged him with rooting out the demonic influence in Orgrimmar, and the Burning Blade was only one of the threats. He kept a straight face the whole time. The Searing Blade answered to a felguard called Taragaman the Hungerer, and Neeru wanted the heart. I brought it, and Neeru promised to tell Thrall of my success himself."] = "Neeru Fireblade had a job of his own for me in the chasm. The Warchief, he explained, had charged him with rooting out the demonic influence in Orgrimmar, and the Burning Blade was only one of the threats. He kept a straight face the whole time. The Searing Blade answered to a felguard called Taragaman the Hungerer, and Neeru wanted the heart. I brought it, and Neeru promised to tell Thrall of my success himself."
L["Testing an Enemy's Strength"] = "Testing an Enemy's Strength"
L["Rahauro"] = "Rahauro"
L["Rahauro, on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, speaks for Magatha Grimtotem. Troggs had been coming up out of the lava tunnels under Orgrimmar, and Magatha, ever benevolent, had sent diplomats to make peace. The troggs killed them. The next envoy was me, and there are sixteen fewer troggs now, half of them shamans. Rahauro said it might be worth finding out someday what the troggs actually want."] = "Rahauro, on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, speaks for Magatha Grimtotem. Troggs had been coming up out of the lava tunnels under Orgrimmar, and Magatha, ever benevolent, had sent diplomats to make peace. The troggs killed them. The next envoy was me, and there are sixteen fewer troggs now, half of them shamans. Rahauro said it might be worth finding out someday what the troggs actually want."
L["Searching for the Lost Satchel"] = "Searching for the Lost Satchel"
L["Magatha had also lost one of her own in the chasm. Maur Grimtotem had found something peculiar down there while trying to talk to the troggs, and never came back up to show her what. I found what was left of him. Clubs or fists, by the look of it. The troggs hadn't taken a thing he carried, having no interest in property that I could see."] = "Magatha had also lost one of her own in the chasm. Maur Grimtotem had found something peculiar down there while trying to talk to the troggs, and never came back up to show her what. I found what was left of him. Clubs or fists, by the look of it. The troggs hadn't taken a thing he carried, having no interest in property that I could see."
L["Returning the Lost Satchel"] = "Returning the Lost Satchel"
L["Maur Grimtotem"] = "Maur Grimtotem"
L["Maur still had a satchel gripped tight in both arms, as if he'd spent the whole beating protecting it. I got it loose and carried it up to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff. Magatha had left word that whoever found her clansman should be rewarded, and Rahauro saw to it."] = "Maur still had a satchel gripped tight in both arms, as if he'd spent the whole beating protecting it. I got it loose and carried it up to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff. Magatha had left word that whoever found her clansman should be rewarded, and Rahauro saw to it."
L["The Power to Destroy..."] = "The Power to Destroy..."
L["Varimathras, in the Undercity's Royal Quarter, explained that the Legion likes to give its followers gifts, and that the Dark Lady feels some of them would be better off in her hands. The Searing Blade had two spellbooks she wished to borrow. Varimathras made the quotation marks around borrow quite audible. I brought back Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether, and the Searing Blade shouldn't expect either one back."] = "Varimathras, in the Undercity's Royal Quarter, explained that the Legion likes to give its followers gifts, and that the Dark Lady feels some of them would be better off in her hands. The Searing Blade had two spellbooks she wished to borrow. Varimathras made the quotation marks around borrow quite audible. I brought back Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether, and the Searing Blade shouldn't expect either one back."
L["Word from Ragefire Chasm has reached the Cleft of Shadow, and Neeru Fireblade is said to be in a foul temper. Thrall, in Grommash Hold, sees a chance to put you closer to Neeru while the warlock is rattled."] = "Word from Ragefire Chasm has reached the Cleft of Shadow, and Neeru Fireblade is said to be in a foul temper. Thrall, in Grommash Hold, sees a chance to put you closer to Neeru while the warlock is rattled."
L["Thrall wanted me closer to Neeru while Neeru was rattled. With two of his leaders dead he might be short of help, and Thrall hoped he'd ask me for some. I was to go back to the Cleft and not be too obvious about it.\n\nNeeru snapped at me before he saw who it was, then apologized. His anger, he said, rivaled a rabid kodo bull's. Some of Thrall's do-gooders had caught his leaders unaware, and he blamed himself for sending travelers down there at all. I kept my face very still.\n\nThen he named me one of his lieutenants. The chasm was mostly a loss now, but his agents in the Barrens and Ashenvale would start on something new. Thrall hadn't heard of the Shadow Council in Ashenvale and put his spies on it.\n\nBoth of them said they'd call on me soon. I'm hoping they don't pick the same day."] = "Thrall wanted me closer to Neeru while Neeru was rattled. With two of his leaders dead he might be short of help, and Thrall hoped he'd ask me for some. I was to go back to the Cleft and not be too obvious about it.\n\nNeeru snapped at me before he saw who it was, then apologized. His anger, he said, rivaled a rabid kodo bull's. Some of Thrall's do-gooders had caught his leaders unaware, and he blamed himself for sending travelers down there at all. I kept my face very still.\n\nThen he named me one of his lieutenants. The chasm was mostly a loss now, but his agents in the Barrens and Ashenvale would start on something new. Thrall hadn't heard of the Shadow Council in Ashenvale and put his spies on it.\n\nBoth of them said they'd call on me soon. I'm hoping they don't pick the same day."
L["Return to Neeru"] = "Return to Neeru"
L["Report to Thrall"] = "Report to Thrall"
L["Thorns of the Razorfen"] = "Thorns of the Razorfen"
L["In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns. In Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army, and she has made enemies a long way from the Barrens.\n\nStart in the Kraul. When it's done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."] = "In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns. In Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army, and she has made enemies a long way from the Barrens.\n\nStart in the Kraul. When it's done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."
L["In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns, and in Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army. Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet has a job in there, and you'll find other reasons once you're inside.\n\nWhen the Kraul is done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."] = "In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns, and in Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army. Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet has a job in there, and you'll find other reasons once you're inside.\n\nWhen the Kraul is done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."
L["In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns, and in Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army. Auld Stonespire, in Thunder Bluff, would like her heart.\n\nWhen the Kraul is done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."] = "In the far south of the Barrens, the quilboar of the Razorfen live in warrens of giant thorns, and in Razorfen Kraul their crone, Charlga Razorflank, is raising an army. Auld Stonespire, in Thunder Bluff, would like her heart.\n\nWhen the Kraul is done with, follow the thorns further south to Razorfen Downs, where the quilboar have been keeping strange company."
L["The Barrens / Feralas / Thunder Bluff / Undercity / Stormwind / Razorfen Kraul / Razorfen Downs"] = "The Barrens / Feralas / Thunder Bluff / Undercity / Stormwind / Razorfen Kraul / Razorfen Downs"
L["Razorfen Kraul"] = "Razorfen Kraul"
L["Blueleaf Tubers"] = "Blueleaf Tubers"
L["the Lower Rise, Thunder Bluff"] = "the Lower Rise, Thunder Bluff"
L["the Tradesmen's Terrace, Darnassus"] = "the Tradesmen's Terrace, Darnassus"
L["a hill outside Razorfen Downs, The Barrens"] = "a hill outside Razorfen Downs, The Barrens"
L["the Magic Quarter, Undercity"] = "the Magic Quarter, Undercity"
L["The Crone of the Kraul"] = "The Crone of the Kraul"
L["The quilboar of the Razorfen have grown a warren of giant thorns in the southern Barrens, Razorfen Kraul, and they don't welcome visitors. Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet wants some tubers dug up in there all the same, and has a gopher to lend for it."] = "The quilboar of the Razorfen have grown a warren of giant thorns in the southern Barrens, Razorfen Kraul, and they don't welcome visitors. Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet wants some tubers dug up in there all the same, and has a gopher to lend for it."
L["Auld Stonespire, on the Lower Rise in Thunder Bluff, remembers when the tauren lived in the southern Barrens, and holds a grudge against the crone who rules Razorfen Kraul there now. In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix has a smaller job in the same thorns."] = "Auld Stonespire, on the Lower Rise in Thunder Bluff, remembers when the tauren lived in the southern Barrens, and holds a grudge against the crone who rules Razorfen Kraul there now. In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix has a smaller job in the same thorns."
L["Somewhere in Razorfen Kraul I picked up the journal of a dwarf named Henrig Lonebrow, who had no further use for it. I took it to Falfindel Waywarder at Thalanaar, on the Feralas border. Falfindel mourned a brave soul and then got down to business.\n\nThe crone who rules the Kraul, Charlga Razorflank, was raising an army in there, and there wasn't time to send to Darnassus for help. Falfindel wanted her medallion as proof she was finished.\n\nSo back into the thorns I went. Charlga kept a great many quilboar between herself and the door, and the medallion came away with me in the end. Falfindel was glad the Alliance could get on with its work there, and started wondering aloud whether treachery had a hand in the rot in that ground. I left Falfindel to it."] = "Somewhere in Razorfen Kraul I picked up the journal of a dwarf named Henrig Lonebrow, who had no further use for it. I took it to Falfindel Waywarder at Thalanaar, on the Feralas border. Falfindel mourned a brave soul and then got down to business.\n\nThe crone who rules the Kraul, Charlga Razorflank, was raising an army in there, and there wasn't time to send to Darnassus for help. Falfindel wanted her medallion as proof she was finished.\n\nSo back into the thorns I went. Charlga kept a great many quilboar between herself and the door, and the medallion came away with me in the end. Falfindel was glad the Alliance could get on with its work there, and started wondering aloud whether treachery had a hand in the rot in that ground. I left Falfindel to it."
L["Auld Stonespire in Thunder Bluff has a long memory. The tauren lived on holy land in the southern Barrens for decades before they were driven out, and Auld has never forgiven it. These days the crone Charlga Razorflank rules down there from Razorfen Kraul and is raising an army. Auld wanted her heart, and said it would be enough to die in peace.\n\nThe Kraul is a maze of thorns as thick as tree trunks, full of quilboar who seemed to know what I'd come for, and Charlga was at the far end of it.\n\nI carried the heart back to Thunder Bluff. Auld was satisfied that the Razorfen finally knew what the tauren had felt. Driving a people from holy ground, Auld told me, is a sin that earns its vengeance. Then came the thanks, very solemn, with the heart still in Auld's hand."] = "Auld Stonespire in Thunder Bluff has a long memory. The tauren lived on holy land in the southern Barrens for decades before they were driven out, and Auld has never forgiven it. These days the crone Charlga Razorflank rules down there from Razorfen Kraul and is raising an army. Auld wanted her heart, and said it would be enough to die in peace.\n\nThe Kraul is a maze of thorns as thick as tree trunks, full of quilboar who seemed to know what I'd come for, and Charlga was at the far end of it.\n\nI carried the heart back to Thunder Bluff. Auld was satisfied that the Razorfen finally knew what the tauren had felt. Driving a people from holy ground, Auld told me, is a sin that earns its vengeance. Then came the thanks, very solemn, with the heart still in Auld's hand."
L["Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet sent me into Razorfen Kraul with a crate full of holes and an owner's manual I was told to read first, so I read it. Out of the crate came a snufflenose gopher, and a poke with the command stick set it rooting for blueleaf tubers while I kept the quilboar off it. Mebok wanted the crate and the stick back along with the six tubers, and got all of it."] = "Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet sent me into Razorfen Kraul with a crate full of holes and an owner's manual I was told to read first, so I read it. Out of the crate came a snufflenose gopher, and a poke with the command stick set it rooting for blueleaf tubers while I kept the quilboar off it. Mebok wanted the crate and the stick back along with the six tubers, and got all of it."
L["A Vengeful Fate"] = "A Vengeful Fate"
L["Auld Stonespire"] = "Auld Stonespire"
L["Willix the Importer"] = "Willix the Importer"
L["near Charlga Razorflank, Razorfen Kraul"] = "near Charlga Razorflank, Razorfen Kraul"
L["Willix the Importer, a goblin, had gone into Razorfen Kraul after blueleaf tubers for Mebok Mizzyrix and ended up held in a tent not far from Charlga Razorflank. I walked Willix out. The whole way there was a running complaint about the quilboar and the smell, and warnings about trouble that tended to arrive at the same moment as the trouble. Outside, Willix thanked me and announced a good long rest before the trip back to Ratchet."] = "Willix the Importer, a goblin, had gone into Razorfen Kraul after blueleaf tubers for Mebok Mizzyrix and ended up held in a tent not far from Charlga Razorflank. I walked Willix out. The whole way there was a running complaint about the quilboar and the smell, and warnings about trouble that tended to arrive at the same moment as the trouble. Outside, Willix thanked me and announced a good long rest before the trip back to Ratchet."
L["Mortality Wanes"] = "Mortality Wanes"
L["Heralath Fallowbrook"] = "Heralath Fallowbrook"
L["Heralath Fallowbrook lay in the Kraul not far from Charlga Razorflank and didn't have long. A quilboar had taken the pendant Heralath shared with Treshala, Heralath's wife in Darnassus, and Heralath wanted it found and taken home to her with word of the death. I found it on one of the quilboar and carried both to the Tradesmen's Terrace. Treshala wouldn't believe it at first, then said the grief would be carried and Heralath's work would go on, and asked to be left alone to mourn. I went."] = "Heralath Fallowbrook lay in the Kraul not far from Charlga Razorflank and didn't have long. A quilboar had taken the pendant Heralath shared with Treshala, Heralath's wife in Darnassus, and Heralath wanted it found and taken home to her with word of the death. I found it on one of the quilboar and carried both to the Tradesmen's Terrace. Treshala wouldn't believe it at first, then said the grief would be carried and Heralath's work would go on, and asked to be left alone to mourn. I went."
L["Lonebrow's Journal"] = "Lonebrow's Journal"
L["Falfindel Waywarder"] = "Falfindel Waywarder"
L["A Host of Evil"] = "A Host of Evil"
L["Myriam Moonsinger keeps watch from a hill near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, at the bottom of the Barrens. A diplomat has set up outside the Downs and is drawing a crowd, and Myriam would like the crowd smaller."] = "Myriam Moonsinger keeps watch from a hill near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, at the bottom of the Barrens. A diplomat has set up outside the Downs and is drawing a crowd, and Myriam would like the crowd smaller."
L["Charlga Razorflank was carrying a small scroll under an insignia you don't recognize. Varimathras, in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, may know it. Near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, Myriam Moonsinger could use a hand with the crowd gathering there."] = "Charlga Razorflank was carrying a small scroll under an insignia you don't recognize. Varimathras, in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, may know it. Near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, Myriam Moonsinger could use a hand with the crowd gathering there."
L["Myriam Moonsinger had been sitting on a hill outside Razorfen Downs, keeping an eye on a diplomat. Ambassador Malcin, Myriam suspected, was Scourge, and handed out undeath to anyone who came asking for it. Plenty came. Every day more of them crept out of the briars to stand near the ambassador, quilboar and Death's Head cultists both, and Myriam was in no position to fight that many alone.\n\nI took eight of each kind off the crowd. Myriam thanked me and said that seeing the diplomat's power up close only proved the Scourge were among the worst threats Azeroth had ever faced. Then it was back to watching and studying, and I was pointed at the cave below the hill, the one shaped like a boar's mouth, with the suggestion that I take friends."] = "Myriam Moonsinger had been sitting on a hill outside Razorfen Downs, keeping an eye on a diplomat. Ambassador Malcin, Myriam suspected, was Scourge, and handed out undeath to anyone who came asking for it. Plenty came. Every day more of them crept out of the briars to stand near the ambassador, quilboar and Death's Head cultists both, and Myriam was in no position to fight that many alone.\n\nI took eight of each kind off the crowd. Myriam thanked me and said that seeing the diplomat's power up close only proved the Scourge were among the worst threats Azeroth had ever faced. Then it was back to watching and studying, and I was pointed at the cave below the hill, the one shaped like a boar's mouth, with the suggestion that I take friends."
L["The crone had been carrying a small scroll under an insignia I didn't recognize. Varimathras did. Down in the Royal Quarter, the dreadlord asked whether it had come off Charlga, who rules the Kraul.\n\nIt was a letter from Ambassador Malcin, a diplomat to Lordaeron before things changed and a servant of the Scourge since. The letter called Charlga My Lady and offered her the Barrens and more if the Scourge could do as it liked there, and Malcin would wait outside Razorfen Downs to talk it over. If the Scourge wanted a foothold in Kalimdor, Varimathras said, it fell to the Horde to answer.\n\nMalcin was waiting where the letter said, among quilboar and cultists hungry for the bargain. A watcher on the hill above wanted that crowd thinner, so I thinned it on the way through, and Malcin's head went back to the Undercity with me."] = "The crone had been carrying a small scroll under an insignia I didn't recognize. Varimathras did. Down in the Royal Quarter, the dreadlord asked whether it had come off Charlga, who rules the Kraul.\n\nIt was a letter from Ambassador Malcin, a diplomat to Lordaeron before things changed and a servant of the Scourge since. The letter called Charlga My Lady and offered her the Barrens and more if the Scourge could do as it liked there, and Malcin would wait outside Razorfen Downs to talk it over. If the Scourge wanted a foothold in Kalimdor, Varimathras said, it fell to the Horde to answer.\n\nMalcin was waiting where the letter said, among quilboar and cultists hungry for the bargain. A watcher on the hill above wanted that crowd thinner, so I thinned it on the way through, and Malcin's head went back to the Undercity with me."
L["An Unholy Alliance"] = "An Unholy Alliance"
L["Small Scroll"] = "Small Scroll"
L["Myriam Moonsinger"] = "Myriam Moonsinger"
L["Extinguishing the Idol"] = "Extinguishing the Idol"
L["Somewhere in Razorfen Downs, in a cage the Scourge haven't got round to emptying, a stranger named Belnistrasz is still alive and has a proposal for whoever reaches the cage first."] = "Somewhere in Razorfen Downs, in a cage the Scourge haven't got round to emptying, a stranger named Belnistrasz is still alive and has a proposal for whoever reaches the cage first."
L["Deep in Razorfen Downs, in a cage, I found Belnistrasz. The stranger had fully expected to die in there or end up as a meal for the Scourge, and was very glad to see me, as people in cages generally are. Home, I gathered, was a long way from the Barrens.\n\nBefore anything else, Belnistrasz handed me an oathstone. Among Belnistrasz's kind an agreement made over one of those is a serious bond, and to take the job I had to give it back. I gave it back.\n\nThe job was the quilboar idol. Belnistrasz meant to shut it down with a ritual, and a ritual means standing in one place for a long while as the whole of the Downs comes to object. I stood in front and objected back. When the ritual was done the idol was finished, and we wound things up at Belnistrasz's brazier."] = "Deep in Razorfen Downs, in a cage, I found Belnistrasz. The stranger had fully expected to die in there or end up as a meal for the Scourge, and was very glad to see me, as people in cages generally are. Home, I gathered, was a long way from the Barrens.\n\nBefore anything else, Belnistrasz handed me an oathstone. Among Belnistrasz's kind an agreement made over one of those is a serious bond, and to take the job I had to give it back. I gave it back.\n\nThe job was the quilboar idol. Belnistrasz meant to shut it down with a ritual, and a ritual means standing in one place for a long while as the whole of the Downs comes to object. I stood in front and objected back. When the ritual was done the idol was finished, and we wound things up at Belnistrasz's brazier."
L["Scourge of the Downs"] = "Scourge of the Downs"
L["Belnistrasz"] = "Belnistrasz"
L["a cage in Razorfen Downs"] = "a cage in Razorfen Downs"
L["The Coldbringer"] = "The Coldbringer"
L["Archbishop Benedictus, in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, has had grim reports out of Razorfen Downs and wants the power behind them put down. The archbishop is asking for volunteers willing to go all the way to the bottom."] = "Archbishop Benedictus, in the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind, has had grim reports out of Razorfen Downs and wants the power behind them put down. The archbishop is asking for volunteers willing to go all the way to the bottom."
L["Andrew Brownell, in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, has studied the master of Razorfen Downs closely enough to want the skull, and would like it fetched up from the very bottom of the Downs."] = "Andrew Brownell, in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, has studied the master of Razorfen Downs closely enough to want the skull, and would like it fetched up from the very bottom of the Downs."
L["Archbishop Benedictus had heard enough about Razorfen Downs. The quilboar there had made a pact with the Scourge, and the pact had bred things worse than either of them. Over all of it sat a lich called Amnennar the Coldbringer, and the archbishop wanted the union ended along with him.\n\nSo down I went, to the very bottom of the Downs, where Amnennar waited in a cold he seems to carry with him. It was a long fight and I did most of it with numb fingers. He went down in the end.\n\nBack at the Cathedral of Light, Benedictus thanked me and said the Scourge would think twice before trying to swell its ranks that way again. I left with the archbishop's blessing of the Light, which was warm, at least."] = "Archbishop Benedictus had heard enough about Razorfen Downs. The quilboar there had made a pact with the Scourge, and the pact had bred things worse than either of them. Over all of it sat a lich called Amnennar the Coldbringer, and the archbishop wanted the union ended along with him.\n\nSo down I went, to the very bottom of the Downs, where Amnennar waited in a cold he seems to carry with him. It was a long fight and I did most of it with numb fingers. He went down in the end.\n\nBack at the Cathedral of Light, Benedictus thanked me and said the Scourge would think twice before trying to swell its ranks that way again. I left with the archbishop's blessing of the Light, which was warm, at least."
L["Andrew Brownell, in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, laid out Razorfen Downs for me like a lecture. The quilboar there had thrown in with the Scourge, and the lich who ruled them, Amnennar the Coldbringer, moved them about with his mind. He also had a line straight to Ner'zhul. Brownell wanted that line cut, and the skull brought back to show for it.\n\nThe bottom of the Downs was colder than anything in the Barrens has a right to be, and Amnennar did his best to keep it that way for a long, long fight. The skull came home with me.\n\nBrownell's view was that a lich's loyalty never wavers, and that loyalty of that sort only ever leads to its own destruction."] = "Andrew Brownell, in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, laid out Razorfen Downs for me like a lecture. The quilboar there had thrown in with the Scourge, and the lich who ruled them, Amnennar the Coldbringer, moved them about with his mind. He also had a line straight to Ner'zhul. Brownell wanted that line cut, and the skull brought back to show for it.\n\nThe bottom of the Downs was colder than anything in the Barrens has a right to be, and Amnennar did his best to keep it that way for a long, long fight. The skull came home with me.\n\nBrownell's view was that a lich's loyalty never wavers, and that loyalty of that sort only ever leads to its own destruction."
L["Bring the Light"] = "Bring the Light"
