L["Andrew Brownell"] = "Andrew Brownell"
L["The Coldbringer's Eye"] = "The Coldbringer's Eye"
L["Archmage Lan'dalock in Dalaran wanted the Coldbringer's Eye brought out of Razorfen Downs. It sat in a blue orb behind Amnennar, which made Amnennar the first step of the errand. Once he was out of the way the orb gave it up, and I carried it all the way to the Alterac Mountains for the archmage."] = "Archmage Lan'dalock in Dalaran wanted the Coldbringer's Eye brought out of Razorfen Downs. It sat in a blue orb behind Amnennar, which made Amnennar the first step of the errand. Once he was out of the way the orb gave it up, and I carried it all the way to the Alterac Mountains for the archmage."
L["Sutara Plainstalker"] = "Sutara Plainstalker"
L["Sutara Plainstalker, an Earthen Ring quartermaster in Mulgore, wanted the Coldbringer's Eye fetched from Razorfen Downs. It sat in a blue orb behind Amnennar, so Amnennar had to be dealt with first, and I was headed that way regardless. With the lich gone the orb let go of it, and I took it back across the Barrens to Sutara."] = "Sutara Plainstalker, an Earthen Ring quartermaster in Mulgore, wanted the Coldbringer's Eye fetched from Razorfen Downs. It sat in a blue orb behind Amnennar, so Amnennar had to be dealt with first, and I was headed that way regardless. With the lich gone the orb let go of it, and I took it back across the Barrens to Sutara."
-- Profession stories: Master of the Wild Leather, The Mithril Order, The Pledge of Secrecy
L["The Mithril Order"] = "The Mithril Order"
L["Galvan the Ancient, a dwarf smith of the old school, left Booty Bay long ago, but the order he belongs to still keeps members in town, looking for a successor.\n\nYour trainer can point you their way, south into the jungles of Stranglethorn, and in time you'll have to choose between armor and weapons."] = "Galvan the Ancient, a dwarf smith of the old school, left Booty Bay long ago, but the order he belongs to still keeps members in town, looking for a successor.\n\nYour trainer can point you their way, south into the jungles of Stranglethorn, and in time you'll have to choose between armor and weapons."
L["Years ago a dwarf named Galvan trained Hank the Hammer, then left for Booty Bay, and Hank promised to pass the teaching on. Hank still keeps that promise, in Stormwind's Dwarven District.\n\nFrom there the road runs south to Stranglethorn and Gadgetzan before it brings you back to the Great Forge in Ironforge, where armorsmiths and weaponsmiths each want you for their own."] = "Years ago a dwarf named Galvan trained Hank the Hammer, then left for Booty Bay, and Hank promised to pass the teaching on. Hank still keeps that promise, in Stormwind's Dwarven District.\n\nFrom there the road runs south to Stranglethorn and Gadgetzan before it brings you back to the Great Forge in Ironforge, where armorsmiths and weaponsmiths each want you for their own."
L["Orokk Omosh, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, is the last of twenty generations of Omosh smiths and wants the family recipes to outlive him. Aturk the Anvil, a few steps away, has older ways to teach.\n\nFrom there the road runs south to Stranglethorn and Gadgetzan before it brings you back to the Valley of Honor, where armorsmiths and weaponsmiths each want you for their own."] = "Orokk Omosh, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, is the last of twenty generations of Omosh smiths and wants the family recipes to outlive him. Aturk the Anvil, a few steps away, has older ways to teach.\n\nFrom there the road runs south to Stranglethorn and Gadgetzan before it brings you back to the Valley of Honor, where armorsmiths and weaponsmiths each want you for their own."
L["Stranglethorn Vale / Tanaris / Winterspring"] = "Stranglethorn Vale / Tanaris / Winterspring"
L["The Origins of Smithing"] = "The Origins of Smithing"
L["Hank the Hammer"] = "Hank the Hammer"
L["between Zul'Gurub and the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound, Stranglethorn Vale"] = "between Zul'Gurub and the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound, Stranglethorn Vale"
L["Joys of Omosh"] = "Joys of Omosh"
L["Twenty generations of Omosh have held the hammer Orokk Omosh holds now, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, and he has no heir for the family recipes. Bring your best bronze work and show him you could carry them on."] = "Twenty generations of Omosh have held the hammer Orokk Omosh holds now, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, and he has no heir for the family recipes. Bring your best bronze work and show him you could carry them on."
L["There's a smith in the Valley of Honor named Orokk Omosh. Twenty generations of Omosh have held the same hammer, and Orokk is the last of them, with the family recipes and no one to leave them to. He looked me over and decided I would have to do.\n\nThe recipes cost me more bronze than I knew Orgrimmar had, and then iron. Every delivery bought one set of barbaric iron plans and a short speech about the fear I'd see in my enemies' eyes. Once he said I was like his own grandfather, Chief Gorokk, and I took that kindly.\n\nThe last family secret was a dance. Orokk was not crying, he told me, there was soot in his eye. Then he taught me the Omosh Dance of Joy, and was panting a bit by the end. I still do it at the forge when a piece comes out right."] = "There's a smith in the Valley of Honor named Orokk Omosh. Twenty generations of Omosh have held the same hammer, and Orokk is the last of them, with the family recipes and no one to leave them to. He looked me over and decided I would have to do.\n\nThe recipes cost me more bronze than I knew Orgrimmar had, and then iron. Every delivery bought one set of barbaric iron plans and a short speech about the fear I'd see in my enemies' eyes. Once he said I was like his own grandfather, Chief Gorokk, and I took that kindly.\n\nThe last family secret was a dance. Orokk was not crying, he told me, there was soot in his eye. Then he taught me the Omosh Dance of Joy, and was panting a bit by the end. I still do it at the forge when a piece comes out right."
L["Barbaric Battlements"] = "Barbaric Battlements"
L["Orokk Omosh"] = "Orokk Omosh"
L["On Iron Pauldrons"] = "On Iron Pauldrons"
L["Trampled Under Foot"] = "Trampled Under Foot"
L["Horns of Frenzy"] = "Horns of Frenzy"
L["Hank the Hammer, in Stormwind's Dwarven District, was trained by a dwarf named Galvan, who made Hank promise to teach any smith with the will to go further. For six golden scale bracers, Hank will show you where smithing comes from."] = "Hank the Hammer, in Stormwind's Dwarven District, was trained by a dwarf named Galvan, who made Hank promise to teach any smith with the will to go further. For six golden scale bracers, Hank will show you where smithing comes from."
L["Aturk the Anvil, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, remembers the days of crushed skulls and has little use for peacetime. Bring four steel breastplates and four steel helms, and he will give you a taste of war."] = "Aturk the Anvil, in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, remembers the days of crushed skulls and has little use for peacetime. Bring four steel breastplates and four steel helms, and he will give you a taste of war."
L["Hank the Hammer learned the trade from Galvan, a dwarf who left for Booty Bay years ago. For six golden scale bracers, Hank taught me where smithing comes from. It never comes from here, I was told, twice, and only from here. I still couldn't tell you which here was which.\n\nThen Hank gave me an insignia to take to McGavan at the Booty Bay smithy. McGavan kept it and swore by Blackhoof's back hair that I was worthy of the Mithril Order. What I got back was a pin to show Galvan, far to the north.\n\nGalvan teaches mining before smithing, so every lesson started with forty bars of mithril. Truesilver got a lecture to itself. He calls it the great silver deceiver, and spent more than ten years in the Alterac Mountains learning why. When my arms worked again, he sent me on to Gadgetzan."] = "Hank the Hammer learned the trade from Galvan, a dwarf who left for Booty Bay years ago. For six golden scale bracers, Hank taught me where smithing comes from. It never comes from here, I was told, twice, and only from here. I still couldn't tell you which here was which.\n\nThen Hank gave me an insignia to take to McGavan at the Booty Bay smithy. McGavan kept it and swore by Blackhoof's back hair that I was worthy of the Mithril Order. What I got back was a pin to show Galvan, far to the north.\n\nGalvan teaches mining before smithing, so every lesson started with forty bars of mithril. Truesilver got a lecture to itself. He calls it the great silver deceiver, and spent more than ten years in the Alterac Mountains learning why. When my arms worked again, he sent me on to Gadgetzan."
L["Aturk the Anvil remembers grinding the bones of fallen enemies into filament powder, and hasn't made peace with the Warchief's peace. For four steel breastplates and four helms, Aturk taught me orcish war leggings and made it plain I was a disappointment.\n\nAturk's neighbor was more cheerful, and knew a guy who knew a guy at the smithy in Booty Bay. That was McGavan, who kept the insignia I'd been handed and swore by Blackhoof's back hair that I was worthy of the Mithril Order. I got a pin in exchange, and directions north to Galvan.\n\nGalvan teaches mining before smithing, so every lesson started with forty bars of mithril. Truesilver got a lecture to itself. He calls it the great silver deceiver, and spent more than ten years in the Alterac Mountains learning why. When my arms worked again, he sent me on to Gadgetzan."] = "Aturk the Anvil remembers grinding the bones of fallen enemies into filament powder, and hasn't made peace with the Warchief's peace. For four steel breastplates and four helms, Aturk taught me orcish war leggings and made it plain I was a disappointment.\n\nAturk's neighbor was more cheerful, and knew a guy who knew a guy at the smithy in Booty Bay. That was McGavan, who kept the insignia I'd been handed and swore by Blackhoof's back hair that I was worthy of the Mithril Order. I got a pin in exchange, and directions north to Galvan.\n\nGalvan teaches mining before smithing, so every lesson started with forty bars of mithril. Truesilver got a lecture to itself. He calls it the great silver deceiver, and spent more than ten years in the Alterac Mountains learning why. When my arms worked again, he sent me on to Gadgetzan."
L["The Old Ways"] = "The Old Ways"
L["Aturk the Anvil"] = "Aturk the Anvil"
L["Booty Bay or Bust!"] = "Booty Bay or Bust!"
