L["The Great Silver Deceiver"] = "The Great Silver Deceiver"
L["The Art of the Imbue"] = "The Art of the Imbue"
L["Galvan's Finest Pupil"] = "Galvan's Finest Pupil"
L["The Mithril Kid"] = "The Mithril Kid"
L["Galvan has sent you to Gadgetzan, in Tanaris, to meet Trenton Lighthammer, the old smith's finest pupil. Trenton can teach you about ornate mithril, and has a blacksmithing championship to get ready for."] = "Galvan has sent you to Gadgetzan, in Tanaris, to meet Trenton Lighthammer, the old smith's finest pupil. Trenton can teach you about ornate mithril, and has a blacksmithing championship to get ready for."
L["Trenton Lighthammer is known in Gadgetzan as the Mithril Kid. Galvan had taught each of us half of the ornate mithril set and left us to find each other, and Trenton saw the plan straight away. So we traded, piece for piece, until we both knew all of it.\n\nThe boots meant the most to Trenton. At last year's All-Valley Blacksmithing Championship, a rival from the Venture Co. Foundry swept his leg, and ornate mithril boots kept him going to the win. This year he wanted the pants too. When we were done, Trenton declared me unsweepable.\n\nAfter that I stood and watched Trenton work. Then I was handed an insignia very like the one I'd given McGavan, and named a blacksmith of the Mithril Order. Galvan had the last word, and a signet worth far more than what I'd given up."] = "Trenton Lighthammer is known in Gadgetzan as the Mithril Kid. Galvan had taught each of us half of the ornate mithril set and left us to find each other, and Trenton saw the plan straight away. So we traded, piece for piece, until we both knew all of it.\n\nThe boots meant the most to Trenton. At last year's All-Valley Blacksmithing Championship, a rival from the Venture Co. Foundry swept his leg, and ornate mithril boots kept him going to the win. This year he wanted the pants too. When we were done, Trenton declared me unsweepable.\n\nAfter that I stood and watched Trenton work. Then I was handed an insignia very like the one I'd given McGavan, and named a blacksmith of the Mithril Order. Galvan had the last word, and a signet worth far more than what I'd given up."
L["A Good Head On Your Shoulders"] = "A Good Head On Your Shoulders"
L["The World At Your Feet"] = "The World At Your Feet"
L["Did You Lose This?"] = "Did You Lose This?"
L["Expert Blacksmith!"] = "Expert Blacksmith!"
L["Armorsmith or Weaponsmith"] = "Armorsmith or Weaponsmith"
L["At the Great Forge in Ironforge, Grumnus Steelshaper trains armorsmiths and Ironus Coldsteel trains weaponsmiths. You can follow only one of them, so hear both out. From level 50, weaponsmiths can seek out three masters in Everlook, in Winterspring."] = "At the Great Forge in Ironforge, Grumnus Steelshaper trains armorsmiths and Ironus Coldsteel trains weaponsmiths. You can follow only one of them, so hear both out. From level 50, weaponsmiths can seek out three masters in Everlook, in Winterspring."
L["In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Okothos Ironrager trains armorsmiths and Borgosh Corebender trains weaponsmiths. You can follow only one of them, so hear both out. From level 50, weaponsmiths can seek out three masters in Everlook, in Winterspring."] = "In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Okothos Ironrager trains armorsmiths and Borgosh Corebender trains weaponsmiths. You can follow only one of them, so hear both out. From level 50, weaponsmiths can seek out three masters in Everlook, in Winterspring."
L["At the Great Forge there are two trainers who will take a smith further, and each thinks the other went wrong. Grumnus Steelshaper calls armor the smart decision. Ironus Coldsteel says weaponsmiths are the ones with all the gold, and was stacking coins into neat piles while saying it.\n\nBoth wanted a pile of finished work before they'd teach a thing, and a smith only gets to pick one of them. I made my choice and the work to go with it. Which one I took is between me and my anvil.\n\nUp in Everlook, three masters each teach a single weapon to weaponsmiths who bring them a trophy from a dungeon. Picking one of them closes the other two doors for good."] = "At the Great Forge there are two trainers who will take a smith further, and each thinks the other went wrong. Grumnus Steelshaper calls armor the smart decision. Ironus Coldsteel says weaponsmiths are the ones with all the gold, and was stacking coins into neat piles while saying it.\n\nBoth wanted a pile of finished work before they'd teach a thing, and a smith only gets to pick one of them. I made my choice and the work to go with it. Which one I took is between me and my anvil.\n\nUp in Everlook, three masters each teach a single weapon to weaponsmiths who bring them a trophy from a dungeon. Picking one of them closes the other two doors for good."
L["In the Valley of Honor there are two trainers who will take a smith further. Okothos Ironrager makes armor for the satisfaction of it, and means to pound steel until there's no breath left to do it with. Borgosh Corebender makes weapons and dreams of a hammer fit for a Warchief, a life's work still in progress.\n\nBoth wanted a pile of finished work first, and both offered one last chance to back out. I made my choice and the work to go with it. Which one I took is between me and my anvil.\n\nUp in Everlook, three masters each teach a single weapon to weaponsmiths who bring them a trophy from a dungeon. Picking one of them closes the other two doors for good."] = "In the Valley of Honor there are two trainers who will take a smith further. Okothos Ironrager makes armor for the satisfaction of it, and means to pound steel until there's no breath left to do it with. Borgosh Corebender makes weapons and dreams of a hammer fit for a Warchief, a life's work still in progress.\n\nBoth wanted a pile of finished work first, and both offered one last chance to back out. I made my choice and the work to go with it. Which one I took is between me and my anvil.\n\nUp in Everlook, three masters each teach a single weapon to weaponsmiths who bring them a trophy from a dungeon. Picking one of them closes the other two doors for good."
L["The Art of the Armorsmith"] = "The Art of the Armorsmith"
L["I took up armor. Grumnus Steelshaper went over my stack of ornate mithril and told me there was no turning back after this, and that it wasn't too late to become a toy maker. A weaponsmith, he meant. I've had a forge tan ever since."] = "I took up armor. Grumnus Steelshaper went over my stack of ornate mithril and told me there was no turning back after this, and that it wasn't too late to become a toy maker. A weaponsmith, he meant. I've had a forge tan ever since."
L["Okothos Ironrager"] = "Okothos Ironrager"
L["I took up armor. Okothos Ironrager checked my ornate mithril and offered me one last chance to back out. I didn't take it, and was wished a lifetime of glory, which I've been working through one helm at a time."] = "I took up armor. Okothos Ironrager checked my ornate mithril and offered me one last chance to back out. I didn't take it, and was wished a lifetime of glory, which I've been working through one helm at a time."
L["The Way of the Weaponsmith"] = "The Way of the Weaponsmith"
L["Ironus Coldsteel"] = "Ironus Coldsteel"
L["I took up weapons. Ironus Coldsteel had customers waiting and took my axes and maces almost before I'd set them down, then told me to pay attention. I've had customers waiting myself ever since, and I'm still looking for all that gold."] = "I took up weapons. Ironus Coldsteel had customers waiting and took my axes and maces almost before I'd set them down, then told me to pay attention. I've had customers waiting myself ever since, and I'm still looking for all that gold."
L["Borgosh Corebender"] = "Borgosh Corebender"
L["I took up weapons. Borgosh Corebender looked over my work and offered me a last chance to back out, then told me to prepare to be consumed by knowledge. He wasn't wrong. Some nights I dream in axe heads."] = "I took up weapons. Borgosh Corebender looked over my work and offered me a last chance to back out, then told me to prepare to be consumed by knowledge. He wasn't wrong. Some nights I dream in axe heads."
L["Sweet Serenity"] = "Sweet Serenity"
L["Lilith the Lithe"] = "Lilith the Lithe"
L["Lilith the Lithe sent me into the Scarlet Bastion in Stratholme, where the Crimson Hammersmith guards the recipe for a hammer called Serenity with his life. He meant it. I brought Lilith his apron and became a hammersmith, with the sword and the axe closed to me from then on."] = "Lilith the Lithe sent me into the Scarlet Bastion in Stratholme, where the Crimson Hammersmith guards the recipe for a hammer called Serenity with his life. He meant it. I brought Lilith his apron and became a hammersmith, with the sword and the axe closed to me from then on."
L["Snakestone of the Shadow Huntress"] = "Snakestone of the Shadow Huntress"
L["Kilram"] = "Kilram"
L["Kilram has a scar from Vosh'gajin, the shadow huntress of Blackrock Spire, and warned me not to let her beauty fool me. I brought back her snakestone, which the legend says keeps an axe razor sharp for a thousand years. Kilram made me an axesmith for it, and the sword and the hammer were closed to me for good."] = "Kilram has a scar from Vosh'gajin, the shadow huntress of Blackrock Spire, and warned me not to let her beauty fool me. I brought back her snakestone, which the legend says keeps an axe razor sharp for a thousand years. Kilram made me an axesmith for it, and the sword and the hammer were closed to me for good."
L["Corruption"] = "Corruption"
L["Seril Scourgebane"] = "Seril Scourgebane"
L["Seril Scourgebane was short with me, and said there was a reason for it. The Black Guard, Baron Rivendare's skeletal elite, had stolen the plans for the great blade Corruption, and their swordsmith in Stratholme was keeping them. I destroyed him and brought his insignia back to Everlook, and Seril made me a swordsmith. The hammer and the axe are closed to me now."] = "Seril Scourgebane was short with me, and said there was a reason for it. The Black Guard, Baron Rivendare's skeletal elite, had stolen the plans for the great blade Corruption, and their swordsmith in Stratholme was keeping them. I destroyed him and brought his insignia back to Everlook, and Seril made me a swordsmith. The hammer and the axe are closed to me now."
L["The Pledge of Secrecy"] = "The Pledge of Secrecy"
L["Past a certain point, engineering splits into two schools. Gnome engineers build devices meant to make life easier, and goblin engineers build explosives and the guns to go with them. Each school guards its schemata from the other, so you can learn one and never the other.\n\nYour engineering trainer has a manual on the subject and strong views on which school a sensible engineer would join. Read it and make up your own mind. Then take the manual to the master of the school you want."] = "Past a certain point, engineering splits into two schools. Gnome engineers build devices meant to make life easier, and goblin engineers build explosives and the guns to go with them. Each school guards its schemata from the other, so you can learn one and never the other.\n\nYour engineering trainer has a manual on the subject and strong views on which school a sensible engineer would join. Read it and make up your own mind. Then take the manual to the master of the school you want."
L["Stormwind / Ironforge / Undercity / Stranglethorn Vale / Tanaris"] = "Stormwind / Ironforge / Undercity / Stranglethorn Vale / Tanaris"
L["Gnome Engineering"] = "Gnome Engineering"
L["Lilliam Sparkspindle"] = "Lilliam Sparkspindle"
L["the Rogues' Quarter, Undercity"] = "the Rogues' Quarter, Undercity"
L["Show Your Work"] = "Show Your Work"
L["Your engineering trainer has a manual for you, and an opinion to go with it. From here the craft splits into a gnome school and a goblin school, and you can only join one. Read the manual before you choose."] = "Your engineering trainer has a manual for you, and an opinion to go with it. From here the craft splits into a gnome school and a goblin school, and you can only join one. Read the manual before you choose."
L["Engineering only goes so far before it splits in two, gnome and goblin, and you have to pick. My trainer gave me a manual on it and made plain which school I ought to join. Gnomes build things to make life easier, says the manual, and some of them even work. Goblins build bombs and guns, which have the opposite problem. Join one school and the other keeps its schemata from you for good. The manual says so twice.\n\nBefore I learned a single schematic there was a pledge of lifelong secrecy to sign. I was told to think it over carefully. I read every line and signed.\n\nLast came the samples, because a master wants to see your work before handing over the good schemata. I spent a few long evenings at the bench. Mine passed, and I was given a membership card."] = "Engineering only goes so far before it splits in two, gnome and goblin, and you have to pick. My trainer gave me a manual on it and made plain which school I ought to join. Gnomes build things to make life easier, says the manual, and some of them even work. Goblins build bombs and guns, which have the opposite problem. Join one school and the other keeps its schemata from you for good. The manual says so twice.\n\nBefore I learned a single schematic there was a pledge of lifelong secrecy to sign. I was told to think it over carefully. I read every line and signed.\n\nLast came the samples, because a master wants to see your work before handing over the good schemata. I spent a few long evenings at the bench. Mine passed, and I was given a membership card."
L["I took the manual to Tinkmaster Overspark in Tinker Town, who said he had all the time in the world, since all he does now is stand about while Gnomeregan sits in its cloud of radiation. Then he begged my pardon for the melodrama."] = "I took the manual to Tinkmaster Overspark in Tinker Town, who said he had all the time in the world, since all he does now is stand about while Gnomeregan sits in its cloud of radiation. Then he begged my pardon for the melodrama."
L["Graham Van Talen"] = "Graham Van Talen"
L["My trainer said that if I wanted to learn to make metal paperweights, Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay was the one to see. Oglethorpe opened by referring me to his barrister, in case I'd come about a homing robot through my wall. Gnomeregan, he told me, lost one of its greatest engineers the day he left."] = "My trainer said that if I wanted to learn to make metal paperweights, Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay was the one to see. Oglethorpe opened by referring me to his barrister, in case I'd come about a homing robot through my wall. Gnomeregan, he told me, lost one of its greatest engineers the day he left."
L["Overspark had signed the same pledge once, like every gnome engineer before me, and was delighted to have me in the fold."] = "Overspark had signed the same pledge once, like every gnome engineer before me, and was delighted to have me in the fold."
L["Overspark's list ran to six mithril tubes and two advanced target dummies, among other things, so he could see where my work might be more gnomish. My card says I'm a member in good standing of the Mechanical Engineering Guild, Associated. I'd spell out the initials, but I signed a pledge."] = "Overspark's list ran to six mithril tubes and two advanced target dummies, among other things, so he could see where my work might be more gnomish. My card says I'm a member in good standing of the Mechanical Engineering Guild, Associated. I'd spell out the initials, but I signed a pledge."
L["Oglethorpe Obnoticus"] = "Oglethorpe Obnoticus"
L["Oglethorpe has no love for Gnomeregan's politics, or for one of its tinkmasters in particular, but he holds the pledge above all of that."] = "Oglethorpe has no love for Gnomeregan's politics, or for one of its tinkmasters in particular, but he holds the pledge above all of that."
L["Oglethorpe went over my mithril tubes and target dummies for gnomish technique. The card he gave me says I'm a member in good standing of the Mechanical Engineering Guild, Associated. I'd spell out the initials, but I signed a pledge."] = "Oglethorpe went over my mithril tubes and target dummies for gnomish technique. The card he gave me says I'm a member in good standing of the Mechanical Engineering Guild, Associated. I'd spell out the initials, but I signed a pledge."
L["Goblin Engineering"] = "Goblin Engineering"
L["I took the manual all the way to Gadgetzan, to Nixx Sprocketspring, who said he can smell a fresh recruit a mile off, like good blasting powder. Any fool can learn the basics, says Nixx, and Gnomeregan proves it. Goblin work takes a steady hand, and he leaned hard on the steady."] = "I took the manual all the way to Gadgetzan, to Nixx Sprocketspring, who said he can smell a fresh recruit a mile off, like good blasting powder. Any fool can learn the basics, says Nixx, and Gnomeregan proves it. Goblin work takes a steady hand, and he leaned hard on the steady."
L["My trainer called goblin engineering the choice of every brilliant engineer, and I don't argue with compliments. Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan said he'd smelled me coming a mile off, like good blasting powder, and that goblin work takes a steady hand. He said steady louder than the rest."] = "My trainer called goblin engineering the choice of every brilliant engineer, and I don't argue with compliments. Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan said he'd smelled me coming a mile off, like good blasting powder, and that goblin work takes a steady hand. He said steady louder than the rest."
L["Nixx Sprocketspring"] = "Nixx Sprocketspring"
L["Nixx kept it simple. It was a one-way trip, he said, and if I was ready, I should hop aboard."] = "Nixx kept it simple. It was a one-way trip, he said, and if I was ready, I should hop aboard."
L["Nixx asked for forty assorted explosives and five explosive sheep, and told me to keep the safeties armed. My card says I'm a member in good standing of the Goblin Experimental Engineering Korporation, with a K. I suspect the initials came first."] = "Nixx asked for forty assorted explosives and five explosive sheep, and told me to keep the safeties armed. My card says I'm a member in good standing of the Goblin Experimental Engineering Korporation, with a K. I suspect the initials came first."
L["Master of the Wild Leather"] = "Master of the Wild Leather"
L["Two leatherworkers in Feralas know how to stitch wildvines into armor, and whichever one teaches you will want you working for them while you learn, paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."] = "Two leatherworkers in Feralas know how to stitch wildvines into armor, and whichever one teaches you will want you working for them while you learn, paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."
L["Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, knows how to stitch wildvines into armor. He'll teach you, if you don't mind working for him while you learn and paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."] = "Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, knows how to stitch wildvines into armor. He'll teach you, if you don't mind working for him while you learn and paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."
L["Jangdor Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas, knows how to stitch wildvines into armor. He'll teach you, if you don't mind working for him while you learn and paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."] = "Jangdor Swiftstrider, at Camp Mojache in Feralas, knows how to stitch wildvines into armor. He'll teach you, if you don't mind working for him while you learn and paying for each pattern in finished leather.\n\nBeyond Wild Leather the trade divides into three high arts, each with a master of its own, and a leatherworker only ever gets to learn one of them."
