L["Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, thinks you're getting good with leather. He knows how to work wildvines into armor and will teach you, though you'll be working for him a while, and he wants ten pieces of thick leather to start."] = "Pratt McGrubben, at Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas, thinks you're getting good with leather. He knows how to work wildvines into armor and will teach you, though you'll be working for him a while, and he wants ten pieces of thick leather to start."
L["Word of your leatherwork has reached Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache in Feralas. He knows how to work wildvines into armor and will teach you, though you'll be working for him a while, and he wants ten pieces of thick leather to start."] = "Word of your leatherwork has reached Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache in Feralas. He knows how to work wildvines into armor and will teach you, though you'll be working for him a while, and he wants ten pieces of thick leather to start."
L["Pratt McGrubben teaches Wild Leather at Feathermoon Stronghold, and warned me up front that I'd be working for him while I learned. I pictured sweeping the shop. He meant armor, made by me and handed to him in pairs of turtle scale and nightscape, with a wildvine tucked into every order.\n\nThe wildvines are the trick. They're potent and chaotic, so whatever you stitch one into comes out strong in ways you can't call in advance. Pratt calls the result second to none, guaranteed.\n\nWith every pattern paid for but one, Pratt wrote a letter and sent me to his own teacher, Telonis, in Darnassus. Telonis read it and allowed that Pratt reminds him of a night elf sometimes, which I took to be the warmest thing Darnassus says about a human. Then the cloak pattern was mine. Few in the world know it, Telonis says."] = "Pratt McGrubben teaches Wild Leather at Feathermoon Stronghold, and warned me up front that I'd be working for him while I learned. I pictured sweeping the shop. He meant armor, made by me and handed to him in pairs of turtle scale and nightscape, with a wildvine tucked into every order.\n\nThe wildvines are the trick. They're potent and chaotic, so whatever you stitch one into comes out strong in ways you can't call in advance. Pratt calls the result second to none, guaranteed.\n\nWith every pattern paid for but one, Pratt wrote a letter and sent me to his own teacher, Telonis, in Darnassus. Telonis read it and allowed that Pratt reminds him of a night elf sometimes, which I took to be the warmest thing Darnassus says about a human. Then the cloak pattern was mine. Few in the world know it, Telonis says."
L["Jangdor Swiftstrider teaches Wild Leather at Camp Mojache, and warned me up front that I'd be working for him while I learned. I pictured hauling hides. He meant armor, made by me and handed to him in pairs of turtle scale and nightscape, with a wildvine tucked into every order.\n\nThe wildvines are the trick. They're potent and chaotic, so whatever you stitch one into comes out strong in ways you can't call in advance. Jangdor calls the result second to none, guaranteed.\n\nWith every pattern paid for but one, Jangdor wrote a letter and sent me up to Thunder Bluff, to Una, who brought him into the craft. Una read it and was pleased to see one of her finest students with a student of his own. I was pleased to get the cloak pattern. Few in the world know it, Una says."] = "Jangdor Swiftstrider teaches Wild Leather at Camp Mojache, and warned me up front that I'd be working for him while I learned. I pictured hauling hides. He meant armor, made by me and handed to him in pairs of turtle scale and nightscape, with a wildvine tucked into every order.\n\nThe wildvines are the trick. They're potent and chaotic, so whatever you stitch one into comes out strong in ways you can't call in advance. Jangdor calls the result second to none, guaranteed.\n\nWith every pattern paid for but one, Jangdor wrote a letter and sent me up to Thunder Bluff, to Una, who brought him into the craft. Una read it and was pleased to see one of her finest students with a student of his own. I was pleased to get the cloak pattern. Few in the world know it, Una says."
