L["The Three Arts"] = "The Three Arts"
L["The leatherworking trade has three high arts, and you may learn only one. Peter Galen in Azshara teaches dragonscale. Sarah Tanner in Searing Gorge teaches elemental leatherworking, and Caryssia Moonhunter at Thalanaar in Feralas teaches tribal. Each has a price for taking you on."] = "The leatherworking trade has three high arts, and you may learn only one. Peter Galen in Azshara teaches dragonscale. Sarah Tanner in Searing Gorge teaches elemental leatherworking, and Caryssia Moonhunter at Thalanaar in Feralas teaches tribal. Each has a price for taking you on."
L["The leatherworking trade has three high arts, and you may learn only one. Thorkaf Dragoneye in the Badlands teaches dragonscale. Brumn Winterhoof in the Arathi Highlands teaches elemental leatherworking, and Se'Jib in Stranglethorn Vale teaches tribal. Each has a price for taking you on."] = "The leatherworking trade has three high arts, and you may learn only one. Thorkaf Dragoneye in the Badlands teaches dragonscale. Brumn Winterhoof in the Arathi Highlands teaches elemental leatherworking, and Se'Jib in Stranglethorn Vale teaches tribal. Each has a price for taking you on."
L["At the top, the leatherworking trade splits three ways, and each way has a master of its own. Every one of them asks for the same promise before teaching you a thing. Learn this art and the other two are closed to you for good.\n\nI thought it over longer than I'd admit to a customer. Then I made up my mind, gathered what my new master wanted, and went to make the promise."] = "At the top, the leatherworking trade splits three ways, and each way has a master of its own. Every one of them asks for the same promise before teaching you a thing. Learn this art and the other two are closed to you for good.\n\nI thought it over longer than I'd admit to a customer. Then I made up my mind, gathered what my new master wanted, and went to make the promise."
L["Dragonscale Leatherworking"] = "Dragonscale Leatherworking"
L["Peter Galen"] = "Peter Galen"
L["Peter Galen, out in Azshara, teaches dragonscale and wanted two kinds of proof before taking me on. Samples of my best scorpid work came first, two breastplates and two pairs of gloves. Then ten worn dragonscales, to show I could get hold of the staple of the trade. Peter said it takes a strong will to make a permanent decision like mine. It takes a fair number of scorpids, too."] = "Peter Galen, out in Azshara, teaches dragonscale and wanted two kinds of proof before taking me on. Samples of my best scorpid work came first, two breastplates and two pairs of gloves. Then ten worn dragonscales, to show I could get hold of the staple of the trade. Peter said it takes a strong will to make a permanent decision like mine. It takes a fair number of scorpids, too."
L["Thorkaf Dragoneye"] = "Thorkaf Dragoneye"
L["Thorkaf Dragoneye teaches dragonscale out in the Badlands and wanted to see my scorpid work first, two breastplates and two pairs of gloves. Those I could make. The ten worn dragonscales I had to go out and find, which I suspect was the point. Once Thorkaf had the lot, the other two arts were closed to me, and I've been working in mail ever since."] = "Thorkaf Dragoneye teaches dragonscale out in the Badlands and wanted to see my scorpid work first, two breastplates and two pairs of gloves. Those I could make. The ten worn dragonscales I had to go out and find, which I suspect was the point. Once Thorkaf had the lot, the other two arts were closed to me, and I've been working in mail ever since."
L["Elemental Leatherworking"] = "Elemental Leatherworking"
L["Sarah Tanner"] = "Sarah Tanner"
L["Sarah Tanner teaches elemental leatherworking in Searing Gorge and wanted proof that I was in tune with the elements, which meant bringing two each of their purest essences. Fire, water, earth and wind. I got them the usual way, off the elementals themselves. Sarah said the elements accepted me. They hadn't seemed to at the time."] = "Sarah Tanner teaches elemental leatherworking in Searing Gorge and wanted proof that I was in tune with the elements, which meant bringing two each of their purest essences. Fire, water, earth and wind. I got them the usual way, off the elementals themselves. Sarah said the elements accepted me. They hadn't seemed to at the time."
L["Brumn Winterhoof"] = "Brumn Winterhoof"
L["Brumn Winterhoof teaches elemental leatherworking out in the Arathi Highlands, and a place cost two each of the elements' essences, hearts of fire, globes of water, cores of earth and breaths of wind. I got them the usual way, off the elementals themselves, who had opinions about it. Once Brumn had them all, the other two arts were closed to me."] = "Brumn Winterhoof teaches elemental leatherworking out in the Arathi Highlands, and a place cost two each of the elements' essences, hearts of fire, globes of water, cores of earth and breaths of wind. I got them the usual way, off the elementals themselves, who had opinions about it. Once Brumn had them all, the other two arts were closed to me."
L["Tribal Leatherworking"] = "Tribal Leatherworking"
L["Caryssia Moonhunter"] = "Caryssia Moonhunter"
L["Caryssia Moonhunter teaches tribal leatherworking at Thalanaar, on the eastern edge of Feralas, and asked first for an offering to nature. Nature, it seems, wanted my finest Wild Leather, a vest and a helmet. I'd have liked to see nature wear them. Caryssia took them on nature's behalf and promised I'd soon be bending it to my will."] = "Caryssia Moonhunter teaches tribal leatherworking at Thalanaar, on the eastern edge of Feralas, and asked first for an offering to nature. Nature, it seems, wanted my finest Wild Leather, a vest and a helmet. I'd have liked to see nature wear them. Caryssia took them on nature's behalf and promised I'd soon be bending it to my will."
L["Se'Jib"] = "Se'Jib"
L["Se'Jib teaches tribal leatherworking southeast of Grom'gol, in Stranglethorn, and asked first for an offering to nature. Nature wanted my finest Wild Leather, a vest and a helmet. I'd have liked to see nature wear them. Se'Jib took them on nature's behalf, and after that the other two arts were closed to me."] = "Se'Jib teaches tribal leatherworking southeast of Grom'gol, in Stranglethorn, and asked first for an offering to nature. Nature wanted my finest Wild Leather, a vest and a helmet. I'd have liked to see nature wear them. Se'Jib took them on nature's behalf, and after that the other two arts were closed to me."
-- WoW Forever secret: The Dawn Waker
L["The Dawn Waker"] = "The Dawn Waker"
L["An old ring from Zephras Isle, dented, with Kaldorei writing worn into the band. A hilt in the ruins of Ban'aethal that only shows itself by torchlight. Ealaane Nimbuswalker knows something about the blade that once fit it.\n\nThis is a secret, and its end hasn't been found yet. The trail crosses Kalimdor as far as anyone has followed it, and some of it takes a group."] = "An old ring from Zephras Isle, dented, with Kaldorei writing worn into the band. A hilt in the ruins of Ban'aethal that only shows itself by torchlight. Ealaane Nimbuswalker knows something about the blade that once fit it.\n\nThis is a secret, and its end hasn't been found yet. The trail crosses Kalimdor as far as anyone has followed it, and some of it takes a group."
L["Zephras Isle / Darkshore / Ashenvale / Shen'dralas / Feralas / Azshara / Winterspring / Mount Hyjal"] = "Zephras Isle / Darkshore / Ashenvale / Shen'dralas / Feralas / Azshara / Winterspring / Mount Hyjal"
L["The Ancient Hilt"] = "The Ancient Hilt"
L["Ancient Hilt"] = "Ancient Hilt"
L["the Ruins of Ban'aethal, Zephras Isle"] = "the Ruins of Ban'aethal, Zephras Isle"
L["the Grove of the Ancients, Darkshore"] = "the Grove of the Ancients, Darkshore"
L["Zoram Strand, Ashenvale"] = "Zoram Strand, Ashenvale"
L["The Ancient Heirloom"] = "The Ancient Heirloom"
L["Rorian the Dayseeker hands an old ring to every Skyborne who comes of age in Thendal Village, and another lies upstairs in a house close by. Wear it, carry a Night Watchman's Torch into the ruins of Ban'aethal, and see what the light turns up. Ealaane Nimbuswalker will want to hear about it."] = "Rorian the Dayseeker hands an old ring to every Skyborne who comes of age in Thendal Village, and another lies upstairs in a house close by. Wear it, carry a Night Watchman's Torch into the ruins of Ban'aethal, and see what the light turns up. Ealaane Nimbuswalker will want to hear about it."
L["I came by an old ring on Zephras Isle. It's dented, and the inside of the band carries a line of Kaldorei script worn so thin I could barely read it. I put it on because it fit.\n\nThere's a dragon asleep in the ruins of Ban'aethal and a hilt there that only shows up by torchlight. I let the dragon sleep and took the hilt to Ealaane Nimbuswalker. She went quiet for a while, then asked me to find the blade that belonged with it.\n\nThe blade wasn't anywhere you'd look on purpose, and I looked in a lot of places before I found it. Ealaane gave it its name, Eluvi'ana, the Night Dancer, and handed it back to me with the hilt. She watched the hilt until I put it away."] = "I came by an old ring on Zephras Isle. It's dented, and the inside of the band carries a line of Kaldorei script worn so thin I could barely read it. I put it on because it fit.\n\nThere's a dragon asleep in the ruins of Ban'aethal and a hilt there that only shows up by torchlight. I let the dragon sleep and took the hilt to Ealaane Nimbuswalker. She went quiet for a while, then asked me to find the blade that belonged with it.\n\nThe blade wasn't anywhere you'd look on purpose, and I looked in a lot of places before I found it. Ealaane gave it its name, Eluvi'ana, the Night Dancer, and handed it back to me with the hilt. She watched the hilt until I put it away."
L["Ancient Heirloom"] = "Ancient Heirloom"
L["Get the Ancient Heirloom. Rorian the Dayseeker gives one to the Skyborne once they come of age, and another lies on the top floor of a house close by."] = "Get the Ancient Heirloom. Rorian the Dayseeker gives one to the Skyborne once they come of age, and another lies on the top floor of a house close by."
L["Eluvi'ana"] = "Eluvi'ana"
L["Ealaane Nimbuswalker"] = "Ealaane Nimbuswalker"
L["The Befouled Water Globe"] = "The Befouled Water Globe"
L["The naga in Darkshore's Ruins of Mathystra each carry a piece of an old amulet. Put it together and take it to the water by the ruins, and something that has guarded them a long time will come up to meet you."] = "The naga in Darkshore's Ruins of Mathystra each carry a piece of an old amulet. Put it together and take it to the water by the ruins, and something that has guarded them a long time will come up to meet you."
L["Baron Aquanis, a water elemental in the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps, guards a globe of strange water. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring, at Zoram'gar Outpost, would very much like to see it."] = "Baron Aquanis, a water elemental in the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps, guards a globe of strange water. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring, at Zoram'gar Outpost, would very much like to see it."
L["The naga in the Ruins of Mathystra carry an old amulet around in pieces, a few to each naga. Twenty pieces later I had the whole thing, and at the water by the ruins it called up Baron Marinous. He came up angry and didn't last, and he left a clouded glass globe behind.\n\nI took the globe to Onu in the Grove of the Ancients. Onu held it a long while before giving it back, and by then the water inside had gone dark and foul. I've carried it around ever since."] = "The naga in the Ruins of Mathystra carry an old amulet around in pieces, a few to each naga. Twenty pieces later I had the whole thing, and at the water by the ruins it called up Baron Marinous. He came up angry and didn't last, and he left a clouded glass globe behind.\n\nI took the globe to Onu in the Grove of the Ancients. Onu held it a long while before giving it back, and by then the water inside had gone dark and foul. I've carried it around ever since."
L["Baron Aquanis keeps to the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps. He's a water elemental, so keeping to anything is a loose way to put it. He left a globe of strange water behind, and Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring wanted a look.\n\nJe'neu studied it for a long time. When I asked for the globe back, he gave it to me. The water inside had gone dark and foul, and I've carried it around ever since."] = "Baron Aquanis keeps to the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps. He's a water elemental, so keeping to anything is a loose way to put it. He left a globe of strange water behind, and Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring wanted a look.\n\nJe'neu studied it for a long time. When I asked for the globe back, he gave it to me. The water inside had gone dark and foul, and I've carried it around ever since."
