L["Befouled Water Globe"] = "Befouled Water Globe"
L["Onu"] = "Onu"
L["Speak with Onu again and ask for the globe back."] = "Speak with Onu again and ask for the globe back."
L["Speak with Je'neu Sancrea again and ask for the globe back."] = "Speak with Je'neu Sancrea again and ask for the globe back."
L["The Highborne Spirit"] = "The Highborne Spirit"
L["Wear the old ring on Zoram Strand, in Ashenvale, with the befouled globe in your pack, and you won't be alone on the beach for long."] = "Wear the old ring on Zoram Strand, in Ashenvale, with the befouled globe in your pack, and you won't be alone on the beach for long."
L["On Zoram Strand, with the ring on my finger and the globe in my pack, I met a Highborne spirit who had been waiting a very long time for someone carrying exactly that. He sent me up the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore.\n\nAthrikus Narassin keeps the top of that tower, and he kept the key to the strongbox behind him on his belt. Inside the box was his tome. I brought it back to the beach, and the spirit sent me on to Shen'dralas."] = "On Zoram Strand, with the ring on my finger and the globe in my pack, I met a Highborne spirit who had been waiting a very long time for someone carrying exactly that. He sent me up the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore.\n\nAthrikus Narassin keeps the top of that tower, and he kept the key to the strongbox behind him on his belt. Inside the box was his tome. I brought it back to the beach, and the spirit sent me on to Shen'dralas."
L["Narassin's Tome"] = "Narassin's Tome"
L["Highborne Spirit"] = "Highborne Spirit"
L["Wear the Ancient Heirloom and speak with the Highborne Spirit on Zoram Strand while carrying the Befouled Water Globe. Then take the Azsharan Key from Athrikus Narassin at the top of the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and open the strongbox behind him."] = "Wear the Ancient Heirloom and speak with the Highborne Spirit on Zoram Strand while carrying the Befouled Water Globe. Then take the Azsharan Key from Athrikus Narassin at the top of the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and open the strongbox behind him."
L["Synthesis"] = "Synthesis"
L["Mordent Evenshade, outside the temple in Shen'dralas, knows what Narassin's Tome is for. Bring him the tome with the hilt, the Night Dancer and the globe, and he'll tell you what it takes to make the water clean again. Some of it takes a group of five."] = "Mordent Evenshade, outside the temple in Shen'dralas, knows what Narassin's Tome is for. Bring him the tome with the hilt, the Night Dancer and the globe, and he'll tell you what it takes to make the water clean again. Some of it takes a group of five."
L["Mordent Evenshade read Narassin's tome and told me the globe needed a Star of Elune, an Abyssal Mote and the Tears of Anguish, none of them anywhere near Shen'dralas.\n\nThe star sat in a vault in the ogre temple in southern Feralas, a vault you only see with the ring on. Opening it took five of us, four pulling switches around the temple at once and one at the vault. The mote was in a chest at the bottom of the sea off Azshara. The tears came off the Highborne ghosts at Lake Kel'theril, and only some of them had any to give."] = "Mordent Evenshade read Narassin's tome and told me the globe needed a Star of Elune, an Abyssal Mote and the Tears of Anguish, none of them anywhere near Shen'dralas.\n\nThe star sat in a vault in the ogre temple in southern Feralas, a vault you only see with the ring on. Opening it took five of us, four pulling switches around the temple at once and one at the vault. The mote was in a chest at the bottom of the sea off Azshara. The tears came off the Highborne ghosts at Lake Kel'theril, and only some of them had any to give."
L["Star of Elune"] = "Star of Elune"
L["the ogre temple in southern Feralas"] = "the ogre temple in southern Feralas"
L["Wear the Ancient Heirloom and find the Shen'dralar Vault on the temple's ground floor. Four Ancient Switches around the temple must be pulled at the same moment to open it, so bring four friends."] = "Wear the Ancient Heirloom and find the Shen'dralar Vault on the temple's ground floor. Four Ancient Switches around the temple must be pulled at the same moment to open it, so bring four friends."
L["Abyssal Mote"] = "Abyssal Mote"
L["under the water off Azshara"] = "under the water off Azshara"
L["Finish the quests that begin with Kirith and end with Azsharite, then open the Abyssal Chest under the water in Azshara."] = "Finish the quests that begin with Kirith and end with Azsharite, then open the Abyssal Chest under the water in Azshara."
L["Tears of Anguish"] = "Tears of Anguish"
L["Lake Kel'theril, Winterspring"] = "Lake Kel'theril, Winterspring"
L["Once Mordent Evenshade has told you what the globe needs, take the Tears of Anguish from the Anguished Highborne and Suffering Highborne at Lake Kel'theril."] = "Once Mordent Evenshade has told you what the globe needs, take the Tears of Anguish from the Anguished Highborne and Suffering Highborne at Lake Kel'theril."
L["The Shrine of Coalescence"] = "The Shrine of Coalescence"
L["With the star, the mote and the tears in hand, Mordent sends you to Hyjal, to the Shrine of Coalescence."] = "With the star, the mote and the tears in hand, Mordent sends you to Hyjal, to the Shrine of Coalescence."
L["At the Shrine of Coalescence in Hyjal I laid out the star, the mote and the tears and used the globe, and the water inside it cleared.\n\nWith the water clear I could see what the globe was. It held the last of an elemental that once guarded a Highborne city, and I had met that elemental at the bottom of its own ruins and killed it. When I brought the globe back to Shen'dralas, Mordent didn't hold that against me."] = "At the Shrine of Coalescence in Hyjal I laid out the star, the mote and the tears and used the globe, and the water inside it cleared.\n\nWith the water clear I could see what the globe was. It held the last of an elemental that once guarded a Highborne city, and I had met that elemental at the bottom of its own ruins and killed it. When I brought the globe back to Shen'dralas, Mordent didn't hold that against me."
L["Cleansed Water Globe"] = "Cleansed Water Globe"
L["the Shrine of Coalescence, Mount Hyjal"] = "the Shrine of Coalescence, Mount Hyjal"
L["Take the Star of Elune, the Abyssal Mote and the Tears of Anguish to the Shrine of Coalescence in Hyjal, and use the Befouled Water Globe there."] = "Take the Star of Elune, the Abyssal Mote and the Tears of Anguish to the Shrine of Coalescence in Hyjal, and use the Befouled Water Globe there."
L["The Two Blades"] = "The Two Blades"
L["Mordent has heard the clean globe out, and sends you to the last prince of Eldre'Thalas in Dire Maul. Prince Tortheldrin remembers two blades. This is as far as anyone has followed the Dawn Waker so far."] = "Mordent has heard the clean globe out, and sends you to the last prince of Eldre'Thalas in Dire Maul. Prince Tortheldrin remembers two blades. This is as far as anyone has followed the Dawn Waker so far."
L["Mordent sent me to Dire Maul, to Prince Tortheldrin, who spoke of two blades, Eluvi'ana and Eluvi'tor, and of knowledge kept for those honored in his court. I had one of the blades on my belt already.\n\nLorekeeper Lydros made me an Arcanum of Binding out of a libram, a black diamond, two brilliant shards and an arcane crystal, and I bound the old hilt with it. When I went back, the prince gave me a scrawled note. It's a short riddle. Day has to wake where night dances, and something has to be cast in flames born of air.\n\nThat's where the trail stops for now, for me and for everyone else hunting it. I keep the hilt and the Night Dancer together, in case the answer turns up."] = "Mordent sent me to Dire Maul, to Prince Tortheldrin, who spoke of two blades, Eluvi'ana and Eluvi'tor, and of knowledge kept for those honored in his court. I had one of the blades on my belt already.\n\nLorekeeper Lydros made me an Arcanum of Binding out of a libram, a black diamond, two brilliant shards and an arcane crystal, and I bound the old hilt with it. When I went back, the prince gave me a scrawled note. It's a short riddle. Day has to wake where night dances, and something has to be cast in flames born of air.\n\nThat's where the trail stops for now, for me and for everyone else hunting it. I keep the hilt and the Night Dancer together, in case the answer turns up."
L["Libram of Binding"] = "Libram of Binding"
L["Dire Maul, Feralas"] = "Dire Maul, Feralas"
L["Scrawled Note"] = "Scrawled Note"
L["Prince Tortheldrin"] = "Prince Tortheldrin"
L["Use the Arcanum of Binding on the Ancient Hilt, then speak with Prince Tortheldrin again. The note's riddle is still unsolved."] = "Use the Arcanum of Binding on the Ancient Hilt, then speak with Prince Tortheldrin again. The note's riddle is still unsolved."
-- WoW Forever: Strahnbrad Mystery
L["Strahnbrad Mystery"] = "Strahnbrad Mystery"
L["Strahnbrad is a ruined town in the Alterac Mountains, and the Syndicate runs its business from there. The Syndicate is a gang of thieves led by Alterac's old nobility. Southshore wants them gone, and Tarren Mill has put a price on one of their barons.\n\nThe gang has a mystery of its own. The casters in Strahnbrad pass around a singed note about the old bellows at the town forge, which are said to come to life when no one is watching."] = "Strahnbrad is a ruined town in the Alterac Mountains, and the Syndicate runs its business from there. The Syndicate is a gang of thieves led by Alterac's old nobility. Southshore wants them gone, and Tarren Mill has put a price on one of their barons.\n\nThe gang has a mystery of its own. The casters in Strahnbrad pass around a singed note about the old bellows at the town forge, which are said to come to life when no one is watching."
L["Southshore's last magistrate was murdered, and the killers were never found. Magistrate Henry Maleb, the new one, is almost certain they were hired by the Syndicate, a gang of thieves led by the old nobles of fallen Alterac.\n\nThe Syndicate keeps a camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill and its headquarters in the ruins of Strahnbrad. Maleb would like to begin with the camp."] = "Southshore's last magistrate was murdered, and the killers were never found. Magistrate Henry Maleb, the new one, is almost certain they were hired by the Syndicate, a gang of thieves led by the old nobles of fallen Alterac.\n\nThe Syndicate keeps a camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill and its headquarters in the ruins of Strahnbrad. Maleb would like to begin with the camp."
L["A wanted poster in Tarren Mill names Baron Vardus, one of the old Alterac nobles who lead the Syndicate, a gang of thieves in the mountains to the north. High Executor Darthalia wants his head.\n\nThe Syndicate's headquarters is the ruined town of Strahnbrad. The casters there pass around a singed note about the old bellows at the town forge, which are said to come to life when no one is watching."] = "A wanted poster in Tarren Mill names Baron Vardus, one of the old Alterac nobles who lead the Syndicate, a gang of thieves in the mountains to the north. High Executor Darthalia wants his head.\n\nThe Syndicate's headquarters is the ruined town of Strahnbrad. The casters there pass around a singed note about the old bellows at the town forge, which are said to come to life when no one is watching."
L["Alterac Mountains / Hillsbrad Foothills"] = "Alterac Mountains / Hillsbrad Foothills"
L["Syndicate Assassins"] = "Syndicate Assassins"
L["Magistrate Henry Maleb"] = "Magistrate Henry Maleb"
L["the Syndicate camp at Sofera's Naze, Alterac Mountains"] = "the Syndicate camp at Sofera's Naze, Alterac Mountains"
L["the wanted poster in Tarren Mill, Hillsbrad Foothills"] = "the wanted poster in Tarren Mill, Hillsbrad Foothills"
L["Southshore's new magistrate, Henry Maleb, has the job because the last one was murdered. The killers were never found, but Maleb's clues point to a Syndicate camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill. Find him in the town hall."] = "Southshore's new magistrate, Henry Maleb, has the job because the last one was murdered. The killers were never found, but Maleb's clues point to a Syndicate camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill. Find him in the town hall."
L["Southshore's new magistrate has the job because the last one was murdered, and Henry Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate paid for it. His clues led to a Syndicate camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill, so I went up and started on their footpads and thieves.\n\nOn a table in the camp at Sofera's Naze lay a list of supplies, everything from food to masks and poison, wanted in a hurry for what it called an important mission against Southshore. Maleb found it very troubling and decided the Syndicate had declared war on his town.\n\nThe gang is run by Alterac's old nobles, who hide among the common members. You tell them apart by the signet ring, Maleb said. I brought seven back from the ruins of Strahnbrad, and the magistrate said the Syndicate was now just a gang of thugs. I'd thought of them that way from the start."] = "Southshore's new magistrate has the job because the last one was murdered, and Henry Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate paid for it. His clues led to a Syndicate camp in the mountains north of Tarren Mill, so I went up and started on their footpads and thieves.\n\nOn a table in the camp at Sofera's Naze lay a list of supplies, everything from food to masks and poison, wanted in a hurry for what it called an important mission against Southshore. Maleb found it very troubling and decided the Syndicate had declared war on his town.\n\nThe gang is run by Alterac's old nobles, who hide among the common members. You tell them apart by the signet ring, Maleb said. I brought seven back from the ruins of Strahnbrad, and the magistrate said the Syndicate was now just a gang of thugs. I'd thought of them that way from the start."
L["Foreboding Plans"] = "Foreboding Plans"
L["Syndicate Documents"] = "Syndicate Documents"
L["Noble Deaths"] = "Noble Deaths"
L["Baron Vardus"] = "Baron Vardus"
L["Shadowy Assassins still slip into Southshore now and then, and one of them carries a contract. Take it and bring it to Magistrate Maleb in the town hall, who will want to know whose name is on it."] = "Shadowy Assassins still slip into Southshore now and then, and one of them carries a contract. Take it and bring it to Magistrate Maleb in the town hall, who will want to know whose name is on it."
L["A wanted poster in Tarren Mill names Baron Vardus, one of the old Alterac nobles who lead the Syndicate up in the mountains. High Executor Darthalia will pay for his head."] = "A wanted poster in Tarren Mill names Baron Vardus, one of the old Alterac nobles who lead the Syndicate up in the mountains. High Executor Darthalia will pay for his head."
L["The Syndicate hadn't given up on Southshore. Their assassins still slipped into town now and then, and one I killed was carrying a contract, which seems careless for someone in that trade. I took it to Maleb.\n\nAfter reading it, the magistrate wanted the head of Baron Vardus, one of the nobles who lead the Syndicate. Vardus moves around the Alterac Mountains, so finding him took some walking, and getting the head off him took less time than that. I brought it back down to Southshore and handed it over."] = "The Syndicate hadn't given up on Southshore. Their assassins still slipped into town now and then, and one I killed was carrying a contract, which seems careless for someone in that trade. I took it to Maleb.\n\nAfter reading it, the magistrate wanted the head of Baron Vardus, one of the nobles who lead the Syndicate. Vardus moves around the Alterac Mountains, so finding him took some walking, and getting the head off him took less time than that. I brought it back down to Southshore and handed it over."
L["There's a wanted poster up in Tarren Mill for Baron Vardus. The Syndicate is a gang of thieves led by what's left of Alterac's nobility, and Vardus is one of those nobles. The poster still calls him Baron, which is more courtesy than most wanted men get.\n\nHigh Executor Darthalia wanted his head. Vardus moves around the Alterac Mountains, so finding him took some walking, and getting the head off him took less time than that. I carried it back down to Tarren Mill and collected the bounty from Darthalia."] = "There's a wanted poster up in Tarren Mill for Baron Vardus. The Syndicate is a gang of thieves led by what's left of Alterac's nobility, and Vardus is one of those nobles. The poster still calls him Baron, which is more courtesy than most wanted men get.\n\nHigh Executor Darthalia wanted his head. Vardus moves around the Alterac Mountains, so finding him took some walking, and getting the head off him took less time than that. I carried it back down to Tarren Mill and collected the bounty from Darthalia."
L["Assassin's Contract"] = "Assassin's Contract"
L["the Shadowy Assassins, Southshore, Hillsbrad Foothills"] = "the Shadowy Assassins, Southshore, Hillsbrad Foothills"
L["Baron's Demise"] = "Baron's Demise"
L["WANTED: Baron Vardus"] = "WANTED: Baron Vardus"
L["The Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad carry a singed note. Rumor has it the old bellows at the town forge come to life when no one is watching. The note is scorched as if by fire magic, and the forge might want a taste of the same."] = "The Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad carry a singed note. Rumor has it the old bellows at the town forge come to life when no one is watching. The note is scorched as if by fire magic, and the forge might want a taste of the same."
L["One of the Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad had a singed note on them. According to the note, the old bellows at the town forge had a mind of their own and came to life when no one was watching. Whoever wrote it wanted the matter cleared up before coming back, ghost story or not.\n\nSo I went and watched the bellows. They did nothing, which to be fair is what the rumor said they'd do. Then I gave each of them some fire. A flare went up over my head both times, and after the second an ancient fire elemental came out of the top of the forge and landed between them.\n\nIt was made of fire and didn't mind more of it, so I put it out the hard way. Afterward I took my findings down to Kundric Zanden, the town historian in Southshore."] = "One of the Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad had a singed note on them. According to the note, the old bellows at the town forge had a mind of their own and came to life when no one was watching. Whoever wrote it wanted the matter cleared up before coming back, ghost story or not.\n\nSo I went and watched the bellows. They did nothing, which to be fair is what the rumor said they'd do. Then I gave each of them some fire. A flare went up over my head both times, and after the second an ancient fire elemental came out of the top of the forge and landed between them.\n\nIt was made of fire and didn't mind more of it, so I put it out the hard way. Afterward I took my findings down to Kundric Zanden, the town historian in Southshore."
L["One of the Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad had a singed note on them. According to the note, the old bellows at the town forge had a mind of their own and came to life when no one was watching. Whoever wrote it wanted the matter cleared up before coming back, ghost story or not.\n\nSo I went and watched the bellows. They did nothing, which to be fair is what the rumor said they'd do. Then I gave each of them some fire. A flare went up over my head both times, and after the second an ancient fire elemental came out of the top of the forge and landed between them.\n\nIt was made of fire and didn't mind more of it, so I put it out the hard way. Afterward I took my findings down to Shara Blazen in Tarren Mill."] = "One of the Syndicate's casters in Strahnbrad had a singed note on them. According to the note, the old bellows at the town forge had a mind of their own and came to life when no one was watching. Whoever wrote it wanted the matter cleared up before coming back, ghost story or not.\n\nSo I went and watched the bellows. They did nothing, which to be fair is what the rumor said they'd do. Then I gave each of them some fire. A flare went up over my head both times, and after the second an ancient fire elemental came out of the top of the forge and landed between them.\n\nIt was made of fire and didn't mind more of it, so I put it out the hard way. Afterward I took my findings down to Shara Blazen in Tarren Mill."
L["the Syndicate Wizards and Argus Shadow Mages, Strahnbrad, Alterac Mountains"] = "the Syndicate Wizards and Argus Shadow Mages, Strahnbrad, Alterac Mountains"
