L["Master Gadrin turned the spider god's true name into a spell of summoning and sent me to read it at the altar of Shadra'Alor, deep in Witherbark country. I read it, and Shadra came. The Witherbark get their strongest venom from her. Now so did I.\n\nApothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill was delighted. One drop had killed nearly two dozen rabbits, he told me, though he admitted some of them had been very small. He wanted a sample sent to his superior in the Undercity, so I carried it there, and the Royal Apothecary Society called my service undeniable. Nobody asked the rabbits."] = "Master Gadrin turned the spider god's true name into a spell of summoning and sent me to read it at the altar of Shadra'Alor, deep in Witherbark country. I read it, and Shadra came. The Witherbark get their strongest venom from her. Now so did I.\n\nApothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill was delighted. One drop had killed nearly two dozen rabbits, he told me, though he admitted some of them had been very small. He wanted a sample sent to his superior in the Undercity, so I carried it there, and the Royal Apothecary Society called my service undeniable. Nobody asked the rabbits."
L["The Divination"] = "The Divination"
L["Return to the Hinterlands"] = "Return to the Hinterlands"
L["Saving Sharpbeak"] = "Saving Sharpbeak"
L["Grimshade kept his end of the bargain. He asked for room to work and warned me that if the ritual went wrong, I'd better close my eyes. It didn't. Sharpbeak was in a cage at the top of Jintha'Alor, and the high priestess of the Vilebranch trolls had the key.\n\nGryphon Master Talonaxe took the news about as calmly as a dwarf can, which is to say not at all. So up I went, all the way to the top of Jintha'Alor, took the key off the priestess, and opened the cage.\n\nSharpbeak's parents flew home with him and fussed over him like new parents, and Talonaxe admitted to a little mist in the eyes. The gryphons of Aerie Peak will sing my name, he says, for a long, long time."] = "Grimshade kept his end of the bargain. He asked for room to work and warned me that if the ritual went wrong, I'd better close my eyes. It didn't. Sharpbeak was in a cage at the top of Jintha'Alor, and the high priestess of the Vilebranch trolls had the key.\n\nGryphon Master Talonaxe took the news about as calmly as a dwarf can, which is to say not at all. So up I went, all the way to the top of Jintha'Alor, took the key off the priestess, and opened the cage.\n\nSharpbeak's parents flew home with him and fussed over him like new parents, and Talonaxe admitted to a little mist in the eyes. The gryphons of Aerie Peak will sing my name, he says, for a long, long time."
L["Angelas Moonbreeze"] = "Angelas Moonbreeze"
