L["The discs from Uldaman had a sequel. Their glyphs mentioned Uldum, a place in the Tanaris desert most people call a myth, and the scholars back home wanted me to carry the discs to its sealed gates and see what happened. Nobody could say what would. They seemed to think that was the exciting part.\n\nAt the gates I touched a pedestal, the discs hummed in my pack, and another stone watcher sprang up, every bit as polite as the first. It was a guardian of entry, it said, and my discs were missing the Plates of Uldum.\n\nNobody knows where the plates are. The scholars put the whole thing on hold and paid me an honorarium. Uldum beckons, they told me. It'll have to keep beckoning."] = "The discs from Uldaman had a sequel. Their glyphs mentioned Uldum, a place in the Tanaris desert most people call a myth, and the scholars back home wanted me to carry the discs to its sealed gates and see what happened. Nobody could say what would. They seemed to think that was the exciting part.\n\nAt the gates I touched a pedestal, the discs hummed in my pack, and another stone watcher sprang up, every bit as polite as the first. It was a guardian of entry, it said, and my discs were missing the Plates of Uldum.\n\nNobody knows where the plates are. The scholars put the whole thing on hold and paid me an honorarium. Uldum beckons, they told me. It'll have to keep beckoning."
