L["Tinkee Steamboil at Flame Crest had invented the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900 and wanted eight broodling essences caught with it from the black broodlings of the Burning Steppes. I caught them. Then Tinkee had a letter for Felnok Steelspring in Everlook, Felnok wanted eight uncracked chillwind horns, and what came of it was a package that had to go all the way back to Flame Crest. Gnomes invent things. Couriers walk them around."] = "Tinkee Steamboil at Flame Crest had invented the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900 and wanted eight broodling essences caught with it from the black broodlings of the Burning Steppes. I caught them. Then Tinkee had a letter for Felnok Steelspring in Everlook, Felnok wanted eight uncracked chillwind horns, and what came of it was a package that had to go all the way back to Flame Crest. Gnomes invent things. Couriers walk them around."
L["Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold had found pieces of a tablet left by the Twilight's Hammer and wanted the rest. I brought eight fragments, and the restored tablet went to Hermit Ortell, who once ran with the cult and now lives alone out in the desert. Ortell wanted the three chapters of the Twilight Lexicon to read the rest of it. The cultists carrying them did not hand them over politely."] = "Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold had found pieces of a tablet left by the Twilight's Hammer and wanted the rest. I brought eight fragments, and the restored tablet went to Hermit Ortell, who once ran with the cult and now lives alone out in the desert. Ortell wanted the three chapters of the Twilight Lexicon to read the rest of it. The cultists carrying them did not hand them over politely."
L["Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles tests people before trusting them. Faith meant stepping off a plank high over the canyon. Endurance meant Grenka's claw, strength meant the fragments of Rok'Alim, and lore meant a trip to Braug Dimspirit in the Stonetalon Mountains, who sent me after the Legacy of the Aspects and then asked me a question about it. I answered right. Braug sent me on to Parqual Fintallas in the Undercity, who had one more test waiting."] = "Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles tests people before trusting them. Faith meant stepping off a plank high over the canyon. Endurance meant Grenka's claw, strength meant the fragments of Rok'Alim, and lore meant a trip to Braug Dimspirit in the Stonetalon Mountains, who sent me after the Legacy of the Aspects and then asked me a question about it. I answered right. Braug sent me on to Parqual Fintallas in the Undercity, who had one more test waiting."
L["Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity needed a pile of kraul guano from Razorfen Kraul. I didn't ask what for. I brought it, Faranell was thrilled, and there was more work after that."] = "Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity needed a pile of kraul guano from Razorfen Kraul. I didn't ask what for. I brought it, Faranell was thrilled, and there was more work after that."
L["Caretaker Alen at Light's Hope Chapel told me the dead of Stratholme can't rest, and that a man named Egan was trying to do something about it. All anyone knew was that Egan had last been seen around Stratholme, so that's where I looked."] = "Caretaker Alen at Light's Hope Chapel told me the dead of Stratholme can't rest, and that a man named Egan was trying to do something about it. All anyone knew was that Egan had last been seen around Stratholme, so that's where I looked."
L["Nathanos Blightcaller doesn't hand out favors. First I had to go to the Quel'Lithien lodge in the north of the Eastern Plaguelands for the Quel'Thalas Registry, and thin out the rangers, pathstriders and woodsmen camped there. Then Nathanos wanted Duskwing, a bat that hunts north of Marris Stead, or at least a patch of its fur. After that, apparently, we could talk."] = "Nathanos Blightcaller doesn't hand out favors. First I had to go to the Quel'Lithien lodge in the north of the Eastern Plaguelands for the Quel'Thalas Registry, and thin out the rangers, pathstriders and woodsmen camped there. Then Nathanos wanted Duskwing, a bat that hunts north of Marris Stead, or at least a patch of its fur. After that, apparently, we could talk."
L["Marvon Rivetseeker had left something called the Stone Circle in a workshop in Ratchet and wanted it fetched. I fetched it, and Marvon had plans for it."] = "Marvon Rivetseeker had left something called the Stone Circle in a workshop in Ratchet and wanted it fetched. I fetched it, and Marvon had plans for it."
L["Brohann Caskbelly of the Explorers' League in Stormwind wanted the Temple of Atal'Hakkar found, and the trail started in the Hinterlands. High Thane Falstad Wildhammer at Aerie Peak sent me to Gryphon Master Talonaxe, who sent me to Rhapsody Shindigger, who knew a tale about the temple and would tell it for a cocktail of roc gizzards, groddoc livers and ironfur livers. I brought the ingredients, heard the tale, and carried a fragment of an Atal'ai tablet back to Brohann."] = "Brohann Caskbelly of the Explorers' League in Stormwind wanted the Temple of Atal'Hakkar found, and the trail started in the Hinterlands. High Thane Falstad Wildhammer at Aerie Peak sent me to Gryphon Master Talonaxe, who sent me to Rhapsody Shindigger, who knew a tale about the temple and would tell it for a cocktail of roc gizzards, groddoc livers and ironfur livers. I brought the ingredients, heard the tale, and carried a fragment of an Atal'ai tablet back to Brohann."
L["Fel'zerul in Stonard wanted to know more about the trolls at the Pool of Tears, and sent me to collect ten of their Atal'ai artifacts. Fel'zerul couldn't make sense of them and sent me with the bundle to an Atal'ai exile hiding in the Hinterlands, who could. Then I took what the exile had to say back to Stonard."] = "Fel'zerul in Stonard wanted to know more about the trolls at the Pool of Tears, and sent me to collect ten of their Atal'ai artifacts. Fel'zerul couldn't make sense of them and sent me with the bundle to an Atal'ai exile hiding in the Hinterlands, who could. Then I took what the exile had to say back to Stonard."
L["Before anyone at Chillwind Camp would talk to me about Scholomance, Commander Ashlam Valorfist wanted Sorrow Hill cleared of skeletal flayers and slavering ghouls, and then the four watchtowers of Andorhal marked with a beacon torch, standing in each doorway in turn. Only then did the commander mention the school."] = "Before anyone at Chillwind Camp would talk to me about Scholomance, Commander Ashlam Valorfist wanted Sorrow Hill cleared of skeletal flayers and slavering ghouls, and then the four watchtowers of Andorhal marked with a beacon torch, standing in each doorway in turn. Only then did the commander mention the school."
L["Before High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark would talk to me about Scholomance, the Scarlet Crusade's camp between Felstone Field and Dalson's Tears had to lose its command tent and gain a Scourge banner, and the four watchtowers of Andorhal had to be marked with a beacon torch, from each doorway in turn. Only then did the executor mention the school."] = "Before High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark would talk to me about Scholomance, the Scarlet Crusade's camp between Felstone Field and Dalson's Tears had to lose its command tent and gain a Scourge banner, and the four watchtowers of Andorhal had to be marked with a beacon torch, from each doorway in turn. Only then did the executor mention the school."
L["Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge sent me to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan, who was worried about a prospector called Agmond, missing out in the Badlands. I found him. He was dead, killed by a trogg called Murdaloc, so I dealt with Murdaloc and twelve of his Stonevault bonesnappers and reported back to Ironband."] = "Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge sent me to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan, who was worried about a prospector called Agmond, missing out in the Badlands. I found him. He was dead, killed by a trogg called Murdaloc, so I dealt with Murdaloc and twelve of his Stonevault bonesnappers and reported back to Ironband."
L["In Searing Gorge, Velarok Windblade told me a story about the black dragonflight and asked for help paying them back. Paying them back took four hearts of flame, four globes of golem oil, eight thorium-plated daggers and a Symbol of Ragnaros, all for the Torch of Retribution. Squire Maltrake then had me carry it into the four sentry towers and set each one ablaze, and the chest that opened afterwards held a black dragonflight molt. Cyrus Therepentous in the Burning Steppes wanted to see it."] = "In Searing Gorge, Velarok Windblade told me a story about the black dragonflight and asked for help paying them back. Paying them back took four hearts of flame, four globes of golem oil, eight thorium-plated daggers and a Symbol of Ragnaros, all for the Torch of Retribution. Squire Maltrake then had me carry it into the four sentry towers and set each one ablaze, and the chest that opened afterwards held a black dragonflight molt. Cyrus Therepentous in the Burning Steppes wanted to see it."
L["Thunderheart in Kargath sent me into Blackrock Mountain first, to the quarry, where Overmaster Pyron kept watch over the way into the depths. Pyron fell, and the way in was open."] = "Thunderheart in Kargath sent me into Blackrock Mountain first, to the quarry, where Overmaster Pyron kept watch over the way into the depths. Pyron fell, and the way in was open."
L["Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania in Kargath wanted ten fractured elemental shards from the golems and elementals of the Burning Steppes. I brought them, and Theodora sent a sample with me to Lotwil Veriatus, camped to the east of Kargath."] = "Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania in Kargath wanted ten fractured elemental shards from the golems and elementals of the Burning Steppes. I brought them, and Theodora sent a sample with me to Lotwil Veriatus, camped to the east of Kargath."
L["Before he told me anything, the old man in the cottage wanted his corner of the Eastern Plaguelands cleaned up: fifteen slabs of meat from the carrion grubs and devourers, thirty plaguebats out of the sky, and a pack of plaguehounds, runts and all. Then he talked."] = "Before he told me anything, the old man in the cottage wanted his corner of the Eastern Plaguelands cleaned up: fifteen slabs of meat from the carrion grubs and devourers, thirty plaguebats out of the sky, and a pack of plaguehounds, runts and all. Then he talked."
-- END CONTENT STRINGS
